91ec77f0b291936faee2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/95152591bf0635e678491ec77f0b291936faee2d"}],"sha":"3b181fa6ad698143a2aab701e8e6632af82ec6a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/3b181fa6ad698143a2aab701e8e6632af82ec6a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/95152591bf0635e678491ec77f0b291936faee2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:41:43Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:41:43Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"chore: stop scheduled version updates, keeping Dependabot for security only\n\nKilian believed every Dependabot PR was a security alert. They were not: this\nconfig scheduled weekly VERSION updates across three ecosystems, and that is\nwhere #137, #138 and #144 came from. #144 carried no advisory and broke the\nweb build. Alerts and security PRs are a repo-level setting, already enabled\nand untouched by this change, so advisories still arrive automatically.\n\nThere is no version-updates opt-out short of removing the config, so the file\ngoes. It is read from the default branch only, so this takes effect when `dev`\nis next promoted.\n\nDeleting it would have left two lines in `CLAUDE.md` false:\n\n- one cited the config as a path, which the path arm of\n  `test_claude_md_claims.py` would have caught. Its subject — a class of file\n  read only from `main` — is still true, and `workflow_dispatch` registration\n  is another member, so the line keeps the doctrine and drops the example.\n- \"SOME pinned action SHAs Dependabot can never bump\" implied the rest were\n  handled. Nothing is now bumped on a schedule, and only an advisory can move\n  an action pin, so the line says every pin is checked by hand.\n\nThe config''s two `ignore` rules were holds, and a prohibition may not be\ndeleted with the file that carried it. The `typescript` hold is already stated\nat `CLAUDE.md:64` and needed nothing. The `@types/node` hold had no home in\nthe tree — only PR #6''s commit body and an archived reason — so it becomes\n`tests/test_node_types_pin.py`, which asserts the `@types/node` major equals\nthe `.nvmrc` runtime major. A guard rather than a tripwire line, because the\nclaim is executable: staleness is the correct state here, nothing else in the\nrepo objects to a newer major, and a hold nothing enforces is one the next\nreader \"fixes\". Shown to fail at `^26.0.0`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"99c69fe35cf62abf7f1e09474dfb66256acb18ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/99c69fe35cf62abf7f1e09474dfb66256acb18ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/95152591bf0635e678491ec77f0b291936faee2d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":