t/trees/ba4008df8029991d22f896967c8f1756dd22a2ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/43d286b2d39860686a69ea8f4e569435be7e742e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/43d286b2d39860686a69ea8f4e569435be7e742e","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDQzZDI4NmIyZDM5ODYwNjg2YTY5ZWE4ZjRlNTY5NDM1YmU3ZTc0MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/eb4c6d1454e0c7a7bd19314539b8b6b7175ac092","sha":"eb4c6d1454e0c7a7bd19314539b8b6b7175ac092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/eb4c6d1454e0c7a7bd19314539b8b6b7175ac092"}],"sha":"43d286b2d39860686a69ea8f4e569435be7e742e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/43d286b2d39860686a69ea8f4e569435be7e742e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/eb4c6d1454e0c7a7bd19314539b8b6b7175ac092/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:55:27Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:55:27Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"chore(deps): v9.4.0 — supersede dependabot #137/#138 at latest stable\n\nTakes all ten packages from the two open dependabot PRs, pinned to the latest\nstable verified against the registry rather than to what those PRs proposed.\nThree land above the proposal: typescript-eslint 8.70.0, @module-federation/vite\n1.21.5, @types/react-dom 19.3.0.\n\npython:  alembic 1.19.2, psycopg[binary] 3.3.5, ruff 0.16.6\nweb:     vitest 5.0.0, eslint 10.10.0, globals 17.12.0, sass 1.104.0\n\n@types/node and typescript keep their held-back majors per dependabot.yml.\n\nvitest 4 -> 5 needed no config or test changes. Verified it is not a vacuous\npass: running vitest 5 against the pre-upgrade dist/ still reports 1502, so the\nrunner contributes zero tests. The web count moves 1502 -> 1505 because\n@module-federation/vite 1.21.5 emits three further chunks reachable from\nremoteEntry.js, and distContract.test.ts derives one case per reachable\nartifact. Server 1430 passed, web 1505 passed across 62 files, no skips.\n\nFour fixes to prose and config that no CI job checks:\n\n- vitest.config.ts told readers to avoid environmentOptions.jsdom.userAgent and\n  use jsdom''s `resources: { userAgent }`, because jsdom >=28 dropped the\n  ResourceLoader export vitest imported. Vitest 5 fixes exactly that, so the\n  prohibition is void and is deleted. Confirmed at both ends: v4.1.11 has the\n  unguarded `new ResourceLoader(...)`, v5.0.0 adds getResourceOptions() with a\n  fallback.\n- distContract.test.ts carried three stale \"measured today\" numbers: 43 -> 51\n  precache entries, 22 -> 21 boot hrefs (its stated breakdown did not sum to its\n  own total), and a byte figure now cited as the KiB workbox actually reports.\n- Naming `exclude` REPLACES vitest''s defaults rather than extending them, so\n  **/.git/** had been silently dropped. Restored, with the reason stated.\n- engines.node was `>=24.15.0`, which admits Node 25 — a version vitest 5\n  refuses outright. Narrowed to `^24.15.0 || >=26.0.0`.\n\nDoes not close the adm-zip advisory: it has no patched version, and\n@module-federation/vite 1.21.5 still pulls adm-zip@0.6.0 via dts-plugin@2.9.0.\nvite.config.ts sets `dts: false`, so that codepath does not load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8aa2db03a9c4b3e70c3e26f33a8e5986689bd494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/8aa2db03a9c4b3e70c3e26f33a8e5986689bd494"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/eb4c6d1454e0c7a7bd19314539b8b6b7175ac092","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/eb4c6d1454e0c7a7bd19314539b8b6b7175ac092","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKGViNGM2ZDE0NTRlMGM3YTdiZDE5MzE0NTM5YjhiNmI3MTc1YWMwOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/b7da0793944666a3300951f5d2ca04cded57aef3","sha":"b7da0793944666a3300951f5d2ca04cded57aef3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/b7da0793944666a3300951f5d2ca04cded57aef3"}],"sha":"eb4c6d1454e0c7a7bd19314539b8b6b7175ac092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/eb4c6d1454e0c7a7bd19314539b8b6b7175ac092"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/b7da0793944666a3300951f5d2ca04cded57aef3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:41:16Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:41:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(docs): delete the findings inbox, audit every tripwire, and drop stale allowlist headroom (#142)\n\nThe `## Findings inbox` section is gone (Kilian). It staged a finding until the next\npromotion to `main`, which ties triage to an event weeks away while nothing re-checks a\nstaged line — so it accumulates claims that have stopped being true. One of the five lines\nit held described a gap that the very PR which surfaced it had already closed: #141 stripped\n1,657 comment lines from the stylesheets *and* shipped the `.scss` budget guard in the same\ncommit. The rule is now one line in the header: a finding is triaged the moment it is found.\n\nThe five staged findings, each routed:\n- the `/api/sessions/completion` off-by-one at the row cap -> filed as a register issue\n- the blanked-dev-server recovery -> folded into the existing tripwire as a clause\n- `.scss` outside the prose budget -> DELETED, already guarded by #141\n- `JournalResponse.trends` having no reader -> added to the unused-columns sweep\n- the web suite''s `settle()` race -> filed as a register issue\n\nTripwires audited, 104 -> 103 bullets. One deletion: the gitleaks bullet, whose digest\nclause duplicated the stronger `openapi-sha256` phrasing and whose `useDefault` clause is\nasserted by `tests/test_gitleaks_config.py`. Three further clauses trimmed because a test\nalready enforces them, and in each case the test was rewritten to own the rule rather than\ncite the prose being deleted — `pwaContract.test.ts` opened \"Four PWA properties CLAUDE.md\nrecords\", which the trim would have made false, so its four reasons moved into the `it()`\nnames and `ABSENT_PATHS` now carries its own.\n\nFour false claims repaired in lines that stayed. `set_index` was described as the whole\nlogged session''s ordinal, which is true of `logged_set` and NOT of `prescribed_set`, where\nit is block-scoped by `UniqueConstraint(\"session_block_id\", \"set_index\")`. A diagnostics\nheader allowlist was asserted in the present tense and does not exist. `_sizes.scss` was\ncited for arithmetic that c95e03a stripped. One archive pointer did not grep-resolve.\n\nThe allowlist had no deletable row, and that is provable rather than a judgement: the arm at\n`test_comment_budget.py:511` fails on any entry covering a comment now within its cap, and\nit is green, so all rows are load-bearing. What was stale is the `limit` field, which no arm\nchecks — 41 rows carried headroom above their measured span, licensing silent regrowth\n(three `useSessionRun.ts` blocks of 3, 5 and 9 lines were all pinned at 26). Lowered to\nspan. One further row was orphaned by the PWA trim and deleted, so 1,279 -> 1,278 entries.\nBASELINE stays 972 and `BASELINE_RATCHET` needs no move: no backlog row was removed.\n\n`npm run check` green: 1430 server, 1502 web across 62 files.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"74d304ed91bd986430d6ce3615ef90f36ce3b179","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/74d304ed91bd986430d6ce3615ef90f36ce3b179"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/b7da0793944666a3300951f5d2ca04cded57aef3","verification":{"payload":"tree 74d304ed91bd986430d6ce3615ef90f36ce3b179\nparent c95e03a0211e38616abb8f72234addb46f95462f\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788972076 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788972076 +0200\n\nchore(docs): delete the findings inbox, audit every tripwire, and drop stale allowlist headroom (#142)\n\nThe `## Findings inbox` section is gone (Kilian). It staged a finding until the next\npromotion to `main`, which ties triage to an event weeks away while nothing re-checks a\nstaged line — so it accumulates claims that have stopped being true. One of the five lines\nit held described a gap that the very PR which surfaced it had already closed: #141 stripped\n1,657 comment lines from the stylesheets *and* shipped the `.scss` budget guard in the same\ncommit. The rule is now one line in the header: a finding is triaged the moment it is found.\n\nThe five staged findings, each routed:\n- the `/api/sessions/completion` off-by-one at the row cap -> filed as a register issue\n- the blanked-dev-server recovery -> folded into the existing tripwire as a clause\n- `.scss` outside the prose budget -> DELETED, already guarded by #141\n- `JournalResponse.trends` having no reader -> added to the unused-columns sweep\n- the web suite''s `settle()` race -> filed as a register issue\n\nTripwires audited, 104 -> 103 bullets. One deletion: the gitleaks bullet, whose digest\nclause duplicated the stronger `openapi-sha256` phrasing and whose `useDefault` clause is\nasserted by `tests/test_gitleaks_config.py`. Three further clauses trimmed because a test\nalready enforces them, and in each case the test was rewritten to own the rule rather than\ncite the prose being deleted — `pwaContract.test.ts` opened \"Four PWA properties CLAUDE.md\nrecords\", which the trim would have made false, so its four reasons moved into the `it()`\nnames and `ABSENT_PATHS` now carries its own.\n\nFour false claims repaired in lines that stayed. `set_index` was described as the whole\nlogged session''s ordinal, which is true of `logged_set` and NOT of `prescribed_set`, where\nit is block-scoped by `UniqueConstraint(\"session_block_id\", \"set_index\")`. A diagnostics\nheader allowlist was asserted in the present tense and does not exist. `_sizes.scss` was\ncited for arithmetic that c95e03a stripped. One archive pointer did not grep-resolve.\n\nThe allowlist had no deletable row, and that is provable rather than a judgement: the arm at\n`test_comment_budget.py:511` fails on any entry covering a comment now within its cap, and\nit is green, so all rows are load-bearing. What was stale is the `limit` field, which no arm\nchecks — 41 rows carried headroom above their measured span, licensing silent regrowth\n(three `useSessionRun.ts` blocks of 3, 5 and 9 lines were all pinned at 26). Lowered to\nspan. One further row was orphaned by the PWA trim and deleted, so 1,279 -> 1,278 entries.\nBASELINE stays 972 and `BASELINE_RATCHET` needs no move: no backlog row was removed.\n\n`npm run check` green: 1430 server, 1502 web across 62 files.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoYwsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiGUQAKe6Dyf1cszOwOWY2msLigot\nkOgaolo+zgLjhR9MKfKHXfLxVJBEqmfZRu0Vvk9WJBacQyC7dcpgpwhxi1Z2WRDt\nSkICCfv35KS8k6oBTQFmm5Idb+jijzngojfnBkmH3DK5r9SCtX/MMlAolTJYAt/e\nMQv8Asu9SADwOL+U6vfrgQ2JmSYw2no40dZXtl2LZpBpUFqWwmZ8160xcQ7BjW7C\nHGn1XjAoM0xR3kbDsQ8rEH0W9PnOAGf7HJysLNqL9RBVj5ADNuwG9qrHNcSEZi9C\nIKA+vLq7yVZ8/t3dQaIkr02tQoAf4056AA7jPzrJjK2lQP/PfbSmqRefFgw369+G\nLekFUwLOPgKFqquoxqw90QF2v6hSUn2A5FTvqdoqmtF3aGfizyes24f2KFkzyXTM\ngof0bzDYS9G2z6bo22UOvD6Om67xpYlIA39G3CcRD57s9Hvh7H3TwgRkS8lCQMGd\niKvSt8+jPxI60GBvF3otMQWCuN/NSqa2x5/FRth65hlmHkaeklmqokj+351T7aJu\nw0/T692u+5Djs+eLeKHRrTG0CZkG8yT6rshUlFfkPzD8O3etigT8xi+GRtmbCfAH\nQjWfdxfDDwPKKDSFOe+mZByy1RjUZ+Ttuy25VwMGSyAXiwwvJELYlSEA8Kdvy21l\nkNr2XqizqcFPQ1hYO7ym\n=ysQX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T16:41:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/b7da0793944666a3300951f5d2ca04cded57aef3","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKGI3ZGEwNzkzOTQ0NjY2YTMzMDA5NTFmNWQyY2EwNGNkZWQ1N2FlZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/c95e03a0211e38616abb8f72234addb46f95462f","sha":"c95e03a0211e38616abb8f72234addb46f95462f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/c95e03a0211e38616abb8f72234addb46f95462f"}],"sha":"b7da0793944666a3300951f5d2ca04cded57aef3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/b7da0793944666a3300951f5d2ca04cded57aef3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/c95e03a0211e38616abb8f72234addb46f95462f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:21:46Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:21:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(diary): read entries back as a per-plan chart, and strip stylesheet prose (#141)\n\nCompletes #16b. The write half shipped in #140; this is the reading half.\n\nThe diary is now one section per plan, each the same shape: the plan''s name\n(renameable), then a card holding its chart, those readings as a table, and its\nown entries. feel/sleep/skin are RAW readings over one span told apart by stroke\nstyle, never colour alone. Entries open in a sheet and edit in place, reusing\neach entry''s own client_uuid so an edit can never mint a second row for one\nsession — which is why this no longer waits on #80.\n\nThe smoothed weight trend was cut rather than built (Kilian), so the Body weight\nsection is absent and the weigh-in is a column of the readings table.\nJournalResponse.trends is left on the wire with no consumer, recorded in the\nfindings inbox rather than removed here.\n\nServer: GET /api/journal in two flavours, scoped to a plan and unscoped, each its\nown cache entry so opening the whole history and going back costs no read. The\nread fetches cap + 1 to tell a real truncation from a count that merely lands on\nthe cap. PUT /api/plans/{id}/name renames a plan, refused for a demo principal.\n\nFixes found while building:\n- the scope switch changed the query key, so the gate met the empty key with its\n  loading page, the document collapsed and the browser clamped the reader to the\n  top. keepPreviousData holds the previous scope until the new read lands, with a\n  test that holds the read open to observe the in-flight moment.\n- .ct-app__chartbox rendered 300x123.75 inside a 1312px card at every screen\n  size. Cross-axis auto margins suppress the flex stretch, so the wrapper\n  shrink-wrapped to the svg''s 300x150 default. It now carries inline-size: 100%,\n  and its size steps 320x132 / 606x250 / 904x373 at the named screen sizes.\n\nStylesheets now carry NO comments at all (Kilian): 1,530 comment lines removed\nfrom the 15 already-committed stylesheets, with _diary.scss arriving new and\nalready free of them — 1,659 lines over 16 files as the sweep actually ran. The compiled CSS is byte-identical — both asset hashes match the\npre-sweep build — so this removed prose and nothing else. .scss is brought under\ntests/test_comment_budget.py at a cap of zero, with a third detector for a\ntrailing comment after code and no allowlist exemption, since a length argument\ncollapses at zero. The rules that prose carried and nothing else stated are now\ntripwire lines in CLAUDE.md; the reasons are gone deliberately.\n\nCLAUDE.md''s landing-page tripwire was stale and is corrected: text over a\nphotograph is legal behind the --ct-scrim overlay, which the code has shipped\nsince it was restored, and the lightest stop under copy is the contrast floor.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"516d593aa1a511c0dfc9b4b10ef75df92c5098af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/516d593aa1a511c0dfc9b4b10ef75df92c5098af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/c95e03a0211e38616abb8f72234addb46f95462f","verification":{"payload":"tree 516d593aa1a511c0dfc9b4b10ef75df92c5098af\nparent 1c7067857d13bfd9aa9fafe4aa1d18608acf3b58\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788967306 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788967306 +0200\n\nfeat(diary): read entries back as a per-plan chart, and strip stylesheet prose (#141)\n\nCompletes #16b. The write half shipped in #140; this is the reading half.\n\nThe diary is now one section per plan, each the same shape: the plan''s name\n(renameable), then a card holding its chart, those readings as a table, and its\nown entries. feel/sleep/skin are RAW readings over one span told apart by stroke\nstyle, never colour alone. Entries open in a sheet and edit in place, reusing\neach entry''s own client_uuid so an edit can never mint a second row for one\nsession — which is why this no longer waits on #80.\n\nThe smoothed weight trend was cut rather than built (Kilian), so the Body weight\nsection is absent and the weigh-in is a column of the readings table.\nJournalResponse.trends is left on the wire with no consumer, recorded in the\nfindings inbox rather than removed here.\n\nServer: GET /api/journal in two flavours, scoped to a plan and unscoped, each its\nown cache entry so opening the whole history and going back costs no read. The\nread fetches cap + 1 to tell a real truncation from a count that merely lands on\nthe cap. PUT /api/plans/{id}/name renames a plan, refused for a demo principal.\n\nFixes found while building:\n- the scope switch changed the query key, so the gate met the empty key with its\n  loading page, the document collapsed and the browser clamped the reader to the\n  top. keepPreviousData holds the previous scope until the new read lands, with a\n  test that holds the read open to observe the in-flight moment.\n- .ct-app__chartbox rendered 300x123.75 inside a 1312px card at every screen\n  size. Cross-axis auto margins suppress the flex stretch, so the wrapper\n  shrink-wrapped to the svg''s 300x150 default. It now carries inline-size: 100%,\n  and its size steps 320x132 / 606x250 / 904x373 at the named screen sizes.\n\nStylesheets now carry NO comments at all (Kilian): 1,530 comment lines removed\nfrom the 15 already-committed stylesheets, with _diary.scss arriving new and\nalready free of them — 1,659 lines over 16 files as the sweep actually ran. The compiled CSS is byte-identical — both asset hashes match the\npre-sweep build — so this removed prose and nothing else. .scss is brought under\ntests/test_comment_budget.py at a cap of zero, with a third detector for a\ntrailing comment after code and no allowlist exemption, since a length argument\ncollapses at zero. The rules that prose carried and nothing else stated are now\ntripwire lines in CLAUDE.md; the reasons are gone deliberately.\n\nCLAUDE.md''s landing-page tripwire was stale and is corrected: text over a\nphotograph is legal behind the --ct-scrim overlay, which the code has shipped\nsince it was restored, and the lightest stop under copy is the contrast floor.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoXmKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAip0QACHlI7FzccNHqhFp8GcMPBod\nK6Z2Nn0lYymTE7Hlo7YfjdGvVFwAI8er2pEGnsDE3MBnVslsAKVu3wwT+2T3S7/D\nbc2u9dYcDth8a9ieZ3M5J5ipUP8H+p0/a3JcTuWx/YFpkC/zku5x0LM5gFWxeg3I\nfNwINS8b2JYH+fsyg2JhUdxqmxBRWygHvK4iNdu208KDp6zi6NT/gMBJM7tUvqx5\nv7bHBSzBYtz7vIVw6bwbMMrFlm/GkfF30FEIomrpTpF7Aa0jb9uiRVTCKhx+xTpA\njkqB0hHZ8IK0SF0txTXK1o8+xI5I3UHM1adTbk8WWxiagA7IvEttb3qw495eHwYz\n9ALDe/gzUwqEdH3AJ4anRVTRYVadbdZkaF+PGxLFr0qizN0VPOQLkLYnQTce6uKo\nxGZSDowcYDGv6OoeUQXFJ29sivYXuxnR++tiehpsnI4BVBJvw3tk71hz6AX4BK/i\n5BeJQUZNlkQLxqnzTDlSJOkf6gmGL7QBw4P+J2FZLKXT/QUdmbUaJ9aYKPu4N0xJ\nmOQpau3sFHjIrJs93OBjkeJMGU9nQgFUfPbZ1MWiVeSGF5sClcMqkm6aHBAooyxL\nf+I0rhKGexVJfs/WBP/eJxjU9lgU8fgRXwJDrxagTcu2iZvfRM3kdPqEw8fFaBa4\ntS279G7kFyij2ZjZd/1c\n=KaFX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T15:21:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/c95e03a0211e38616abb8f72234addb46f95462f","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKGM5NWUwM2EwMjExZTM4NjE2YWJiOGY3MjIzNGFkZGI0NmY5NTQ2MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/1c7067857d13bfd9aa9fafe4aa1d18608acf3b58","sha":"1c7067857d13bfd9aa9fafe4aa1d18608acf3b58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/1c7067857d13bfd9aa9fafe4aa1d18608acf3b58"}],"sha":"c95e03a0211e38616abb8f72234addb46f95462f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/c95e03a0211e38616abb8f72234addb46f95462f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/1c7067857d13bfd9aa9fafe4aa1d18608acf3b58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T08:11:36Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T08:11:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(journal): write how a session felt, from the summary or mid-run (#140)\n\n`journal_entry` has carried free text, three 1-5 scales and a weigh-in since\nthe schema was written, with nothing able to fill it: no endpoint, no UI, no\nrows. This adds both ends.\n\n`PUT /api/journal/{client_uuid}` upserts on `(user_id, client_uuid)` with the\nuser taken from the token, so replay-safety and authorisation are one\nmechanism rather than two. An unowned `logged_session_id` gets the same 404 as\none that does not exist. No free text is echoed back, so nothing in the\nresponse needs escaping downstream. The `not_empty` CHECK is enforced at the\nedge as a 422 rather than reaching Postgres as a 500.\n\nThe write form renders in two places against one draft: inline on the session\nsummary, and in an overlay over the running player, because a note is often\nworth taking mid-session rather than only after Finish. Both reuse the run''s\nuuid, so a second submit edits the row instead of adding one. The draft lives\non the persisted `RunRecord` and is written on every keystroke, so a failed\nwrite cannot lose what was typed. The save control states what the press would\ndo — absent when there is nothing to send, Save when nothing has landed\n(including after a 4xx), Update only when the server holds a row.\n\nOpening the overlay stops the countdown through the player''s existing pause,\nand gives back only the pause it took: a run the climber had already paused\ndeliberately stays paused on close.\n\nThis is the app''s first overlay, so it owns the machinery every later one will\ncopy — focus in and back to its opener, a Tab trap, Escape, and a visible\nClose as the primary way out. Native `<dialog>` was rejected because jsdom\nimplements neither `showModal` nor `close`, which would have left every focus\nand trap claim unprovable in the gate.\n\nThe weigh-in input is gated on `show_body_metrics`, and an unread profile\nreads as off, so nothing prompts for a weight it was told not to ask for. No\ncopy anywhere frames weight as something to reduce.\n\nNo migration: DB stays at `0008` and `GENERATOR_VERSION` is untouched. The\nper-set body-weight snapshot stays null until #135, its only consumer.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7470b5fcd8c58f09ca710174a8e814023004796d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/7470b5fcd8c58f09ca710174a8e814023004796d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/1c7067857d13bfd9aa9fafe4aa1d18608acf3b58","verification":{"payload":"tree 7470b5fcd8c58f09ca710174a8e814023004796d\nparent 969031c7b0617d7b00fc92efa39af7987278956a\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788855096 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788855096 +0200\n\nfeat(journal): write how a session felt, from the summary or mid-run (#140)\n\n`journal_entry` has carried free text, three 1-5 scales and a weigh-in since\nthe schema was written, with nothing able to fill it: no endpoint, no UI, no\nrows. This adds both ends.\n\n`PUT /api/journal/{client_uuid}` upserts on `(user_id, client_uuid)` with the\nuser taken from the token, so replay-safety and authorisation are one\nmechanism rather than two. An unowned `logged_session_id` gets the same 404 as\none that does not exist. No free text is echoed back, so nothing in the\nresponse needs escaping downstream. The `not_empty` CHECK is enforced at the\nedge as a 422 rather than reaching Postgres as a 500.\n\nThe write form renders in two places against one draft: inline on the session\nsummary, and in an overlay over the running player, because a note is often\nworth taking mid-session rather than only after Finish. Both reuse the run''s\nuuid, so a second submit edits the row instead of adding one. The draft lives\non the persisted `RunRecord` and is written on every keystroke, so a failed\nwrite cannot lose what was typed. The save control states what the press would\ndo — absent when there is nothing to send, Save when nothing has landed\n(including after a 4xx), Update only when the server holds a row.\n\nOpening the overlay stops the countdown through the player''s existing pause,\nand gives back only the pause it took: a run the climber had already paused\ndeliberately stays paused on close.\n\nThis is the app''s first overlay, so it owns the machinery every later one will\ncopy — focus in and back to its opener, a Tab trap, Escape, and a visible\nClose as the primary way out. Native `<dialog>` was rejected because jsdom\nimplements neither `showModal` nor `close`, which would have left every focus\nand trap claim unprovable in the gate.\n\nThe weigh-in input is gated on `show_body_metrics`, and an unread profile\nreads as off, so nothing prompts for a weight it was told not to ask for. No\ncopy anywhere frames weight as something to reduce.\n\nNo migration: DB stays at `0008` and `GENERATOR_VERSION` is untouched. The\nper-set body-weight snapshot stays null until #135, its only consumer.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn8M4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMmAQABmUs85V/tD9b5WErLUu+DwY\nkb2emxW+enq1chKqaBagMSROOj2c4zleZGm+1c6MnBtK8n0NIYVpuamDu576ozOZ\nBRgWMpkP6NkN8MdkmBQkffit9lWIjg8VBj7LKcaIS+8h45AyDLeuofVv4b5KS+WP\nD2vgNsqnW0ifJ09m71/mcWxeyCsW/i4840zegWUtw2+KYrNxgJolYVHGjr4H6kzZ\n0Yv7lklh3dCAnIiz+NY5e9QNAOcBwycyibn8YPYvXOrEUoAI5SnbF84P7+Mj9Zz4\n0JUQ2okYy3TklcaJo7FxU9UjTRI0DXZYommo9H9xyqvL95jG9Bw2AXFtv93FAMUg\n9aLGwzBQLWl2qywu3j2tA/x3FDstd7wsMnob+Ya2bhjlXbejOyTuk2CBr3vFQTiO\nutbAh/b4xbOzW6bagrL0FT03DPVRuYK+yCkh5Ec7EJDrb9L2S4/r4R94c/dkSyuj\nQFy6wJDTbTwsPbpcxMXaQTzWcuwWFdOtWwBcqYhbmddHgoumJxmGPNs1U0E3U+rl\nLOHZk4CIxIrEGQANyD0i9cVOtz1+ekbgsl4OOFv75GTc4EuL9Vr28bePZ7PKCVpu\ntB55sYYW4WEBQAUK02yAMLqqy1MwQlZc/Er8HSwjnDJ39+yv+TsYXN5XWKrGc5Bl\n/udm/5Vbp7r5HzBe8q7c\n=89Ms\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T08:11:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/1c7067857d13bfd9aa9fafe4aa1d18608acf3b58","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDFjNzA2Nzg1N2QxM2JmZDlhYTlmYWZlNGFhMWQxODYwOGFjZjNiNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/969031c7b0617d7b00fc92efa39af7987278956a","sha":"969031c7b0617d7b00fc92efa39af7987278956a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/969031c7b0617d7b00fc92efa39af7987278956a"}],"sha":"1c7067857d13bfd9aa9fafe4aa1d18608acf3b58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/1c7067857d13bfd9aa9fafe4aa1d18608acf3b58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/969031c7b0617d7b00fc92efa39af7987278956a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T13:15:10Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T13:15:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: cut ascent logging from the product (#79) (#136)\n\nAscents are cut, not deferred. Nothing in the app trains on one: the plan\ngenerator takes no new inputs and `current_grade_id` is stored rather than\nderived, so an ascent log would have fed only two unbuilt display views.\n\nThe feature rested on `Ascent`''s docstring opening \"the emotional payload of\nthe whole app\" — a sentence both `server/sessions/__init__.py` and #79 were\nquoting, and which the register mis-attributed to CLAUDE.md, where the word\n\"ascent\" has never appeared.\n\nThe three `ascent*` tables stay as inert schema; dropping them is the contract\nhalf of expand -> deploy -> contract and is scheduled separately. The session\npackage''s note is rewritten from a promise into the prohibition it needs to be,\nso nobody wires them up.\n\n`server/sessions/routes.py`''s \"Ascents are not loggable here.\" stays: it is a\nroute docstring, so FastAPI ships it as the OpenAPI description and it is\nfrozen under the generated types'' `openapi-sha256`. Deleting it fails\n`test_the_generated_types_were_built_from_this_api` (b33338e3 != 02aac3d6);\nverified red, then restored. It reads as a flat statement of the contract.\n\nThe grade-floor filter in `web/src/profile/grades.ts` is kept — the ascent log\njustified one bullet about its *placement*, never the filter, and two of the\nthree placement reasons stand alone.\n\nREADME item 4 is rewritten: the diary is rescoped from replaying what you did,\nwhich the plan screen already shows, to recording how it felt.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b1e794c1eb952a5d98059dafd209891de1a6eb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/0b1e794c1eb952a5d98059dafd209891de1a6eb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/969031c7b0617d7b00fc92efa39af7987278956a","verification":{"payload":"tree 0b1e794c1eb952a5d98059dafd209891de1a6eb9\nparent 9956d36377678d0e521a94eb765a3a04298dbfd2\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788786910 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788786910 +0000\n\ndocs: cut ascent logging from the product (#79) (#136)\n\nAscents are cut, not deferred. Nothing in the app trains on one: the plan\ngenerator takes no new inputs and `current_grade_id` is stored rather than\nderived, so an ascent log would have fed only two unbuilt display views.\n\nThe feature rested on `Ascent`''s docstring opening \"the emotional payload of\nthe whole app\" — a sentence both `server/sessions/__init__.py` and #79 were\nquoting, and which the register mis-attributed to CLAUDE.md, where the word\n\"ascent\" has never appeared.\n\nThe three `ascent*` tables stay as inert schema; dropping them is the contract\nhalf of expand -> deploy -> contract and is scheduled separately. The session\npackage''s note is rewritten from a promise into the prohibition it needs to be,\nso nobody wires them up.\n\n`server/sessions/routes.py`''s \"Ascents are not loggable here.\" stays: it is a\nroute docstring, so FastAPI ships it as the OpenAPI description and it is\nfrozen under the generated types'' `openapi-sha256`. Deleting it fails\n`test_the_generated_types_were_built_from_this_api` (b33338e3 != 02aac3d6);\nverified red, then restored. It reads as a flat statement of the contract.\n\nThe grade-floor filter in `web/src/profile/grades.ts` is kept — the ascent log\njustified one bullet about its *placement*, never the filter, and two of the\nthree placement reasons stand alone.\n\nREADME item 4 is rewritten: the diary is rescoped from replaying what you did,\nwhich the plan screen already shows, to recording how it felt.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnrjeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvp4QAIhJM1+hHiuNy3mFkffWJpGA\ndE1BEXkLLQKw400N1OAZ01yaAQKEZ7mUuojnzOSz+NHDIwlpOXfOM06rept/ofde\nQ7zdmJG1DiquKfgI2zn7Bz6no/ryaRUTZus4BYyyHj/ACOsu86J+Zgm0NhiABqAv\noQj8s98ZybIjz7YhHA5K57De/qsOH3a2bFnuSX34hKbnk373zcAYQ0zul7RX5zDC\nJBJsEsQvohAv+Mv89r0GXM3hDghmGRFzt3ECJFSvn99aqJs/u+/l5Cs0huQbgYhn\nam3nOwocaTpr+5Rjqj9H/3t0Q1Vv90iBVADRu9GXMP+q2pTsXjHOVRSB8MYr4/qy\ni2zDgTNllDDTuo1d2Ll25JgIRoh84Ki7a0cqFbmK4b+s/pVLf1lZ6cfEMFV5I+Xd\nmfoWojhijGqJF1flYSgdhgFMNqHQIiJYCA5bDfHDydfgTIvJ9sbJh+Bj47/MspzR\n95usv4uuXK6alR74sj9v4Jj11VY8kz8xu5utnFw/lI5tYHdScZqq+30iJxqYlRQH\n/p+JxbRMf3dbqZMZxWYvZy5a4jl+HT8M5Tf2jyTizM7S5pJf2944mj1meg/IGd0J\n8/tLKw7lWbv0hbuI8LXRk7NnY5pKyu8hApkKmTSwULzZXpr/5CDVtfRWv3+WTmuq\n/BcD0ZMZTTzqjKx2YXBP\n=+c10\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T13:15:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/969031c7b0617d7b00fc92efa39af7987278956a","node_id":"