ll,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/80e9c093f88217ebcacfc9e724a8062e9632de80","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDgwZTljMDkzZjg4MjE3ZWJjYWNmYzllNzI0YTgwNjJlOTYzMmRlODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/7ffa9bd313f507577c3170e334af9fcf750bf1ff","sha":"7ffa9bd313f507577c3170e334af9fcf750bf1ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/7ffa9bd313f507577c3170e334af9fcf750bf1ff"}],"sha":"80e9c093f88217ebcacfc9e724a8062e9632de80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/80e9c093f88217ebcacfc9e724a8062e9632de80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/7ffa9bd313f507577c3170e334af9fcf750bf1ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T10:23:21Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T10:23:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): bump fast-uri to 3.1.7 to clear four dev-only advisories (#132)\n\n`workbox-build` → `ajv@8.20.0` → `fast-uri@3.1.5` carried four high-severity\nadvisories (SSRF and host confusion), all patched in 3.1.6. ajv''s declared\nrange is `^3.0.1`, so a lockfile refresh was sufficient — no `package.json`\nentry and no `overrides` clause to maintain.\n\nThe dependency is build-time only (`\"dev\": true`): ajv uses fast-uri to\nresolve JSON-schema `$id`/`$ref` while validating workbox''s own config, so\nno untrusted URI reaches it and it never enters the browser bundle. Cleared\nas advisory noise on a public repo, not as an exposure.\n\n`npm ci` reports 0 vulnerabilities; the build still emits `sw.js`, which is\nthe path that consumes it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3eb5ec02faece39dfd7ef93d2fd5a5a253dc31a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/f3eb5ec02faece39dfd7ef93d2fd5a5a253dc31a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/7ffa9bd313f507577c3170e334af9fcf750bf1ff","verification":{"payload":"tree f3eb5ec02faece39dfd7ef93d2fd5a5a253dc31a\nparent 84852eb5a8231adcb778ffc70af059a4b2c18b4f\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788776601 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788776601 +0200\n\nchore(deps): bump fast-uri to 3.1.7 to clear four dev-only advisories (#132)\n\n`workbox-build` → `ajv@8.20.0` → `fast-uri@3.1.5` carried four high-severity\nadvisories (SSRF and host confusion), all patched in 3.1.6. ajv''s declared\nrange is `^3.0.1`, so a lockfile refresh was sufficient — no `package.json`\nentry and no `overrides` clause to maintain.\n\nThe dependency is build-time only (`\"dev\": true`): ajv uses fast-uri to\nresolve JSON-schema `$id`/`$ref` while validating workbox''s own config, so\nno untrusted URI reaches it and it never enters the browser bundle. Cleared\nas advisory noise on a public repo, not as an exposure.\n\n`npm ci` reports 0 vulnerabilities; the build still emits `sw.js`, which is\nthe path that consumes it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnpCZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeM4QABkQpP73ERj0s7IH7aThR2ji\njIIGMG4MLL7mCFdMKlFgv+MHTUnD/GWafiwVGT/2E3BMS0Cd38jMiWTirpWG+lKs\nq4Cs4KteuKe6XFPUKM2D0BTTQPVmWtA6G6h5ajSUZ7QEILHYPW8XFjMQ189qCiKb\nFTVNHHVXxnicjBw0YtXsBpaKs4UcUJOVR4EgBSkOesjI7EilJBYg10cAdCwOi7DH\nuGry636Spsz9jXkRlNiLs1/lPHzGvZTAU5yBb6IeiQMLXOoAWkyocZ1r0q1U4dCE\n4ItJIUtvMHHa9hiLXKAUo8eepoGdwCOkieIF2p6ux8KakAvi8buzZSsgBi+3AytM\nL0jSO7i7mU5nRMItavR5h3Qc3Dfn+2Z1ybSIA8Ex8PBBRuRG2lo+6cIdzAMHy/D/\noO8mclY4EIXuq+v7YgBQU90X6LQqH40JoSVSX9vt/z+cW4ziiRklJpg6k/cX9QBg\nL5Y5FxCfW89zha47ArQ1j3TMAk5Q6eKI7WLecODFLgoazwXOHbrfZ/loqAAIL2K2\nWp4HNhUjg4WotmgdrYMkqD2ri1KmPFshqStBNtlfHV11oKLck6ud/yvQ5Wztl7NJ\n8WjwRk/Drx2cQm90XEj+l9Qp/059U3me7I/5F/O7VJZYwCmUfDM+qPe0OLqeTkNo\nzZQHqPmwucTgpIdOQ32F\n=cZk9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T10:23:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/7ffa9bd313f507577c3170e334af9fcf750bf1ff","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDdmZmE5YmQzMTNmNTA3NTc3YzMxNzBlMzM0YWY5ZmNmNzUwYmYxZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/84852eb5a8231adcb778ffc70af059a4b2c18b4f","sha":"84852eb5a8231adcb778ffc70af059a4b2c18b4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/84852eb5a8231adcb778ffc70af059a4b2c18b4f"}],"sha":"7ffa9bd313f507577c3170e334af9fcf750bf1ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/7ffa9bd313f507577c3170e334af9fcf750bf1ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/84852eb5a8231adcb778ffc70af059a4b2c18b4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T10:06:46Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T10:06:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: retire the plan files and put every decision they held in the repo (#131)\n\n`~/.claude/plans/` (22 files) and the archived project memory are deleted. They were a\nlog of finished work: 1455 lines of doctrine for 46 rulings, plus per-PR state files and\nreports. Everything load-bearing now lives where a reader meets it.\n\nTwo prohibitions had NO home in the repo and are now tripwires (CLAUDE.md +2):\n\n- \"no user input, no override, no new form control\" (Kilian, 2026-08-24) was deleted by\n  35b5ace along with the gap-derived length it was attached to. The reason went stale and\n  the prohibition went with it — it existed in no file, and not in the archive either.\n- ruling 7''s three declined dose corrections (`lead_route_doubles`, `campus_ladders`,\n  `hangboard_repeaters`) never reached the repo at all.\n\nFive citation sites offered a ruling number as their only justification; each now states\nthe decision. The other 226 of 239 already did — the house style is `ruling N''s <noun\nphrase naming the decision>`, which is why nobody noticed that rulings 8, 21, 22 and 28\nhave been dangling for some time.\n\nColumn widths, 1310 -> 1312 arms: `test_authored_strings_fit_their_columns` is extended\nfrom `EXERCISES` to the vocabulary tuples and gains a twin in `test_grades.py` for the\ngrade ladder, plus one arm for `plan.generator_version`, which no blueprint tree carries.\nLimits are read off `model.__table__.columns`, and a field-set arm stops a rename leaving\nthe check green over zero comparisons. Shown red both ways first.\n\nCorrected in `climbing.py`: F14''s length fill measured 44/55/64%, not the 42/54/65% the\ncomment claimed, and it cited \"advanced `power`\" — a phase no plan has carried since\nruling 51. The trio share was stale by ~1pp. Basis now stated inline so it cannot drift.\n\nAlso dropped three docstring pointers to `.claude/` state files that have not existed\nfor weeks, and one `→` pointer that named the wrong archive section.\n\nCLAUDE.md is +2 over its own \"archive one to add one\" budget: the only archivable\ncandidate is the sole pointer to its own archive heading, and archiving a prohibition is\nnot allowed. Left for Kilian.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2f01ffc81a7bb5764cd819202021a1155d27db9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/e2f01ffc81a7bb5764cd819202021a1155d27db9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/84852eb5a8231adcb778ffc70af059a4b2c18b4f","verification":{"payload":"tree e2f01ffc81a7bb5764cd819202021a1155d27db9\nparent 35b5ace5819c7e4a88b048be6b268a6abaf30ef9\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788775606 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788775606 +0200\n\ndocs: retire the plan files and put every decision they held in the repo (#131)\n\n`~/.claude/plans/` (22 files) and the archived project memory are deleted. They were a\nlog of finished work: 1455 lines of doctrine for 46 rulings, plus per-PR state files and\nreports. Everything load-bearing now lives where a reader meets it.\n\nTwo prohibitions had NO home in the repo and are now tripwires (CLAUDE.md +2):\n\n- \"no user input, no override, no new form control\" (Kilian, 2026-08-24) was deleted by\n  35b5ace along with the gap-derived length it was attached to. The reason went stale and\n  the prohibition went with it — it existed in no file, and not in the archive either.\n- ruling 7''s three declined dose corrections (`lead_route_doubles`, `campus_ladders`,\n  `hangboard_repeaters`) never reached the repo at all.\n\nFive citation sites offered a ruling number as their only justification; each now states\nthe decision. The other 226 of 239 already did — the house style is `ruling N''s <noun\nphrase naming the decision>`, which is why nobody noticed that rulings 8, 21, 22 and 28\nhave been dangling for some time.\n\nColumn widths, 1310 -> 1312 arms: `test_authored_strings_fit_their_columns` is extended\nfrom `EXERCISES` to the vocabulary tuples and gains a twin in `test_grades.py` for the\ngrade ladder, plus one arm for `plan.generator_version`, which no blueprint tree carries.\nLimits are read off `model.__table__.columns`, and a field-set arm stops a rename leaving\nthe check green over zero comparisons. Shown red both ways first.\n\nCorrected in `climbing.py`: F14''s length fill measured 44/55/64%, not the 42/54/65% the\ncomment claimed, and it cited \"advanced `power`\" — a phase no plan has carried since\nruling 51. The trio share was stale by ~1pp. Basis now stated inline so it cannot drift.\n\nAlso dropped three docstring pointers to `.claude/` state files that have not existed\nfor weeks, and one `→` pointer that named the wrong archive section.\n\nCLAUDE.md is +2 over its own \"archive one to add one\" budget: the only archivable\ncandidate is the sole pointer to its own archive heading, and archiving a prohibition is\nnot allowed. Left for Kilian.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnoy2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATI8QAHq5/DbCYter7/Ik7zfktyut\nLzkcQTtnZD35aBxpE+6Kd4TUhrU+cnoz4zkSutYzz83pbjwG5060yFhHopvzMq+Q\nKcRIoD7tiAx6LWcDdFO8eHmUH8C7JXoO4Be2DZfcPskBkl70Rj9KpSA1b07XaRzb\n5b3+aWp9lB77oH0xl+UWoS4kMM/6yZb/k6YlVq/5z2KCT5l3iXLpDmvN9jBKJSge\nE20rVs87DL+zKWhzeD8JtAtNw7NTKX2/MskSrwN9Pc8q8uDvTHx9PxpRwinT8Pa2\n5ICD4gov2JIYGzJqta2sKItGpLQMPkns5sNwwnrLg+G5dcLx6/sGHjxZPjQ+qZ33\n6xYwDYsFzOU+MQJ75OUmHBkFWtWtiCYZftuse2wi5ddfG+1UgUKVueyfQ8y/S+wl\n5MT4AfBGN6p3gbWew3fYnI4hBkjZqQ3iKXGfawJQOLk/SJryT921Hhe2F74buHxW\nucfpGb4goSJRSlEYTxxg43k9lhLhHJW0mUkLAyL7Mt9oZ1XoNpkzv+tvqwDrYCri\ngXly1PEaoDVLHJfLqQTIwQHRm3xUM0dDYxRrWjAGvcs9RqsdYLGJ6yTk+D5pE01N\nWOg9/nti2zkj32ZQUOe+ck7kRkdrDNQVoPQIOcfZb1X0S+keVdfUpJ0wcHWq9AAo\nidbjL921qgwCl8GYxg7u\n=hTDa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T10:06:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/84852eb5a8231adcb778ffc70af059a4b2c18b4f","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDg0ODUyZWI1YTgyMzFhZGNiNzc4ZmZjNzBhZjA1OWE0YjJjMThiNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/35b5ace5819c7e4a88b048be6b268a6abaf30ef9","sha":"35b5ace5819c7e4a88b048be6b268a6abaf30ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/35b5ace5819c7e4a88b048be6b268a6abaf30ef9"}],"sha":"84852eb5a8231adcb778ffc70af059a4b2c18b4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/84852eb5a8231adcb778ffc70af059a4b2c18b4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/35b5ace5819c7e4a88b048be6b268a6abaf30ef9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T08:14:10Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T08:14:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(planner): fix plan length at sixteen weeks in four blocks, and drop the power block (#130)\n\nRulings 49/51/52/54. Plan length stops deriving from the grade gap: every plan is\nsixteen weeks as four 4-week blocks, in the order base -> strength -> power\nendurance -> performance (candidate D2). Ruling 37''s shape is untouched —\nLOADING_WEEKS, the microcycle machinery and the deload floors are all unchanged and\nonly the phase list and the length derivation are re-authored.\n\nPlan digest c1009f3a57f759d5 -> 6d1509cdf6ae6045: 7349 blocks, 148 540 min, over the\n24-profile sweep. Blocks -18.1% and minutes -20.0%, which is exactly 16/20, while per\nprofile-week goes 386.7 -> 386.8 — weekly volume is untouched and the plan is simply\nshorter. GENERATOR_VERSION 8.0.0 -> 9.0.0.\n\nThe POWER block is the one that goes, because dropping it costs the power quality\n27.4% -> 24.2% of prescribed seconds while dropping the power-endurance block would\nhave cost power endurance 9.4% -> 2.4%, three quarters of itself.\n\nThis removes F9''s shipping surface. PHASE_GUIDE[POWER]''s paragraph stops shipping and\ntakes with it \"Anaerobic capacity is kept alive at roughly one session a week\" — the\nsentence PR #124 made true (113/126 power-weeks at 1) in order to close F9. F9 was\nclosed by making a sentence true, and this deletes the sentence. Deleting rather than\nmerely not rendering it required re-pointing the PHASE_GUIDE coverage guard from the\nPhase enum at the phases a generated plan actually carries.\n\nCopy re-authored to measured truths, none softened:\n\n- The power-endurance day boundary moved five -> four days and now pins three\n  regimes that must tile day counts 1-7: biggest at four days and under (24 of 24\n  profiles), \"about even\" at five (3 of 6 each way, thinnest margin 0.2 points), and\n  ordinary climbing bigger at six or seven (12 of 12). The old five-day boundary was\n  guarded by an unread constant — sabotaging it came back green.\n- PHASE_GUIDE[BASE]''s adaptation-time sentence (ruling 54, F2) now states the source\n  requirement and what the plan delivers side by side, and the anaerobic range is\n  four to twelve of sixteen weeks, guarded over 90 plans spanning session counts 1-7\n  and all three weakness values. An earlier figure of eight to twelve was measured\n  over a sweep starting at two sessions a week and was false for every one-day-a-week\n  climber; an arm now fails if that audience is narrowed back.\n\nRemoved as having no subject on a fixed-length plan: beyond_one_plan_note,\nNoteKind.TARGET_BEYOND_ONE_PLAN, _GAP_TABLE and block_count_for. Guard 8''s table was\nthe decision it pinned, and clamp(2 + gap, 2, 8) was an app invention its comment\ncalled \"verbatim from the approved plan\" — deleted rather than retitled.\n\nLength keeps two independent sources on purpose. generate() derives week_count from\nthe spans and tests/test_plans_api.py reads the constant, so a change to one and not\nthe other is caught rather than tautological.\n\nSix library rows are no longer prescribed to anyone and are registered in\n_ACCEPTABLY_UNREACHABLE with a reason and a reproducible sabotage each. No exercise\ncontent changed; exercises.py is not in this diff.\n\nFiles F28, the plan-absolute rotation index: _intended_aspect keys its turn on the\nplan-absolute week number, so where a block sits decides what its sessions draw. One\nmechanism, three symptoms — the perverse declared-weakness row (declaring\npower_endurance lowers it, -3.3% on one profile of 24) and two of the six orphans.\nIsolating control: hold sixteen weeks and four blocks and swap only the middle two,\nand that row reads +5656 s green, so it is the position and not the length. The fix\nis a block-relative turn; it is unpriced, changes what every user is prescribed, and\nis deliberately out of scope here. The registered row asserts more than the arm it\nreplaced: prescribed minutes rise on 48 of 48 rows, only ruling 29''s elastic filler\nruns backwards, and breaking the boost outright fails 47 of 49 arms including the\nregistered one.\n\nArms 1327 -> 1310: 16 deleted as no longer meaning anything under a fixed length, 14\nlost to re-basing two MAX_BLOCKS sweeps and guard 9 onto a fixed 4-tuple, 13 added.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"78f9064895ea8725444a71aa5879f29293635ed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/78f9064895ea8725444a71aa5879f29293635ed7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/35b5ace5819c7e4a88b048be6b268a6abaf30ef9","verification":{"payload":"tree 78f9064895ea8725444a71aa5879f29293635ed7\nparent 23d844264d5dd315d1959fec1e1535c89e136d6e\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788768850 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788768850 +0200\n\nfeat(planner): fix plan length at sixteen weeks in four blocks, and drop the power block (#130)\n\nRulings 49/51/52/54. Plan length stops deriving from the grade gap: every plan is\nsixteen weeks as four 4-week blocks, in the order base -> strength -> power\nendurance -> performance (candidate D2). Ruling 37''s shape is untouched —\nLOADING_WEEKS, the microcycle machinery and the deload floors are all unchanged and\nonly the phase list and the length derivation are re-authored.\n\nPlan digest c1009f3a57f759d5 -> 6d1509cdf6ae6045: 7349 blocks, 148 540 min, over the\n24-profile sweep. Blocks -18.1% and minutes -20.0%, which is exactly 16/20, while per\nprofile-week goes 386.7 -> 386.8 — weekly volume is untouched and the plan is simply\nshorter. GENERATOR_VERSION 8.0.0 -> 9.0.0.\n\nThe POWER block is the one that goes, because dropping it costs the power quality\n27.4% -> 24.2% of prescribed seconds while dropping the power-endurance block would\nhave cost power endurance 9.4% -> 2.4%, three quarters of itself.\n\nThis removes F9''s shipping surface. PHASE_GUIDE[POWER]''s paragraph stops shipping and\ntakes with it \"Anaerobic capacity is kept alive at roughly one session a week\" — the\nsentence PR #124 made true (113/126 power-weeks at 1) in order to close F9. F9 was\nclosed by making a sentence true, and this deletes the sentence. Deleting rather than\nmerely not rendering it required re-pointing the PHASE_GUIDE coverage guard from the\nPhase enum at the phases a generated plan actually carries.\n\nCopy re-authored to measured truths, none softened:\n\n- The power-endurance day boundary moved five -> four days and now pins three\n  regimes that must tile day counts 1-7: biggest at four days and under (24 of 24\n  profiles), \"about even\" at five (3 of 6 each way, thinnest margin 0.2 points), and\n  ordinary climbing bigger at six or seven (12 of 12). The old five-day boundary was\n  guarded by an unread constant — sabotaging it came back green.\n- PHASE_GUIDE[BASE]''s adaptation-time sentence (ruling 54, F2) now states the source\n  requirement and what the plan delivers side by side, and the anaerobic range is\n  four to twelve of sixteen weeks, guarded over 90 plans spanning session counts 1-7\n  and all three weakness values. An earlier figure of eight to twelve was measured\n  over a sweep starting at two sessions a week and was false for every one-day-a-week\n  climber; an arm now fails if that audience is narrowed back.\n\nRemoved as having no subject on a fixed-length plan: beyond_one_plan_note,\nNoteKind.TARGET_BEYOND_ONE_PLAN, _GAP_TABLE and block_count_for. Guard 8''s table was\nthe decision it pinned, and clamp(2 + gap, 2, 8) was an app invention its comment\ncalled \"verbatim from the approved plan\" — deleted rather than retitled.\n\nLength keeps two independent sources on purpose. generate() derives week_count from\nthe spans and tests/test_plans_api.py reads the constant, so a change to one and not\nthe other is caught rather than tautological.\n\nSix library rows are no longer prescribed to anyone and are registered in\n_ACCEPTABLY_UNREACHABLE with a reason and a reproducible sabotage each. No exercise\ncontent changed; exercises.py is not in this diff.\n\nFiles F28, the plan-absolute rotation index: _intended_aspect keys its turn on the\nplan-absolute week number, so where a block sits decides what its sessions draw. One\nmechanism, three symptoms — the perverse declared-weakness row (declaring\npower_endurance lowers it, -3.3% on one profile of 24) and two of the six orphans.\nIsolating control: hold sixteen weeks and four blocks and swap only the middle two,\nand that row reads +5656 s green, so it is the position and not the length. The fix\nis a block-relative turn; it is unpriced, changes what every user is prescribed, and\nis deliberately out of scope here. The registered row asserts more than the arm it\nreplaced: prescribed minutes rise on 48 of 48 rows, only ruling 29''s elastic filler\nruns backwards, and breaking the boost outright fails 47 of 49 arms including the\nregistered one.\n\nArms 1327 -> 1310: 16 deleted as no longer meaning anything under a fixed length, 14\nlost to re-basing two MAX_BLOCKS sweeps and guard 9 onto a fixed 4-tuple, 13 added.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnnJSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfoMQAF6+II44UBeRav3ab+v1au9v\noAA7RHtCSLt6+hb7zJgY19MuTwpLvRrO2G+Ylqhz1Hbam8ffJBDYTjq7Nj/M/raE\npTefAHY+BHvK9enz66eg1yMFjsHzNfdCR3708ZYC/8N+kbEBoSTEPFYC6EmyjuNs\nNMpm2KukBNr9NlCcsPtBQFD6j/Mezni2RFKud7qMGfbKI2cRW/VTzzuaUzrumfpw\nfbAgDSumEJfZ/SgF6qMsjfp4k8aJVmkiGHeP+kbJT5y8imFbpqQbJSSVnyEd59qr\nqu4t8PnFEiG86K23ga2cRpctHQ4Gw7FAaxUGdbXfQwNycsxpwPplurGUMzDQtOGO\n//UY+aCyiSKAo22QOeIVShQunjJti/fiEkmmxPSTlSuuDUMAu4LXSozRkNRy6Njz\nFZq+Wqg03WBHJE3hhVP5seHlCdFAQpQS+y78kVzyKupswymblUl79PSvtFiqXho0\nKqHeN1LdpusVca+PdpbRxCYsufpYX5hudHtwLl2iHnzEMQ9d1HynrXyeO7hrIB2Z\ntFsk36AY6YZrg3RGYycJc9lJBoLKo4rjE3HYVlaTrNOrSxHbNrjzFrwd8WS8AHR5\nf7Yyhyrv4sXRql/KKaXKnTiQFE2BrXcu/06zt0/aumNN4xfEFQ5b2D5AfSwOYykX\n+//4XTWdeM99vcM5XuCo\n=e9xu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T08:14:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/35b5ace5819c7e4a88b048be6b268a6abaf30ef9","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDM1YjVhY2U1ODE5YzdlNGE4OGIwNDhiZTZiMjY4YTZhYmFmMzBlZjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/23d844264d5dd315d1959fec1e1535c89e136d6e","sha":"23d844264d5dd315d1959fec1e1535c89e136d6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/23d844264d5dd315d1959fec1e1535c89e136d6e"}],"sha":"35b5ace5819c7e4a88b048be6b268a6abaf30ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/35b5ace5819c7e4a88b048be6b268a6abaf30ef9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/23d844264d5dd315d1959fec1e1535c89e136d6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T19:24:43Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T19:24:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(planner): make a plan that misreports its own length unconstructible (#129)\n\nCloses the two structural traps the plan-length report found, on today''s code\nwith today''s behaviour unchanged, so the fixed-16-week change lands where the\nfailure is impossible.\n\nInvariant 1 - a plan must tile its own `week_count`, split across two\nconstructors because the claim has two halves. `MesocycleBlueprint`: the\nmicrocycle `week_no`s, in order, are exactly `range(start_week, end_week+1)`.\n`PlanBlueprint`: those numbers concatenated over all mesocycles are exactly\n`range(1, week_count+1)`. Tuple equality rather than a pairwise contiguity\nloop, which would pass vacuously on an empty `mesocycles` tuple.\n\nInvariant 2 - one read. `generate()` takes `mesocycle_spans(block_count_for(\ngap))` and derives `week_count` from `spans[-1].end_week`. This fixes nothing\ntoday: `week_count_for(gap)` is defined as `block_count_for(gap) *\nWEEKS_PER_BLOCK`, so both former call sites already routed through one formula\nand could not disagree. It fires the moment plan length gets a second source\nof truth, which is the next PR. `week_count_for` is left in place so\n`tests/test_plans_api.py:136` stays a cross-check rather than a tautology.\n\nDigest byte-identical over the 24-profile sweep, `b079fce09ee80126` both\nsides, so `GENERATOR_VERSION` stays at 8.0.0 per PR #127''s precedent.\n\nAlso deletes two comments that told the reader the schema cannot check\nsomething it can - `check (weekday = extract(isodow from scheduled_on) - 1)`\nis accepted by Postgres and bites, verified against the test database. No\nconstraint added: the Python check fails earlier and names the day.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"481121379ee7072b129920191b734e5e6fb13dad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/481121379ee7072b129920191b734e5e6fb13dad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/23d844264d5dd315d1959fec1e1535c89e136d6e","verification":{"payload":"tree 481121379ee7072b129920191b734e5e6fb13dad\nparent 87b7b5ead7019d3e077498474231abb726ff2e57\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788722683 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788722683 +0200\n\nfix(planner): make a plan that misreports its own length unconstructible (#129)\n\nCloses the two structural traps the plan-length report found, on today''s code\nwith today''s behaviour unchanged, so the fixed-16-week change lands where the\nfailure is impossible.\n\nInvariant 1 - a plan must tile its own `week_count`, split across two\nconstructors because the claim has two halves. `MesocycleBlueprint`: the\nmicrocycle `week_no`s, in order, are exactly `range(start_week, end_week+1)`.\n`PlanBlueprint`: those numbers concatenated over all mesocycles are exactly\n`range(1, week_count+1)`. Tuple equality rather than a pairwise contiguity\nloop, which would pass vacuously on an empty `mesocycles` tuple.\n\nInvariant 2 - one read. `generate()` takes `mesocycle_spans(block_count_for(\ngap))` and derives `week_count` from `spans[-1].end_week`. This fixes nothing\ntoday: `week_count_for(gap)` is defined as `block_count_for(gap) *\nWEEKS_PER_BLOCK`, so both former call sites already routed through one formula\nand could not disagree. It fires the moment plan length gets a second source\nof truth, which is the next PR. `week_count_for` is left in place so\n`tests/test_plans_api.py:136` stays a cross-check rather than a tautology.\n\nDigest byte-identical over the 24-profile sweep, `b079fce09ee80126` both\nsides, so `GENERATOR_VERSION` stays at 8.0.0 per PR #127''s precedent.\n\nAlso deletes two comments that told the reader the schema cannot check\nsomething it can - `check (weekday = extract(isodow from scheduled_on) - 1)`\nis accepted by Postgres and bites, verified against the test database. No\nconstraint added: the Python check fails earlier and names the day.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnb37CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp44QAIsPlQyMTjhnDrq0XXh7V7Q6\nkxQ5kinfTR2Wbn9L0S1IDTgBPosZWzXsn/V47bdDtGsL6hztasqEOHI3aGiCfsN3\nNHhJENORyjvRwz+6zlfymhD3QjrHIPuHB3w1QyOhvHZH7fKOQ4WrdrHxWFPfdQRz\nDOyz+iDSg9FCEvR/zrnLecKDus3e9sLkIExSIu3a+VYSHc9skOSUaz9fuANy1UfB\nAyRU3oJiUriAd3Gu2ItVdg5KvldYzbL1oz+Ig1+xaPNkfY+VF4f8YlsiOWi2eHYA\ncTX3Nn5fa/ttHuZwFuNLGK6sEa2kcPhnd/kvoHsQNZ9z7SI06+qymV75edZ+WNY/\nqEkIKiUOyhe8n9hyAOxK43amxzK0iheCJ3IHkgkP5jpJcHAvgkZbwhYE+FpDOnna\nxZx7eJmeZT8YoPXYSByNvS951o5WVuBkvkrTf9Ljl7kvzRJYuFN768sOetkb79Tz\ntpqTjluDSaVSTww+O4shH1Ww/zGlGbly7GfefLsTz1AxT2aE+tLiVHLOSUM3y7zd\nFw91MggEXf4w/X2gHlMJV9EWr3j7p9JEcct2gajgM/a31I/uTzQwzp/6CjQdmVWG\nxcln/O21gFQGUH+Nxx9X16SA/keW6+cQrMxjQ2q82Wp42gkf3JB1pulSegzBDP+9\nhO7lNwYYRumDSzNKQAEX\n=DfZ5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T19:24:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/23d844264d5dd315d1959fec1e1535c89e136d6e","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDIzZDg0NDI2NGQ1ZGQzMTVkMTk1OWZlYzFlMTUzNWM4OWUxMzZkNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/87b7b5ead7019d3e077498474231abb726ff2e57","sha":"87b7b5ead7019d3e077498474231abb726ff2e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/87b7b5ead7019d3e077498474231abb726ff2e57"}],"sha":"23d844264d5dd315d1959fec1e1535c89e136d6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/23d844264d5dd315d1959fec1e1535c89e136d6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/87b7b5ead7019d3e077498474231abb726ff2e57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T18:34:56Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T18:34:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(library): dose the broken circuit at climbing pace, and guard the rate (#128)\n\n`broken_circuit_redpoint`''s `work_seconds` was 25 in STRENGTH and POWER against\ninstructions saying \"around twenty-five moves\" — the move count leaked into a\nseconds field, at 1.00 s/move. Ruling 50: 90 s in all three phases, which deletes\nthe 3.6x phase step rather than rescaling it. PERFORMANCE already carried 90;\n`sets` 4/4/3 and the rests are untouched, because a set of a work_seconds-carrying\ncircuit is one attempt at the whole circuit by the library''s own filing convention.\n\nNo source states a move->seconds rate for An Pow, so the conversion is declared at\nthe row as the app''s own rather than dressed as sourced.\n\nThe guard is the load-bearing half: that cell''s `work_seconds` was read by NO guard\nin the repo, so it could have been 90, 120 or 180 with a green suite.\n\n- a move-rate band over every row stating a move count AND carrying `work_seconds`\n  (1.50-4.17 s/move), reading BOTH ends so editing the prose to close a breach\n  fails just as loudly\n- the progression arm''s sampling unit widened from a week PAIR to a DRAWN CELL:\n  `shorter_rest` 15 -> 189 cells, and this row 0 -> 99. Pair arm kept beside it\n- per-(rule, phase) coverage floors, so a phase falling silent turns red instead\n  of going quiet\n\nDisplacement, 72-plan sweep sabotage-checked at 9999 s first: only `power` moves,\n+256.3 min there, ruling 27''s fill absorbs it; pooled -87.1 min / -9 blocks.\n`library_digest` ad0cbbc9 -> cca51ea1, which is the intended provenance signal.\n`GENERATOR_VERSION` unmoved: the library is a third input covered by the digest,\nand every past bump also changed the planner package.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fbfd03c7f532079af2c4d76c8ef633bc6a09ce3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/fbfd03c7f532079af2c4d76c8ef633bc6a09ce3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/87b7b5ead7019d3e077498474231abb726ff2e57","verification":{"payload":"tree fbfd03c7f532079af2c4d76c8ef633bc6a09ce3e\nparent d5cedaac40b2e21a5ae30858f6503665c0198c8e\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788719696 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788719696 +0200\n\nfix(library): dose the broken circuit at climbing pace, and guard the rate (#128)\n\n`broken_circuit_redpoint`''s `work_seconds` was 25 in STRENGTH and POWER against\ninstructions saying \"around twenty-five moves\" — the move count leaked into a\nseconds field, at 1.00 s/move. Ruling 50: 90 s in all three phases, which deletes\nthe 3.6x phase step rather than rescaling it. PERFORMANCE already carried 90;\n`sets` 4/4/3 and the rests are untouched, because a set of a work_seconds-carrying\ncircuit is one attempt at the whole circuit by the library''s own filing convention.\n\nNo source states a move->seconds rate for An Pow, so the conversion is declared at\nthe row as the app''s own rather than dressed as sourced.\n\nThe guard is the load-bearing half: that cell''s `work_seconds` was read by NO guard\nin the repo, so it could have been 90, 120 or 180 with a green suite.\n\n- a move-rate band over every row stating a move count AND carrying `work_seconds`\n  (1.50-4.17 s/move), reading BOTH ends so editing the prose to close a breach\n  fails just as loudly\n- the progression arm''s sampling unit widened from a week PAIR to a DRAWN CELL:\n  `shorter_rest` 15 -> 189 cells, and this row 0 -> 99. Pair arm kept beside it\n- per-(rule, phase) coverage floors, so a phase falling silent turns red instead\n  of going quiet\n\nDisplacement, 72-plan sweep sabotage-checked at 9999 s first: only `power` moves,\n+256.3 min there, ruling 27''s fill absorbs it; pooled -87.1 min / -9 blocks.\n`library_digest` ad0cbbc9 -> cca51ea1, which is the intended provenance signal.\n`GENERATOR_VERSION` unmoved: the library is a third input covered by the digest,\nand every past bump also changed the planner package.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnbJQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqxIQACrpXnnE/uKDaSwYuiLIBQH9\n+9vbz3HoJjw6GfZUAYAq5GUXjYUpQt/PV9Sb686o+DgzOhLEO9rFfqeg3M/LOopC\nL6GQh/uuTN3xB6WPBhs7R5aFYVDR+3XrojAFXnm9ZKu7C57yWxU5A4Ya0bKrIFuZ\nUyk4xdWZNAyA/VhJMj5p+O22Eg5xl66aIjHhggY5cSSd1DoNBZ1ns2B0/2VyaE1z\nck/kggUldybKFsLGg4OycZ8dQSxcWQrHTx+HrynMkb86mZ6nFLRUTWhoRiSGUagT\nrOsB+T1qaCzIKDjJAMFqhCK4BZPRBkXCyd2jWn4m/xINtRNXildMFLmbbh/Mctki\n5qsHjVRbNPP6l9Qw+8VP9H4i8SmRn0sPvFkUzV6GUE/x+E4/3yzwW40bNvgvU3OZ\npmo28LafJw7PHTq1xgNMUbom+bBQGBSFrKfy5ZNErAl7QboZZ4mS9P+A1ZbkXEgz\nKLCi/FemjwhZ5kAJYfHQXTEnNHgZ50HjT1928Ya0puOlZ6djaTf3cM7oZLcG3aY+\nbRY/5kR9yPTQLaS0fc2af7t13q+KCd0cT1DBDAvIPuKTrsii0NmLJJEcSwY7BhKp\nohaFsqz2BfQ8SF8n1xc0zYpigFHYrybxi+uMUCGHYoyMEUDXhwFf7KTOj2yzGbOa\nf3RVuHYl2nzPNLqAqFLB\n=bRiT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T18:34:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/87b7b5ead7019d3e077498474231abb726ff2e57","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDg3YjdiNWVhZDcwMTlkM2UwNzc0OTg0NzQyMzFhYmI3MjZmZjJlNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/d5cedaac40b2e21a5ae30858f6503665c0198c8e","sha":"d5cedaac40b2e21a5ae30858f6503665c0198c8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/d5cedaac40b2e21a5ae30858f6503665c0198c8e"}],"sha":"87b7b5ead7019d3e077498474231abb726ff2e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/87b7b5ead7019d3e077498474231abb726ff2e57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/d5cedaac40b2e21a5ae30858f6503665c0198c8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T17:56:44Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T17:56:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vocabulary): make the power_endurance rest sentence true of its own doses (#127)\n\n`CLIMBING_ASPECTS[\"power_endurance\"]` told the climber their rests are \"no\nlonger than the work\". Measured per (exercise, phase) row, 6 of the 8 rows a\nratio can be read from broke that claim — so the published sentence was false\nof the plan the user is given, and false in the direction that makes the app\nlook harsher than its own sources.\n\nThe sentence now reads \"on rests at least as long as the work\", the exact\ninversion of the false clause.\n\nNot re-authored to §7''s 1-2x Aero Pow band, which is what the register asked\nfor: `bodyweight_anaerobic_circuit` is filed here at 3.00-4.00x and ruling 44\nkeeps that filing, so the aspect''s real spread is 1.00x-4.00x and a 1-2x\nsentence would have moved the mismatch rather than ended it. The floor is the\none edge the whole shipped set supports.\n\nThe guard is the durable half. No guard existed on any `CLIMBING_ASPECTS`\ndescription before this one; the existing POWER_ENDURANCE copy guard is on\n`PHASE_GUIDE`, a different object. Four arms, per row and never pooled:\na verbatim copy pin, the per-row floor, a readable-set non-vacuity arm, and a\ntightness arm so the floor cannot go slack in either direction.\n\nNo behaviour change: plan digest `d47286bf3abe4e17` before and after, over a\n72-plan sweep and 22,979,055 payload bytes. `GENERATOR_VERSION` stays 8.0.0 on\n#125''s precedent; `package.json` 8.12.0 -> 8.13.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"90c3bf2c5cadb7976dc8104a7ee9bddddddafff2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/90c3bf2c5cadb7976dc8104a7ee9bddddddafff2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/d5cedaac40b2e21a5ae30858f6503665c0198c8e","verification":{"payload":"tree 90c3bf2c5cadb7976dc8104a7ee9bddddddafff2\nparent b6cc76950810b42a1e72c5f28b2db73b54a3e3c3\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788717404 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788717404 +0200\n\nfix(vocabulary): make the power_endurance rest sentence true of its own doses (#127)\n\n`CLIMBING_ASPECTS[\"power_endurance\"]` told the climber their rests are \"no\nlonger than the work\". Measured per (exercise, phase) row, 6 of the 8 rows a\nratio can be read from broke that claim — so the published sentence was false\nof the plan the user is given, and false in the direction that makes the app\nlook harsher than its own sources.\n\nThe sentence now reads \"on rests at least as long as the work\", the exact\ninversion of the false clause.\n\nNot re-authored to §7''s 1-2x Aero Pow band, which is what the register asked\nfor: `bodyweight_anaerobic_circuit` is filed here at 3.00-4.00x and ruling 44\nkeeps that filing, so the aspect''s real spread is 1.00x-4.00x and a 1-2x\nsentence would have moved the mismatch rather than ended it. The floor is the\none edge the whole shipped set supports.\n\nThe guard is the durable half. No guard existed on any `CLIMBING_ASPECTS`\ndescription before this one; the existing POWER_ENDURANCE copy guard is on\n`PHASE_GUIDE`, a different object. Four arms, per row and never pooled:\na verbatim copy pin, the per-row floor, a readable-set non-vacuity arm, and a\ntightness arm so the floor cannot go slack in either direction.\n\nNo behaviour change: plan digest `d47286bf3abe4e17` before and after, over a\n72-plan sweep and 22,979,055 payload bytes. `GENERATOR_VERSION` stays 8.0.0 on\n#125''s precedent; `package.json` 8.12.0 -> 8.13.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnalcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgfkQAJEmRh+TrB/WzAQYGAMPmMzI\nzlY0krE/D+vRrPuCOeopoGBfQlBJi3iAPUqwv0y5dt50Gzjr+q71Ed+g4C87Ybym\nBeX72aCUSVaOIMXXimti+YRvj3Humm6s4VKKyaUw0cM1lqUyPPOC2ndYTE4/g0B4\npsjTeJr3nA/reUsiobS3HJEe6jqlGLowDOrWcg8pSditjo8pj8p7XDBsNfqJxa7b\nB3Cz/88pHDIVnaoo24B2NIYMvcNAh6bDHwr0lED+MF0XJtpEIO2F2WYzo+6AH4Xt\nZpPJTNUj9Dk7JEAw2MoQWDczUF7W9nnzolkHX7M8uJkwsdQrOmyt1In3QSvn/Eq/\nXi16evj2n6D6zmW+FsnfntNYgXXFujVkrG97YpbQR+BNYRZsTbImTySXW7UilJzI\nAZmLn43Caup2295O57HtDjzXgUdWA4R+m5aBr1wNpte3x1zFAvLkk6KkK0j3Zua0\nbOug/9vU2RoYIoayyYS0xLqt4U06uz8Q3dgx0pSXC1Nc12DnbJcklVZNMMMbJaq8\n3YXfTNiWkc3XWAxzOUy9cDgdDK7i5Fl4PHteGQHnWEUZW+j7+it9gy+bbJnaQYmw\nvgzFs3CKiysPOxzLzfhRLBan/SAK9icb9eg65GgwvAvTwwpznnOzzdbZOhA/WaTT\nsA4G5+jB+q3POGYYMOJN\n=NtkX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T17:56:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/d5cedaac40b2e21a5ae30858f6503665c0198c8e","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKGQ1Y2VkYWFjNDBiMmUyMWE1YWUzMDg1OGY2NTAzNjY1YzAxOThjOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/b6cc76950810b42a1e72c5f28b2db73b54a3e3c3","sha":"b6cc76950810b42a1e72c5f28b2db73b54a3e3c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/b6cc76950810b42a1e72c5f28b2db73b54a3e3c3"}],"sha":"d5cedaac40b2e21a5ae30858f6503665c0198c8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/d5cedaac40b2e21a5ae30858f6503665c0198c8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/b6cc76950810b42a1e72c5f28b2db73b54a3e3c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T16:01:47Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T16:01:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(planner): progress the dose weekly, habituate a beginner''s BASE, and put easy aerobic work on the wall (#126)\n\nPR 2 of the doctrine-audit tail, at v8.12.0. Rulings 35-38 and 41 in\nct_plan_doctrine.md, plus rulings 46-48 taken while building it. Nothing here\nwas decided in this commit; the amendments record what measured differently.\n\n- #117 (rulings 36, 46): a dose now moves week to week inside a block. The rule\n  is keyed on the (aspect_key, protocol_kind) PAIR, never on aspect_key alone —\n  `power` holds lactic An Pow AND alactic max-effort work, which the sources\n  progress in opposite directions. `power` x `intervals` is the only cell\n  holding both, so that cell alone reads work_seconds, split at 15 s, and a\n  guard pins the cell to its two rows so a third is a decision, not a pass.\n  An Cap scales work AND both rest fields together, so \"longer work\" and \"never\n  less rest\" hold at once and §7''s 2-4x band holds by construction (2.00-3.00x,\n  n=1353). Absence from the rule table IS the not-a-volume-multiplier\n  invariant, and a guard asserts it. No migration: UniqueConstraint\n  (exercise_id, phase) is untouched and week_no reaches the dose seam instead.\n  Dose cells identical across a week-pair 78.9% -> 60.6%; 0 of 1192 cells\n  carrying a sourced rule remain identical.\n  The second, mechanical cause too: `spread % len(pool)` cancelled the week\n  term wherever a pool''s length matched the stride. All four sites now route\n  through one `_pool_index`, `_spread`''s own two terms swapped, no new constant.\n- #118 + guard 5 (ruling 35): BASE draws `hangboard_density_hangs`. The\n  beginner zero was never the gate — `_fill_finger_strength` returns before it,\n  so a beginner''s finger work always arrived through the ordinary supplementary\n  slot, and 115 of 115 swept BASE finger blocks were max hangs or repeaters.\n  So this scales CONTENT, which is what the sources scale: HABITUATION_PROTOCOLS\n  / HABITUATION_PHASES filter that one pool. BASE occurrences 0 -> 70, grade gap\n  1-2 0 -> 28, plans drawing it in BASE 0/60 -> 40/60. The guard reads PER LEVEL\n  because the seven-profile union could never assert one band. Guard 5''s strict\n  `<` gains its written reason at both ends now that the zero is a decision.\n- Ruling 41: `easy_climbing_flush`, the on-wall easy-climbing `endurance` row\n  STRENGTH and POWER had no candidate for, at §7''s 600 s floor exactly. An Cap\n  weeks carrying no aerobic work 39.4% -> 12.5% (strength 61.1% -> 2.8%, power\n  77.5% -> 9.8%), POWER_ENDURANCE out of scope by ruling 24. It PAYS INTO F14\n  rather than deepening it: general_strength +144 blocks in strength, +120 in\n  power, strength share 3.87% -> 6.14% — the opposite of the rejected\n  `_try_supplementary` override, which cost general_strength 57%.\n- F11 (rulings 38, 47): closed as a DECLARED divergence. Ruling 38''s\n  instruction was refused by measurement — seven readings against the whole\n  suite and only the current cap is green; uncapped turns 9 guards red,\n  including ruling 30''s out-training invariant. `_rotated_pool` enters at\n  `spread % len(ring)`, so a 2-session week reads 2 of 16 positions at an\n  offset set by the week number: re-weighting moves presence, not proportion.\n  Delivered instead: one shared `aspect_rank()` across both surfaces, three\n  guards making the flattening a decision, three false docstrings corrected.\n\nProse corrections, none of them catchable by any guard: a comment cited a\n`rest_seconds` column CHECK that does not exist (the floor is ours; the table\nchecks sets, intensity_pct and target_rpe only); \"eleven rows\" was fourteen;\n\"BASE authors two HOLD rows\" — it authors seven, two of them finger; and\n`easy_climbing_flush`''s copy said \"ten unhurried minutes\" while the row is\nexpandable to 1200 s, so it says \"a few\" instead.\n\nTwo things a reviewer should know. Ruling 41''s row re-based #117''s shorter-rest\narm from 57 cells to 15 and `boulders_on_the_two_minute` now contributes none,\nso that arm reads one exercise and stayed green throughout — recovering it is\ntied to F26. And F11''s first measurement round read byte-identical across all\nsix readings because `import server.domain.planner.generate as G` binds the\nfunction re-exported by `planner/__init__.py`, not the module: the harness was\nmeasuring nothing. Sabotage and confirm red before trusting a null result.\n\nEvery guard added or touched was shown red first; the red is in the PR body.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43ac5bfadeeb334fdeea1233ea3cf0b889653f94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/43ac5bfadeeb334fdeea1233ea3cf0b889653f94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/b6cc76950810b42a1e72c5f28b2db73b54a3e3c3","verification":{"payload":"tree 43ac5bfadeeb334fdeea1233ea3cf0b889653f94\nparent 7f5f403c0694390e15d6880ed8defe9df7f1e65b\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788710507 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788710507 +0200\n\nfeat(planner): progress the dose weekly, habituate a beginner''s BASE, and put easy aerobic work on the wall (#126)\n\nPR 2 of the doctrine-audit tail, at v8.12.0. Rulings 35-38 and 41 in\nct_plan_doctrine.md, plus rulings 46-48 taken while building it. Nothing here\nwas decided in this commit; the amendments record what measured differently.\n\n- #117 (rulings 36, 46): a dose now moves week to week inside a block. The rule\n  is keyed on the (aspect_key, protocol_kind) PAIR, never on aspect_key alone —\n  `power` holds lactic An Pow AND alactic max-effort work, which the sources\n  progress in opposite directions. `power` x `intervals` is the only cell\n  holding both, so that cell alone reads work_seconds, split at 15 s, and a\n  guard pins the cell to its two rows so a third is a decision, not a pass.\n  An Cap scales work AND both rest fields together, so \"longer work\" and \"never\n  less rest\" hold at once and §7''s 2-4x band holds by construction (2.00-3.00x,\n  n=1353). Absence from the rule table IS the not-a-volume-multiplier\n  invariant, and a guard asserts it. No migration: UniqueConstraint\n  (exercise_id, phase) is untouched and week_no reaches the dose seam instead.\n  Dose cells identical across a week-pair 78.9% -> 60.6%; 0 of 1192 cells\n  carrying a sourced rule remain identical.\n  The second, mechanical cause too: `spread % len(pool)` cancelled the week\n  term wherever a pool''s length matched the stride. All four sites now route\n  through one `_pool_index`, `_spread`''s own two terms swapped, no new constant.\n- #118 + guard 5 (ruling 35): BASE draws `hangboard_density_hangs`. The\n  beginner zero was never the gate — `_fill_finger_strength` returns before it,\n  so a beginner''s finger work always arrived through the ordinary supplementary\n  slot, and 115 of 115 swept BASE finger blocks were max hangs or repeaters.\n  So this scales CONTENT, which is what the sources scale: HABITUATION_PROTOCOLS\n  / HABITUATION_PHASES filter that one pool. BASE occurrences 0 -> 70, grade gap\n  1-2 0 -> 28, plans drawing it in BASE 0/60 -> 40/60. The guard reads PER LEVEL\n  because the seven-profile union could never assert one band. Guard 5''s strict\n  `<` gains its written reason at both ends now that the zero is a decision.\n- Ruling 41: `easy_climbing_flush`, the on-wall easy-climbing `endurance` row\n  STRENGTH and POWER had no candidate for, at §7''s 600 s floor exactly. An Cap\n  weeks carrying no aerobic work 39.4% -> 12.5% (strength 61.1% -> 2.8%, power\n  77.5% -> 9.8%), POWER_ENDURANCE out of scope by ruling 24. It PAYS INTO F14\n  rather than deepening it: general_strength +144 blocks in strength, +120 in\n  power, strength share 3.87% -> 6.14% — the opposite of the rejected\n  `_try_supplementary` override, which cost general_strength 57%.\n- F11 (rulings 38, 47): closed as a DECLARED divergence. Ruling 38''s\n  instruction was refused by measurement — seven readings against the whole\n  suite and only the current cap is green; uncapped turns 9 guards red,\n  including ruling 30''s out-training invariant. `_rotated_pool` enters at\n  `spread % len(ring)`, so a 2-session week reads 2 of 16 positions at an\n  offset set by the week number: re-weighting moves presence, not proportion.\n  Delivered instead: one shared `aspect_rank()` across both surfaces, three\n  guards making the flattening a decision, three false docstrings corrected.\n\nProse corrections, none of them catchable by any guard: a comment cited a\n`rest_seconds` column CHECK that does not exist (the floor is ours; the table\nchecks sets, intensity_pct and target_rpe only); \"eleven rows\" was fourteen;\n\"BASE authors two HOLD rows\" — it authors seven, two of them finger; and\n`easy_climbing_flush`''s copy said \"ten unhurried minutes\" while the row is\nexpandable to 1200 s, so it says \"a few\" instead.\n\nTwo things a reviewer should know. Ruling 41''s row re-based #117''s shorter-rest\narm from 57 cells to 15 and `boulders_on_the_two_minute` now contributes none,\nso that arm reads one exercise and stayed green throughout — recovering it is\ntied to F26. And F11''s first measurement round read byte-identical across all\nsix readings because `import server.domain.planner.generate as G` binds the\nfunction re-exported by `planner/__init__.py`, not the module: the harness was\nmeasuring nothing. Sabotage and confirm red before trusting a null result.\n\nEvery guard added or touched was shown red first; the red is in the PR body.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnY5rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAo9oQAExZv/BgoyVXCyM2PcMHXwkh\ngwWKX4Nhm9z4vs60U4+obVxcA587Ru6mtv749AFlPfFN/QyRrGKpTNKWjI4b3gca\nmgDyGAjadHph072hLkDdneLPPhX1W7esKT8/aXpxOJqcUTRNT/6DIqC9gt68KMSh\n5pn1VhqzNGb7CL9wojtmgGB0I+YwX9veRZbSLu3m44qQp+znHkRO9abIlt9NqA+7\nAGXn99rAfnf8Tbf59Fqbm7CLnV5u5q+eYoDMLNOOGEe9oHX7KsMNzrLi2QCh0T8f\nO3YhaR6Z9Rs82i/Vnw7PWq8GcnQ40ZqB7PViwW8jI94RPsQIwWAyP5Terz2aKHKj\nOwgvAruwcZ7QeHHU/uwQFHmKKluZSAc4KCnU3/TgPKWbedWOnB6E+7GmuoMWW+0q\npq9GBo7Hu3AMj4d1ATyMq39/TtYFPpKWK1O0RkvDGNxMfWCLkzlvlq9dt1aWGabu\nlMEUxDyTJCwB2Sqqi11oy6AC0hfrt+1RflstHGWIzPqbH3R6E+dINXenN93hVmdr\nYvWT26A5jOZCB0QhQIxksrZD3MRMJgxomQeWtjlqR86FBcdhkRTJOZLGQsKdfS9j\nOZJaErHmu7M2oY8naD5irK2ZVdaK1isY6TCVIKy6d2n1BP0BG7DHOygY0EHtytSr\naHx2WSyw2t1h4+sx3oYu\n=AfEt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T16:01:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/b6cc76950810b42a1e72c5f28b2db73b54a3e3c3","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKGI2Y2M3Njk1MDgxMGI0MmExZTcyYzVmMjhiMmRiNzNiNTRhM2UzYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/7f5f403c0694390e15d6880ed8defe9df7f1e65b","sha":"7f5f403c0694390e15d6880ed8defe9df7f1e65b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/7f5f403c0694390e15d6880ed8defe9df7f1e65b"}],"sha":"b6cc76950810b42a1e72c5f28b2db73b54a3e3c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/b6cc76950810b42a1e72c5f28b2db73b54a3e3c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/7f5f403c0694390e15d6880ed8defe9df7f1e65b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:46:00Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:46:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"guard(library): check every §7 dose against its band, and declare four divergences (#125)\n\nThe dose and filing half of the doctrine-audit tail, at v8.11.0. Rulings 39 and\n42-45 in ct_plan_doctrine.md; nothing here was decided in this commit.\n\n- F19 (ruling 39): every `endurance` row above RPE 6 comes down to 6 — four\n  exercises, seven (exercise, phase) rows, three of them in PERFORMANCE. An\n  aspect-wide RPE ceiling guard replaces the old exemption, which cited F19 by\n  name while letting it stand. `lead_endurance_pyramid`''s instructions are\n  reworded because our own re-dose is what made \"near your onsight level\" false.\n- F17: `machine_anaerobic_intervals`/POWER_ENDURANCE goes 1.50x -> 2.0x, matching\n  its own DELOAD row and §7''s floor. Measured drawn 0 times, and the plan digest\n  is byte-identical, as expected. `auto_belay_interval_laps` is re-filed\n  anaerobic_capacity -> power_endurance: 90 s of work is Aero Pow by dose.\n- The §7 rest:work guard, keyed on the (aspect, protocol_kind) PAIR — the aspect\n  names the attribute, the kind decides scope. 136 rows in the four §7 aspects,\n  60 carry work_seconds, 6 are OPEN_CLIMBING_KEYS, 24 are read by a band. A\n  within-set-only reading of the rest scores 0 of 24, so the non-vacuity arm\n  pins the 24. No exemption register: every breach is ruled instead.\n- Four declared divergences at the rows they describe: F18 keeps `power` because\n  the honest target is structurally unprescribable; F25 keeps `power_endurance`\n  because the row is the gearless taper''s aerobic power; `long_boulder_link_ups`\n  keeps 300 s because raising it makes another quality out-train the block it is\n  named after; F14''s strength share is 3.6-6.0% against Dylan''s 15-20%, mostly a\n  consequence of ruling 27''s length fill rather than an authoring omission.\n- #100: `vocabulary.plan_goal` stays and records why — it is the only\n  user-facing carrier of ruling 31''s declared divergence.\n- Prose corrections: guard 5''s re-attribution gains its date in both copies, and\n  test_planner_library_reach''s comments go from 100 exercises to 105, ceilings\n  96/87 to 101/92, with all seven measured shares re-measured. The distinct-share\n  floor keeps 63 deliberately; its slack is recorded, not spent.\n\nEvery guard added or touched was shown red first; the red is in the PR body.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"59c1f34dc117c85b5540fb3add62c10779881659","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/59c1f34dc117c85b5540fb3add62c10779881659"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/7f5f403c0694390e15d6880ed8defe9df7f1e65b","verification":{"payload":"tree 59c1f34dc117c85b5540fb3add62c10779881659\nparent 9f0db1428622c463d878cf46f719432d7d1f50e2\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788698760 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788698760 +0200\n\nguard(library): check every §7 dose against its band, and declare four divergences (#125)\n\nThe dose and filing half of the doctrine-audit tail, at v8.11.0. Rulings 39 and\n42-45 in ct_plan_doctrine.md; nothing here was decided in this commit.\n\n- F19 (ruling 39): every `endurance` row above RPE 6 comes down to 6 — four\n  exercises, seven (exercise, phase) rows, three of them in PERFORMANCE. An\n  aspect-wide RPE ceiling guard replaces the old exemption, which cited F19 by\n  name while letting it stand. `lead_endurance_pyramid`''s instructions are\n  reworded because our own re-dose is what made \"near your onsight level\" false.\n- F17: `machine_anaerobic_intervals`/POWER_ENDURANCE goes 1.50x -> 2.0x, matching\n  its own DELOAD row and §7''s floor. Measured drawn 0 times, and the plan digest\n  is byte-identical, as expected. `auto_belay_interval_laps` is re-filed\n  anaerobic_capacity -> power_endurance: 90 s of work is Aero Pow by dose.\n- The §7 rest:work guard, keyed on the (aspect, protocol_kind) PAIR — the aspect\n  names the attribute, the kind decides scope. 136 rows in the four §7 aspects,\n  60 carry work_seconds, 6 are OPEN_CLIMBING_KEYS, 24 are read by a band. A\n  within-set-only reading of the rest scores 0 of 24, so the non-vacuity arm\n  pins the 24. No exemption register: every breach is ruled instead.\n- Four declared divergences at the rows they describe: F18 keeps `power` because\n  the honest target is structurally unprescribable; F25 keeps `power_endurance`\n  because the row is the gearless taper''s aerobic power; `long_boulder_link_ups`\n  keeps 300 s because raising it makes another quality out-train the block it is\n  named after; F14''s strength share is 3.6-6.0% against Dylan''s 15-20%, mostly a\n  consequence of ruling 27''s length fill rather than an authoring omission.\n- #100: `vocabulary.plan_goal` stays and records why — it is the only\n  user-facing carrier of ruling 31''s declared divergence.\n- Prose corrections: guard 5''s re-attribution gains its date in both copies, and\n  test_planner_library_reach''s comments go from 100 exercises to 105, ceilings\n  96/87 to 101/92, with all seven measured shares re-measured. The distinct-share\n  floor keeps 63 deliberately; its slack is recorded, not spent.\n\nEvery guard added or touched was shown red first; the red is in the PR body.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnWCICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd7AQAGcz57WarRRlhmpoZzpoEM6O\noX85KnHoHj+MRQ6LYQgnOsWtgW81c3IHaxihnHugXrfuRQE1YIMmyZ9wh/yZ6EG5\nLFuSSefpvLKTMl3RlKFKOFgSR+0jyO5S9Z3k8OkEWyyWT3D4YMpyNSAT7W6hX9Fd\nw1QamXlOVsYG/Nmd9hpBEFQXZGl0d71BmTa7mL4JAsL9c2BIcX6tTFD78HTxRQzo\naEXthyxSIGI9Y63IJpPHMJnUGQ/80ebrZtm5PiXANZP9q4BlWzgTl36cY3kezp6h\nONNMVjTWjcX4o1qLTUFrWGS/W7c0abegbXr+ULqK75m+4uxxpdC+liEGZjYs6Z92\nKkcQ1UQFmH/IwkGv+ubd2vIkUeupKjVU72SYxlJWSK4cga35f8oQ40eMEKs1Oufg\nMuYYqTJOz+bJPkKRYpA6HDoQe8s8pHrI3wAijNrw36OTj/CQxmugdB9umcovPnqF\nldNzSjA+pkq6WkCjPFQJEY5Ie2YAIR8l1skV04f2ekJ17Lp3AsFlmE9PnL6YJ+oz\njisrVcV51D68Ft619ZKbfO3WCUMhNLHxXQTWHcnLoZsUOS7zYFL8pIp//mopz/eR\nj5IzfG+HbElXZzjLjf+FUq4rZhVw/HUx2Dj5dUpMCmTF1XLXwblmY4WTUEQrN5z1\nYgr9s8TxL7TyYaCnxJcc\n=qYIg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T12:46:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/7f5f403c0694390e15d6880ed8defe9df7f1e65b","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDdmNWY0MDNjMDY5NDM5MGUxNWQ2ODgwZWQ4ZGVmZTlkZjdmMWU2NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/9f0db1428622c463d878cf46f719432d7d1f50e2","sha":"9f0db1428622c463d878cf46f719432d7d1f50e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/9f0db1428622c463d878cf46f719432d7d1f50e2"}],"sha":"7f5f403c0694390e15d6880ed8defe9df7f1e65b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/7f5f403c0694390e15d6880ed8defe9df7f1e65b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/9f0db1428622c463d878cf46f719432d7d1f50e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:49:53Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:49:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Cap hard energy-system days, give every session its level''s length, and clear the findings inbox (#124)\n\n* feat(planner): cap hard energy-system days and An Cap sessions a week\n\nRuling 18''s two WEEKLY FREQUENCY ceilings, read off the week''s drafts rather\nthan off a counter so they cannot drift out of step with what the week holds.\n`climbing.py` gains `ENERGY_SYSTEM_ASPECTS` (An Cap + An Pow + Aero Pow, and\ndeliberately NOT `INTENSITY_TIERS`'' top tier, which holds `power` beside\n`finger_strength` and `general_strength` — §4.2 runs four strength sessions a\nweek alongside ~3 hard energy days), `HARD_ENERGY_DAYS_PER_WEEK = 3` with the\nTAPER exempt by authored decision, `ANAEROBIC_SESSIONS_PER_WEEK` per phase off\n§4.2''s worked example, and `week_ceiling_governs` as the single choke point the\ngenerator''s predicate and `selection.py`''s import-time floor both read.\n\n`generate.py::_week_ceiling_allows` binds THREE passes, not the two the plan\nnamed: the rotated wall ring in `_fill_climbing`, `_length_pick`''s top-up and\nthe supplementary fill. Removing the gate from any one of them goes red. A day\nwhose hard pick is refused spends `BLOCKS_PER_SESSION` wall blocks instead of\nthe band''s budget — ruling 9 removes hard WORK, ruling 4 forbids removing\nCLIMBING.\n\nMeasured over 480 weeks (6 climbers x sessions {2,3,5,7}, gap 3, full\nvocabulary):\n\n  - An Cap weeks breaching THEIR OWN PHASE''s ceiling: 206 -> 0\n  - weeks with >=3 An Cap sessions:                    136 -> 0\n  - weeks over 3 hard energy days outside TAPER:       177 -> 0\n  - 5-day climbers with 4 or 5 hard days:  80 of 120 -> 6 of 120, all TAPER\n\nAlso in this story, because the ceilings are what made them true or possible:\n\n  - Ruling 20 moves `endurance` to index 8 in `ASPECT_EMPHASIS[POWER_ENDURANCE]`\n    and `power` to 7. Endurance out-trains power endurance on 4 of 24 profiles\n    at index 7 and 2 of 24 at index 8. Ruling 13''s rejection reason for 8 was\n    stale arithmetic from before the ceilings existed.\n  - Ruling 21''s slot-1 yield, `WEAKNESS_YIELDS_SLOT_ONE_EVERY = 3`. Rotating a\n    yielded turn over the whole `_secondary_pool` does not work at any N (8 of\n    24 profiles still starved at N=2, 13 of 24 at N=3), because a base block is\n    three weeks and the pool is nine aspects long. It rotates over\n    `_no_other_route` instead — not wall-led in this phase, not a\n    `SUPPORT_ASPECTS` member — which is `general_strength`''s only route into a\n    plan. Base-block general strength: 1 of 24 profiles -> 24 of 24 at both\n    weakness values. Cost: plan-wide weakness multiplier 1.26x-3.42x ->\n    1.14x-2.67x.\n  - Ruling 32 opens the finger gate by having `_fill_finger_strength` READ\n    `_block_ceiling` instead of restating `BLOCKS_PER_SESSION`. All 28 finger\n    rows green, `_ACCEPTED_FINGER_GAPS` stays `()` as a measurement. Price over\n    1176 weeks: 796 -> 800 hangboard blocks, 523 -> 525 weeks holding one.\n    The ruling''s prescribed THIRD condition on `_block_ceiling` measured\n    byte-identical over those weeks and was NOT shipped; the docstring records\n    the attempt so it is not re-tried.\n\nGuards: four new in `test_planner_climbing_floor.py` (both ceilings per week per\nclimber with anti-vacuity arms, and two declared-weakness arms), the base-copy\nguard moved from pooled to per climber over a 72-plan weakness sweep, and\n`_validate_frequency_ceilings` / `_validate_aspect_emphasis`'' survivor floor at\nimport. `GENERATOR_VERSION` 6.0.0 -> 7.0.0, bumped once for the whole PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(planner): give every session its level''s length as a FLOOR\n\nRulings 25, 26, 27, 28 and 31. `SESSION_MINUTES_TARGET` is 90 / 120 / 150 min\nby LEVEL — the high end of Horst''s published per-session bands and above\nLattice''s measured medians, so KILIAN''S numbers and never \"the sources''\", and\nbanded by level rather than by weekly frequency because no source scales length\ninversely with frequency and Lattice argues the opposite. Per Kilian''s\ncorrection the marks are MINIMA: a short session takes ONE block of plain\nclimbing sized to the gap and never shorter than `LENGTH_FILL_MINUTES = 30`,\nplaced by `_fill_session_length`, which runs LAST so it can never take a slot a\nfloor is owed. Overshoot is correct, not a miss.\n\nMeasured, loading weeks, 6 climbers x sessions {2,3,5,7}, gap 3:\n\n  level         before   mean now   worst session   floor\n  beginner       55.6      96.0         90.0          90\n  intermediate   56.4     120.5        120.0         120\n  advanced       56.1     150.0        150.0         150\n\n0 of 1530 sessions short of their floor. Ruling 26 takes the warm-up 15 -> 20\nmin flat; its share of a session falls 27.0% -> 20.8 / 16.6 / 13.3% by level,\ni.e. inside the ruling''s own 13-22% estimate, and the round-3 correction\nclaiming the divergence was wider is withdrawn (it measured sessions that had\nnot yet reached the floor). Still outside Dylan''s 5-10% and still declared.\n\nNeither currency ruling 27 forbade was needed: `MAX_BLOCKS_PER_SESSION` stays 5\nand no library row was re-dosed. The largest single win was NOT the fill but\nkeeping ruling 3''s floor and ruling 25''s length APART — `_window_floor` is\nruling 3''s and `_session_floor` is ruling 25''s, and only the fill reads the\nlatter. Wiring the length into the discretionary passes instead put every band\n30 points over target, left `_fill_finger_strength` no session with a free slot,\nmade twelve off-the-wall library rows unreachable and cost 174 reds;\nre-pointing `_block_ceiling`, `_share_allows` and `_supplementary_rounds` back\nto `_window_floor` repaired the 12 rows, the 5 taper reds and 25 of the 26 that\nround opened. `session_window_across` replaces the leading block''s window, so a\n15-minute limit-boulder block behind a max hang no longer takes MAX_HANG''s\n20-minute floor; `_session_ceiling` adds the level target, without which no\nadvanced session could pass 45 minutes. `_leading_kind` is deleted — its\ndocstring claimed to name the kind that SETS THE WINDOW, which had become false.\n\nRuling 31: the floors hold at EVERY session count, so seven available days buy\nseven whole sessions. Loading-week hours at 2 / 3 / 5 / 7 days: beginner 3.2 /\n4.9 / 8.0 / 11.1 h, intermediate 4.0 / 6.0 / 10.0 / 14.0, advanced 5.0 / 7.5 /\n12.5 / 17.5 — 2-4x above every band Lattice measured. A DECLARED divergence,\nKilian''s and not the sources'', carried in `climbing.py`''s comment and in\n`PLAN_GOAL`''s copy, with capping the week and dividing by the days recorded as\nconsidered and REFUSED.\n\nRuling 17 holds by construction rather than by accident: the length goes through\n`session_floor_pct`, so an unload session owes half of what a loading one does.\nRuling 4''s `_ACCEPTED_INVERSIONS` empties to `()` — the fill repaired all seven\nrows the register ever held, and ruling 22''s reverse arm is what deletes them.\n\nRuling 28 makes `CLIMBING_TARGET_PCT`''s guard FLOOR-ONLY and named as such. The\nceiling was NOT re-based: at the honest maximum of 94/94/92 the `_wall_pref`\nsabotage stayed GREEN on 36 of 36 beginner rows, so ruling 14''s condition fails\nand a ceiling the sabotage passes catches nothing. 108 open reds are gone. The\nreplacement is two arms — `_wall_pref`''s three regimes asserted directly off a\nhand-built `_Draft`, because the promise is about candidate ORDER and no\nfinished plan records it, plus a behavioural arm that every ADVANCED loading\nsession keeps something off the wall: honest 0 of 1632, sabotaged 14. Both go\nred under `return \"first\"` while the floor-only band stays green on all 108\nrows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(planner): author the open-climbing filler family and re-point the copy\n\nRulings 23, 29 and 30, plus ruling 31''s copy half and ruling 24''s revocation.\n\nRuling 23 adds `long_boulder_link_ups`, the first aerobic row a BOULDERER can\nbe given in a power-endurance block: all four `endurance` rows prescribable\nthere are `discipline=sport`, so boulder profiles took ZERO aerobic minutes at\nevery session count. 12 of 12 boulder profiles -> 0 of 12 with none. Dosed\nsustained and moderate at RPE 6, never to failure, because a hard row filed\nunder `endurance` would recreate F19.\n\nRulings 29 and 30 are implemented as a FAMILY of four rows, `OPEN_CLIMBING_KEYS`,\nand not the single row the ruling guessed at. The measured reason: FIVE of seven\nphases lead on a quality ruling 9''s weekly ceilings govern, so a filler keyed to\nthe block''s lead aspect is REFUSED on every day the ~3-hard-days ceiling has\nmade easy — and a filter has no fallback, so the session falls short of ruling\n25''s length. The family is ordered by the phase''s own `ASPECT_EMPHASIS` and the\nfirst row the ceilings allow wins, so the fill is credited to the block''s own\nquality on every hard day and walks to a non-governed row only on the easy ones.\nMeasured over ~9800 sessions: 0 off-lead fills on a hard day, 0 sessions with\ntwo fills. `_fill_rank`, `wall_fill_aspects` and the repeat fallback are\nDELETED, and the 386 `straight_sets` fill blocks are 0 of 1984 — filling time\nwith non-climbing was the opposite of ruling 27''s intent. \"Climb for fun is also\ntraining\" is Kilian''s doctrine and is attributed to him in `exercises.py`.\n\nRuling 31 closes the five-round POWER_ENDURANCE copy red by RE-AUTHORING the\nblock''s copy rather than the generator, and the whole clause moved rather than\nthe half that prompted it. Four claims were false, each only at particular\nsession counts: \"never enough to out-train the quality the block is named after\"\n(7 days, 6A boulder, 27.0% aerobic vs 23.0% power endurance), \"enough to let the\nnext hard session happen two days later\" (1 day on 6 of 6 profiles, 2 days on 2\nof 6, 3 days on 3 of 6), \"kept to a small share\" (0.0% at one day, 27.0% at\nseven), and the implicit promise that power endurance leads its own block —\n`technique` is the largest quality on 12 of 12 profiles at six and seven days,\n37.5-50.8% against power endurance''s 23.0-34.2%. 53-90% of those technique\nminutes are this commit''s filler, which is what earns the copy the words\nORDINARY CLIMBING. The retired guard is replaced by two, over session counts\n1-7, both shown red under sabotage.\n\nRuling 24 is REVOKED — no aerobic floor — and the copy that replaces it was\nFALSE at a granularity nothing was reading. The sentence said that from four\ndays up EVERY WEEK carries some aerobic work: per profile true on 18 of 18 and\ngreen, per WEEK 12 of those same 72 weeks hold none, all in week 14 or 15. No\nday boundary repairs it and no dose length does either. Re-authored to \"you\nalways get some of it, though not always in every week\", and the guard is three\narms, one per clause — arm 1 per CLIMBER because \"you\" is one climber, arms 2\nand 3 per WEEK — each shown red, including under the pooled read it replaced.\nA comment beside `FINGER_SESSIONS_PER_WEEK` records that the floor was declined\non the merits, because with no mechanism behind it the copy IS the mechanism.\n\nAlso here:\n\n  - `_length_pick`''s body restructure. The `band is None` branch that draws the\n    filler family and the `offered()` helper carrying the ceiling gate and the\n    band-top filter are one indivisible rewrite sharing a `prescribable(...)`\n    call, so it lands with the family it draws from rather than split across\n    the two earlier commits.\n  - `selection.py::ordinary` subtracts the family from every pool the ordinary\n    passes draw from, so \"climb for X minutes, your choice\" can only ever\n    arrive as the length fill and never as a session''s prescribed work.\n    `_validate_open_climbing_fill` proves at import that every phase''s filler\n    order ends in a row no ceiling governs.\n  - `tests/comment_budget_allowlist.toml`: the PR''s hand-written rows, no\n    `BASELINE` reasons, so `BASELINE_RATCHET` is untouched.\n  - `CLAUDE.md`: the findings-inbox pass this PR owed. Twelve dated inbox lines\n    routed to exactly one destination each — three kept as TRIPWIRES with `->`\n    pointers (no dose length closes the sport aerobic gap; the finger gate that\n    mattered was block count, not the climbing floor; measure the counterfactual\n    before shipping a prescribed mechanism), the rest deleted because a guard\n    now asserts them or archived for their reasoning. The archive section lives\n    at `../.archive/climb-trainer-CLAUDE-2026-09-03.md`, outside this repo, so\n    it is not part of this commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* guard: prove the quality gate''s ORDER, and empty the findings inbox\n\nEvery dated line in `CLAUDE.md`''s findings inbox routed to exactly one\ndestination, plus two authored claims that were false.\n\n`tests/test_claude_md_claims.py` — the `## Quality gate` chain arm tested each\ndocumented step with `step in script_value`, i.e. substring membership. It caught\na RENAMED step and nothing else: a reordered chain passed, and a documented\n`ruff format` passed against a script running `ruff format --check`. Its own\ndocstring claimed the documented order is the only place the gate''s order exists,\nso the arm did not prove the thing it existed for. It now splits the script on\n`&&` as well and walks forward from the last match, so index-monotonic order is\nrequired, and it compares at TOKEN level after stripping the runner prefix —\nliteral equality is impossible because every documented step is an abbreviation\n(`check:web` for `npm run check:web`, `ruff check` for `uv run ruff check .`).\nShown RED twice before green: swapping `build` and `test` in the documented\n`check:web` chain, and dropping `--check` from the documented `ruff format` step,\nwhich is the exact case the old arm passed. `.`/`-q` are still tolerated as\nbehaviour-free, which is the one difference the arm does not read.\n\n`tests/test_planner_selection.py` — the note on\n`test_aspect_emphasis_agrees_with_the_library_in_both_directions` said its first\nloop \"is the thing that fails in a test run\". It cannot be: `conftest.py` imports\n`server.app`, which reaches `selection.py`''s import-time validator at module\nscope, so an emphasis/library disagreement aborts COLLECTION and that assertion\ncan never be the red. Relabelled as unreachable by construction and kept only to\nname the cell, per the audit''s \"label it, don''t delete it\". Arm 2 untouched.\n\n`climbing.py` and `tests/test_planner_climbing_floor.py` — both credited\n`FINGER_SESSIONS_PER_WEEK[BEGINNER] = 0` to \"the sources want 6-12 months of\nconsistent climbing first\". That claim is in NEITHER extracted source; the\nconstant stays 0 and the attribution moves to Kilian, in both copies, because\nfixing one was a half-fix. No date invented — there is no recorded one. Note the\nsources are not silent on beginners: both say beginners habituate before they\nload hard, and Dylan programmes an explicit habituation protocol, so they scale\nhangboard CONTENT by level while never scaling session FREQUENCY by it. The\nmerits of the zero stay open as guard 5 and #118, which must be taken together.\n\n`CLAUDE.md` — the inbox is now EMPTY. The `_spread` mod-7 aliasing line moved to\n`issuesplan.md` as a named cause of #117 (it is a cause, not a prohibition, so it\ndoes not qualify as a tripwire). The §3.4 tier-ordering line is DELETED: it said\n`PHASE_GUIDE[POWER_ENDURANCE]` may not be upgraded to a lead claim until the\nweekly frequency ceilings land, and they landed — `d7c4235` then re-authored that\ncopy honestly rather than upgrading it. The substring-membership line is closed\nby the guard above.\n\nTripwire budget, per this file''s own \"to add a line here, archive one\":\n\n  + session length must never scale INVERSELY with training frequency\n  - the warm-up dose-in-moves finding, ARCHIVED instead of added\n  - the SQLite / real-Postgres line, ARCHIVED\n\nThe warm-up finding was routed to a tripwire and then re-routed, deliberately:\nunder the four-way rule it is reasoning about a ruling already taken, not a\nprohibition, and a tripwire would have been the only place in the repo its two\ncitations existed while its `→` pointed at a heading that did not hold them. It\nnow lives under `### Ruling 26''s warm-up share` in the archive (append-only,\ndiff-verified as a pure insertion). The SQLite line went because both halves are\nalready authored in `tests/conftest.py`''s module docstring, in bold with their\nreasoning, in the exact file anyone adding SQLite would be editing. The other\nthree archive candidates were REFUSED: each would have lost a prohibition whose\nonly other home is a self-attested PR-template checkbox or nothing at all.\n\nTwo prose fixes the above exposed, neither covered by any guard:\n\n  - `.github/workflows/ci.yml` cited `CLAUDE.md, \"SQLite is disqualified for\n    tests\"`, a string that existed only in the line this commit deletes. Now\n    points at `tests/conftest.py`''s module docstring, the live canonical home.\n    Nothing checks comment-to-CLAUDE.md citations, so this was found by hand.\n  - `conftest.py`''s remedy told the reader `npm run check:server` \"clears\n    DATABASE_URL\". It does not: it substitutes `CT_TEST_DATABASE_URL`, which is\n    empty only when that variable is unset. Re-worded to say what it does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(release): v8.10.0 — the weekly ceilings, session length and the filler family\n\nThe three commits before this one carried no bump: `package.json` still read\n8.9.0 and no `8.10.0` string existed anywhere in the repo, while\n`issuesplan.md`''s state line already asserted \"v8.10.0 on dev\" and every backlog\nentry named that version. A register that STATES the version rather than reading\nit will confirm a bump that never happened — the register is fixed in the same\npass, and the check is `package.json`, never the register.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"deed17a36ebcfc7d103166e317982adb7494eab9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/deed17a36ebcfc7d103166e317982adb7494eab9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/9f0db1428622c463d878cf46f719432d7d1f50e2","verification":{"payload":"tree deed17a36ebcfc7d103166e317982adb7494eab9\nparent 57d6919966000593951d0d4226809cfda80c1ea2\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788688193 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788688193 +0200\n\nCap hard energy-system days, give every session its level''s length, and clear the findings inbox (#124)\n\n* feat(planner): cap hard energy-system days and An Cap sessions a week\n\nRuling 18''s two WEEKLY FREQUENCY ceilings, read off the week''s drafts rather\nthan off a counter so they cannot drift out of step with what the week holds.\n`climbing.py` gains `ENERGY_SYSTEM_ASPECTS` (An Cap + An Pow + Aero Pow, and\ndeliberately NOT `INTENSITY_TIERS`'' top tier, which holds `power` beside\n`finger_strength` and `general_strength` — §4.2 runs four strength sessions a\nweek alongside ~3 hard energy days), `HARD_ENERGY_DAYS_PER_WEEK = 3` with the\nTAPER exempt by authored decision, `ANAEROBIC_SESSIONS_PER_WEEK` per phase off\n§4.2''s worked example, and `week_ceiling_governs` as the single choke point the\ngenerator''s predicate and `selection.py`''s import-time floor both read.\n\n`generate.py::_week_ceiling_allows` binds THREE passes, not the two the plan\nnamed: the rotated wall ring in `_fill_climbing`, `_length_pick`''s top-up and\nthe supplementary fill. Removing the gate from any one of them goes red. A day\nwhose hard pick is refused spends `BLOCKS_PER_SESSION` wall blocks instead of\nthe band''s budget — ruling 9 removes hard WORK, ruling 4 forbids removing\nCLIMBING.\n\nMeasured over 480 weeks (6 climbers x sessions {2,3,5,7}, gap 3, full\nvocabulary):\n\n  - An Cap weeks breaching THEIR OWN PHASE''s ceiling: 206 -> 0\n  - weeks with >=3 An Cap sessions:                    136 -> 0\n  - weeks over 3 hard energy days outside TAPER:       177 -> 0\n  - 5-day climbers with 4 or 5 hard days:  80 of 120 -> 6 of 120, all TAPER\n\nAlso in this story, because the ceilings are what made them true or possible:\n\n  - Ruling 20 moves `endurance` to index 8 in `ASPECT_EMPHASIS[POWER_ENDURANCE]`\n    and `power` to 7. Endurance out-trains power endurance on 4 of 24 profiles\n    at index 7 and 2 of 24 at index 8. Ruling 13''s rejection reason for 8 was\n    stale arithmetic from before the ceilings existed.\n  - Ruling 21''s slot-1 yield, `WEAKNESS_YIELDS_SLOT_ONE_EVERY = 3`. Rotating a\n    yielded turn over the whole `_secondary_pool` does not work at any N (8 of\n    24 profiles still starved at N=2, 13 of 24 at N=3), because a base block is\n    three weeks and the pool is nine aspects long. It rotates over\n    `_no_other_route` instead — not wall-led in this phase, not a\n    `SUPPORT_ASPECTS` member — which is `general_strength`''s only route into a\n    plan. Base-block general strength: 1 of 24 profiles -> 24 of 24 at both\n    weakness values. Cost: plan-wide weakness multiplier 1.26x-3.42x ->\n    1.14x-2.67x.\n  - Ruling 32 opens the finger gate by having `_fill_finger_strength` READ\n    `_block_ceiling` instead of restating `BLOCKS_PER_SESSION`. All 28 finger\n    rows green, `_ACCEPTED_FINGER_GAPS` stays `()` as a measurement. Price over\n    1176 weeks: 796 -> 800 hangboard blocks, 523 -> 525 weeks holding one.\n    The ruling''s prescribed THIRD condition on `_block_ceiling` measured\n    byte-identical over those weeks and was NOT shipped; the docstring records\n    the attempt so it is not re-tried.\n\nGuards: four new in `test_planner_climbing_floor.py` (both ceilings per week per\nclimber with anti-vacuity arms, and two declared-weakness arms), the base-copy\nguard moved from pooled to per climber over a 72-plan weakness sweep, and\n`_validate_frequency_ceilings` / `_validate_aspect_emphasis`'' survivor floor at\nimport. `GENERATOR_VERSION` 6.0.0 -> 7.0.0, bumped once for the whole PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(planner): give every session its level''s length as a FLOOR\n\nRulings 25, 26, 27, 28 and 31. `SESSION_MINUTES_TARGET` is 90 / 120 / 150 min\nby LEVEL — the high end of Horst''s published per-session bands and above\nLattice''s measured medians, so KILIAN''S numbers and never \"the sources''\", and\nbanded by level rather than by weekly frequency because no source scales length\ninversely with frequency and Lattice argues the opposite. Per Kilian''s\ncorrection the marks are MINIMA: a short session takes ONE block of plain\nclimbing sized to the gap and never shorter than `LENGTH_FILL_MINUTES = 30`,\nplaced by `_fill_session_length`, which runs LAST so it can never take a slot a\nfloor is owed. Overshoot is correct, not a miss.\n\nMeasured, loading weeks, 6 climbers x sessions {2,3,5,7}, gap 3:\n\n  level         before   mean now   worst session   floor\n  beginner       55.6      96.0         90.0          90\n  intermediate   56.4     120.5        120.0         120\n  advanced       56.1     150.0        150.0         150\n\n0 of 1530 sessions short of their floor. Ruling 26 takes the warm-up 15 -> 20\nmin flat; its share of a session falls 27.0% -> 20.8 / 16.6 / 13.3% by level,\ni.e. inside the ruling''s own 13-22% estimate, and the round-3 correction\nclaiming the divergence was wider is withdrawn (it measured sessions that had\nnot yet reached the floor). Still outside Dylan''s 5-10% and still declared.\n\nNeither currency ruling 27 forbade was needed: `MAX_BLOCKS_PER_SESSION` stays 5\nand no library row was re-dosed. The largest single win was NOT the fill but\nkeeping ruling 3''s floor and ruling 25''s length APART — `_window_floor` is\nruling 3''s and `_session_floor` is ruling 25''s, and only the fill reads the\nlatter. Wiring the length into the discretionary passes instead put every band\n30 points over target, left `_fill_finger_strength` no session with a free slot,\nmade twelve off-the-wall library rows unreachable and cost 174 reds;\nre-pointing `_block_ceiling`, `_share_allows` and `_supplementary_rounds` back\nto `_window_floor` repaired the 12 rows, the 5 taper reds and 25 of the 26 that\nround opened. `session_window_across` replaces the leading block''s window, so a\n15-minute limit-boulder block behind a max hang no longer takes MAX_HANG''s\n20-minute floor; `_session_ceiling` adds the level target, without which no\nadvanced session could pass 45 minutes. `_leading_kind` is deleted — its\ndocstring claimed to name the kind that SETS THE WINDOW, which had become false.\n\nRuling 31: the floors hold at EVERY session count, so seven available days buy\nseven whole sessions. Loading-week hours at 2 / 3 / 5 / 7 days: beginner 3.2 /\n4.9 / 8.0 / 11.1 h, intermediate 4.0 / 6.0 / 10.0 / 14.0, advanced 5.0 / 7.5 /\n12.5 / 17.5 — 2-4x above every band Lattice measured. A DECLARED divergence,\nKilian''s and not the sources'', carried in `climbing.py`''s comment and in\n`PLAN_GOAL`''s copy, with capping the week and dividing by the days recorded as\nconsidered and REFUSED.\n\nRuling 17 holds by construction rather than by accident: the length goes through\n`session_floor_pct`, so an unload session owes half of what a loading one does.\nRuling 4''s `_ACCEPTED_INVERSIONS` empties to `()` — the fill repaired all seven\nrows the register ever held, and ruling 22''s reverse arm is what deletes them.\n\nRuling 28 makes `CLIMBING_TARGET_PCT`''s guard FLOOR-ONLY and named as such. The\nceiling was NOT re-based: at the honest maximum of 94/94/92 the `_wall_pref`\nsabotage stayed GREEN on 36 of 36 beginner rows, so ruling 14''s condition fails\nand a ceiling the sabotage passes catches nothing. 108 open reds are gone. The\nreplacement is two arms — `_wall_pref`''s three regimes asserted directly off a\nhand-built `_Draft`, because the promise is about candidate ORDER and no\nfinished plan records it, plus a behavioural arm that every ADVANCED loading\nsession keeps something off the wall: honest 0 of 1632, sabotaged 14. Both go\nred under `return \"first\"` while the floor-only band stays green on all 108\nrows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(planner): author the open-climbing filler family and re-point the copy\n\nRulings 23, 29 and 30, plus ruling 31''s copy half and ruling 24''s revocation.\n\nRuling 23 adds `long_boulder_link_ups`, the first aerobic row a BOULDERER can\nbe given in a power-endurance block: all four `endurance` rows prescribable\nthere are `discipline=sport`, so boulder profiles took ZERO aerobic minutes at\nevery session count. 12 of 12 boulder profiles -> 0 of 12 with none. Dosed\nsustained and moderate at RPE 6, never to failure, because a hard row filed\nunder `endurance` would recreate F19.\n\nRulings 29 and 30 are implemented as a FAMILY of four rows, `OPEN_CLIMBING_KEYS`,\nand not the single row the ruling guessed at. The measured reason: FIVE of seven\nphases lead on a quality ruling 9''s weekly ceilings govern, so a filler keyed to\nthe block''s lead aspect is REFUSED on every day the ~3-hard-days ceiling has\nmade easy — and a filter has no fallback, so the session falls short of ruling\n25''s length. The family is ordered by the phase''s own `ASPECT_EMPHASIS` and the\nfirst row the ceilings allow wins, so the fill is credited to the block''s own\nquality on every hard day and walks to a non-governed row only on the easy ones.\nMeasured over ~9800 sessions: 0 off-lead fills on a hard day, 0 sessions with\ntwo fills. `_fill_rank`, `wall_fill_aspects` and the repeat fallback are\nDELETED, and the 386 `straight_sets` fill blocks are 0 of 1984 — filling time\nwith non-climbing was the opposite of ruling 27''s intent. \"Climb for fun is also\ntraining\" is Kilian''s doctrine and is attributed to him in `exercises.py`.\n\nRuling 31 closes the five-round POWER_ENDURANCE copy red by RE-AUTHORING the\nblock''s copy rather than the generator, and the whole clause moved rather than\nthe half that prompted it. Four claims were false, each only at particular\nsession counts: \"never enough to out-train the quality the block is named after\"\n(7 days, 6A boulder, 27.0% aerobic vs 23.0% power endurance), \"enough to let the\nnext hard session happen two days later\" (1 day on 6 of 6 profiles, 2 days on 2\nof 6, 3 days on 3 of 6), \"kept to a small share\" (0.0% at one day, 27.0% at\nseven), and the implicit promise that power endurance leads its own block —\n`technique` is the largest quality on 12 of 12 profiles at six and seven days,\n37.5-50.8% against power endurance''s 23.0-34.2%. 53-90% of those technique\nminutes are this commit''s filler, which is what earns the copy the words\nORDINARY CLIMBING. The retired guard is replaced by two, over session counts\n1-7, both shown red under sabotage.\n\nRuling 24 is REVOKED — no aerobic floor — and the copy that replaces it was\nFALSE at a granularity nothing was reading. The sentence said that from four\ndays up EVERY WEEK carries some aerobic work: per profile true on 18 of 18 and\ngreen, per WEEK 12 of those same 72 weeks hold none, all in week 14 or 15. No\nday boundary repairs it and no dose length does either. Re-authored to \"you\nalways get some of it, though not always in every week\", and the guard is three\narms, one per clause — arm 1 per CLIMBER because \"you\" is one climber, arms 2\nand 3 per WEEK — each shown red, including under the pooled read it replaced.\nA comment beside `FINGER_SESSIONS_PER_WEEK` records that the floor was declined\non the merits, because with no mechanism behind it the copy IS the mechanism.\n\nAlso here:\n\n  - `_length_pick`''s body restructure. The `band is None` branch that draws the\n    filler family and the `offered()` helper carrying the ceiling gate and the\n    band-top filter are one indivisible rewrite sharing a `prescribable(...)`\n    call, so it lands with the family it draws from rather than split across\n    the two earlier commits.\n  - `selection.py::ordinary` subtracts the family from every pool the ordinary\n    passes draw from, so \"climb for X minutes, your choice\" can only ever\n    arrive as the length fill and never as a session''s prescribed work.\n    `_validate_open_climbing_fill` proves at import that every phase''s filler\n    order ends in a row no ceiling governs.\n  - `tests/comment_budget_allowlist.toml`: the PR''s hand-written rows, no\n    `BASELINE` reasons, so `BASELINE_RATCHET` is untouched.\n  - `CLAUDE.md`: the findings-inbox pass this PR owed. Twelve dated inbox lines\n    routed to exactly one destination each — three kept as TRIPWIRES with `->`\n    pointers (no dose length closes the sport aerobic gap; the finger gate that\n    mattered was block count, not the climbing floor; measure the counterfactual\n    before shipping a prescribed mechanism), the rest deleted because a guard\n    now asserts them or archived for their reasoning. The archive section lives\n    at `../.archive/climb-trainer-CLAUDE-2026-09-03.md`, outside this repo, so\n    it is not part of this commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* guard: prove the quality gate''s ORDER, and empty the findings inbox\n\nEvery dated line in `CLAUDE.md`''s findings inbox routed to exactly one\ndestination, plus two authored claims that were false.\n\n`tests/test_claude_md_claims.py` — the `## Quality gate` chain arm tested each\ndocumented step with `step in script_value`, i.e. substring membership. It caught\na RENAMED step and nothing else: a reordered chain passed, and a documented\n`ruff format` passed against a script running `ruff format --check`. Its own\ndocstring claimed the documented order is the only place the gate''s order exists,\nso the arm did not prove the thing it existed for. It now splits the script on\n`&&` as well and walks forward from the last match, so index-monotonic order is\nrequired, and it compares at TOKEN level after stripping the runner prefix —\nliteral equality is impossible because every documented step is an abbreviation\n(`check:web` for `npm run check:web`, `ruff check` for `uv run ruff check .`).\nShown RED twice before green: swapping `build` and `test` in the documented\n`check:web` chain, and dropping `--check` from the documented `ruff format` step,\nwhich is the exact case the old arm passed. `.`/`-q` are still tolerated as\nbehaviour-free, which is the one difference the arm does not read.\n\n`tests/test_planner_selection.py` — the note on\n`test_aspect_emphasis_agrees_with_the_library_in_both_directions` said its first\nloop \"is the thing that fails in a test run\". It cannot be: `conftest.py` imports\n`server.app`, which reaches `selection.py`''s import-time validator at module\nscope, so an emphasis/library disagreement aborts COLLECTION and that assertion\ncan never be the red. Relabelled as unreachable by construction and kept only to\nname the cell, per the audit''s \"label it, don''t delete it\". Arm 2 untouched.\n\n`climbing.py` and `tests/test_planner_climbing_floor.py` — both credited\n`FINGER_SESSIONS_PER_WEEK[BEGINNER] = 0` to \"the sources want 6-12 months of\nconsistent climbing first\". That claim is in NEITHER extracted source; the\nconstant stays 0 and the attribution moves to Kilian, in both copies, because\nfixing one was a half-fix. No date invented — there is no recorded one. Note the\nsources are not silent on beginners: both say beginners habituate before they\nload hard, and Dylan programmes an explicit habituation protocol, so they scale\nhangboard CONTENT by level while never scaling session FREQUENCY by it. The\nmerits of the zero stay open as guard 5 and #118, which must be taken together.\n\n`CLAUDE.md` — the inbox is now EMPTY. The `_spread` mod-7 aliasing line moved to\n`issuesplan.md` as a named cause of #117 (it is a cause, not a prohibition, so it\ndoes not qualify as a tripwire). The §3.4 tier-ordering line is DELETED: it said\n`PHASE_GUIDE[POWER_ENDURANCE]` may not be upgraded to a lead claim until the\nweekly frequency ceilings land, and they landed — `d7c4235` then re-authored that\ncopy honestly rather than upgrading it. The substring-membership line is closed\nby the guard above.\n\nTripwire budget, per this file''s own \"to add a line here, archive one\":\n\n  + session length must never scale INVERSELY with training frequency\n  - the warm-up dose-in-moves finding, ARCHIVED instead of added\n  - the SQLite / real-Postgres line, ARCHIVED\n\nThe warm-up finding was routed to a tripwire and then re-routed, deliberately:\nunder the four-way rule it is reasoning about a ruling already taken, not a\nprohibition, and a tripwire would have been the only place in the repo its two\ncitations existed while its `→` pointed at a heading that did not hold them. It\nnow lives under `### Ruling 26''s warm-up share` in the archive (append-only,\ndiff-verified as a pure insertion). The SQLite line went because both halves are\nalready authored in `tests/conftest.py`''s module docstring, in bold with their\nreasoning, in the exact file anyone adding SQLite would be editing. The other\nthree archive candidates were REFUSED: each would have lost a prohibition whose\nonly other home is a self-attested PR-template checkbox or nothing at all.\n\nTwo prose fixes the above exposed, neither covered by any guard:\n\n  - `.github/workflows/ci.yml` cited `CLAUDE.md, \"SQLite is disqualified for\n    tests\"`, a string that existed only in the line this commit deletes. Now\n    points at `tests/conftest.py`''s module docstring, the live canonical home.\n    Nothing checks comment-to-CLAUDE.md citations, so this was found by hand.\n  - `conftest.py`''s remedy told the reader `npm run check:server` \"clears\n    DATABASE_URL\". It does not: it substitutes `CT_TEST_DATABASE_URL`, which is\n    empty only when that variable is unset. Re-worded to say what it does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(release): v8.10.0 — the weekly ceilings, session length and the filler family\n\nThe three commits before this one carried no bump: `package.json` still read\n8.9.0 and no `8.10.0` string existed anywhere in the repo, while\n`issuesplan.md`''s state line already asserted \"v8.10.0 on dev\" and every backlog\nentry named that version. A register that STATES the version rather than reading\nit will confirm a bump that never happened — the register is fixed in the same\npass, and the check is `package.json`, never the register.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnTdBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIDMQABxDT/EjYHijlj4lJ+GoMdcS\nVuTlYDnLzW9gJjbnrOdgI/Rt5GfFsFmobsveAKi7W9ngQ6BtdtRY7xn/VvvRxWwB\nrrArjZ990ov78xiRDo5Ub6THSIAcUFlXwnaMoJI6I4iBNoo1QHOB3DOjk4Scn18b\nZHvFOswKibQVOtgAMCrhuingm9EzYhBvNa80XpX0sIElbVuvMXC3ZQytT/flXQKg\nNixkdxc7IyPv1iAgasYcedyXdmAPeY7mo5vA2U3g+2nbwtYay4Ibmuvaf9Ma6Ps/\nVl/rqSBdCClEWxceBhQ0+SSPO8tY05AQygX4i1sJzQ9aHRlRUDhvvcUHl4QnzAyG\nEByLjoDldMg6b9uzPokf/M6WSqHImyHRIPA6cgfbi7zISODHEo9+HwecIIkYF6yM\nD4YITgk7GxImTEkqS9LNUj4Sb3wxMnvzAbBhC4I5N0QWPdH+hEyiCMf/uwWvPfVJ\npjPOI6bliZhltPOWX5SMfX+INHpGICzPikMEGC6Om6FdDE8svgAtRE3Bfq9H9W3N\nIJNxVOS0ccMJzrktXtOU74IvZ8qkiij/Y7Hxgm5b4mzuwfcFC0qAsrO8beg3ghdL\n7HJ6KNNnn6N8cGZN8M3pMxssMYk2DGZxPXFviPW7CTKwI9Vh89rKisLBRLOhGsND\nwv9dqUyYamheTXFYDWKN\n=gdzy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T09:49:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/9f0db1428622c463d878cf46f719432d7d1f50e2","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDlmMGRiMTQyODYyMmM0NjNkODc4Y2Y0NmY3MTk0MzJkN2QxZjUwZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/57d6919966000593951d0d4226809cfda80c1ea2","sha":"57d6919966000593951d0d4226809cfda80c1ea2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/57d6919966000593951d0d4226809cfda80c1ea2"}],"sha":"9f0db1428622c463d878cf46f719432d7d1f50e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/9f0db1428622c463d878cf46f719432d7d1f50e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/57d6919966000593951d0d4226809cfda80c1ea2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T22:33:47Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T22:33:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(planner): record the unload band''s missing ceiling as ruled, not owed (#123)\n\nKilian, 2026-09-05: the unload band has a 40% floor and no ceiling. On a week\nmeant for recovery the plan would rather leave work in than take too much out.\n\nBoth sources cap an unload week at 60% and v8.9.0 runs to 85.5%, so this\ndiverges from BOTH — which the interpretive rule normally makes a defect\nregardless of declaration. This is the ruled exception, recorded as doctrine\nruling 17, and the guard''s comment now says so instead of calling it an open\ndecision for Kilian. No assertion changed: guard 4 was already floor-only and\nits name already said so.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c3b42706f11bca651f713f7311d747f0a5b4c60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/6c3b42706f11bca651f713f7311d747f0a5b4c60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/57d6919966000593951d0d4226809cfda80c1ea2","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c3b42706f11bca651f713f7311d747f0a5b4c60\nparent f48ac6dfae0fde170de13a8d078fc36c3b246704\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788561227 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788561227 +0200\n\ndocs(planner): record the unload band''s missing ceiling as ruled, not owed (#123)\n\nKilian, 2026-09-05: the unload band has a 40% floor and no ceiling. On a week\nmeant for recovery the plan would rather leave work in than take too much out.\n\nBoth sources cap an unload week at 60% and v8.9.0 runs to 85.5%, so this\ndiverges from BOTH — which the interpretive rule normally makes a defect\nregardless of declaration. This is the ruled exception, recorded as doctrine\nruling 17, and the guard''s comment now says so instead of calling it an open\ndecision for Kilian. No assertion changed: guard 4 was already floor-only and\nits name already said so.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqm0dLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc3sQAI7DMO5/QjXd1EgZR95XOTWZ\ndY6QI+FJTiObr3+xLpRf4tMgThk1qkBYODGLOtLsqG8GrrFM2EIOM+DeQ6qL6LG1\npDJsUYO0OiV714gqvNEgyetCEEpWW0Fr8lDDYOvCTOyo07jOWZJ6LioujNJM3u9X\nSuj2fFuwn9XFo4O+hoCrIfTeuBjNG01MxTgmcThDK/vfdiDoBgBZ5vTw77IKdp/N\nxD6oVcyoCO/yqcgkMgz+kdwb0KY64hj7QYkdwXrBPvKpP4fsPenStycL9qwwCE7m\nPXWMNCku+NWPT/qkd4lmwECND6L6ycyw02h+f5jBd5iv8S0ROZ4sXEGKSR5S14gH\nzDfRJIpL/ptS5W1x5dh8XUx44LBwUTk0gQaB84CGPlGCfFVPXjrL7nH8WIf0XgBU\nbKh/Ygo3I+kGCJhrqFsLg3iYcZMeld6Wtc7frraeyxOdBfutqADSqJXjzDihE4Tu\nAtWbzUYhSJ8dqQ2+ZmPJCadbOsYDlEhFNImxKzzvPPXSTM77OX9E7ESjEmiYh2R9\nD/d0BjMOqAebxwA38bfdp3LjLP2i76ocIVWwKbTGNkjFg72iow2j1rUlnSqLWoxu\nFLzXrixyELQDAQUQz/hguOtfmTRINRDiD+QBr9dEkJZrx74QV7Lc9Kq9Z3sw1S8k\nEH886Du0XEK3Pw7jxZwl\n=uIag\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T22:33:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/57d6919966000593951d0d4226809cfda80c1ea2","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDU3ZDY5MTk5NjYwMDA1OTM5NTFkMGQ0MjI2ODA5Y2ZkYTgwYzFlYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/f48ac6dfae0fde170de13a8d078fc36c3b246704","sha":"f48ac6dfae0fde170de13a8d078fc36c3b246704","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/f48ac6dfae0fde170de13a8d078fc36c3b246704"}],"sha":"57d6919966000593951d0d4226809cfda80c1ea2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/57d6919966000593951d0d4226809cfda80c1ea2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/f48ac6dfae0fde170de13a8d078fc36c3b246704/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T22:18:40Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T22:18:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(planner): order work by intensity, re-author the taper, lift unload depth (#122)\n\nBarrows §3.4, §3.3 and both sources'' unload band, from the doctrine audit.\n\n§3.4 — hardest work first, within a session and across back-to-back days.\n`INTENSITY_TIERS` in `climbing.py` encodes the source''s chain; it is the third\nkey in `_ordered_blocks`''s rank, after `is_priority`, and `_kinds` is ordered\nthe same way so the block that leads a session is the block that sets its\nwindow. `_descend_by_intensity` reassigns weekday VALUES inside a run of\nconsecutive days — never the drafts list, which would re-key `_spread` and\nevery candidate pool. Within-session inversions 442/2040 -> 0, adjacent-day\n296/1080 -> 0. A Mon/Wed/Fri week is untouched, and the guard asserts it\ncontributes zero adjacent pairs so its green is by construction.\n\n§3.3 — the taper drops all An Cap, Aero Cap and ARC (`endurance` 47% of taper\nminutes -> 0) and carries the two ingredients the section says it is made of\n(0.0% -> 27.8%): `power_endurance` on four rows and short upper-body pulling\nstrength on two. The finger exclusion stays and is re-attributed to Kilian on\ninjury grounds, declared out loud in `PHASE_GUIDE[TAPER]` — the source would\nkeep hard finger work.\n\nUnload depth — `_short_of_its_window` no longer exempts unloading phases, so\nruling 3''s ordinary-climbing top-up reaches a halved session floor. Deloads\n25-52% -> 43-86% and tapers 14-49% -> 49-68% of their own block''s loading mean.\nNo row was re-dosed. Both `PHASE_GUIDE` lines now claim exactly the 40% floor\nthe guard asserts; \"roughly half\" is gone from both.\n\nThe 60% CEILING is deliberately NOT closed (Kilian, 2026-09-05): a deload is a\nmesocycle in its own right and does not know which block it closes. Filed as\nitem 5 with the mechanism and two rejected levers. Guard 4 is floor-only and\nsays so in its name; the hole is recorded with its captured non-red — doubling\nevery unload row''s sets produces no failure.\n\nCloses audit findings F4, F5, F16 and guard findings 2, 3, 14, 15; F6 and guard\nfinding 7 half-closed. `GENERATOR_VERSION` 6.0.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1b16a85038eef96383905fb2361fd149f2f0c88e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/1b16a85038eef96383905fb2361fd149f2f0c88e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/f48ac6dfae0fde170de13a8d078fc36c3b246704","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b16a85038eef96383905fb2361fd149f2f0c88e\nparent e3271d4015edbc8f4dc9cfe3c67a3a89e0c45f21\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788560320 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788560320 +0200\n\nfeat(planner): order work by intensity, re-author the taper, lift unload depth (#122)\n\nBarrows §3.4, §3.3 and both sources'' unload band, from the doctrine audit.\n\n§3.4 — hardest work first, within a session and across back-to-back days.\n`INTENSITY_TIERS` in `climbing.py` encodes the source''s chain; it is the third\nkey in `_ordered_blocks`''s rank, after `is_priority`, and `_kinds` is ordered\nthe same way so the block that leads a session is the block that sets its\nwindow. `_descend_by_intensity` reassigns weekday VALUES inside a run of\nconsecutive days — never the drafts list, which would re-key `_spread` and\nevery candidate pool. Within-session inversions 442/2040 -> 0, adjacent-day\n296/1080 -> 0. A Mon/Wed/Fri week is untouched, and the guard asserts it\ncontributes zero adjacent pairs so its green is by construction.\n\n§3.3 — the taper drops all An Cap, Aero Cap and ARC (`endurance` 47% of taper\nminutes -> 0) and carries the two ingredients the section says it is made of\n(0.0% -> 27.8%): `power_endurance` on four rows and short upper-body pulling\nstrength on two. The finger exclusion stays and is re-attributed to Kilian on\ninjury grounds, declared out loud in `PHASE_GUIDE[TAPER]` — the source would\nkeep hard finger work.\n\nUnload depth — `_short_of_its_window` no longer exempts unloading phases, so\nruling 3''s ordinary-climbing top-up reaches a halved session floor. Deloads\n25-52% -> 43-86% and tapers 14-49% -> 49-68% of their own block''s loading mean.\nNo row was re-dosed. Both `PHASE_GUIDE` lines now claim exactly the 40% floor\nthe guard asserts; \"roughly half\" is gone from both.\n\nThe 60% CEILING is deliberately NOT closed (Kilian, 2026-09-05): a deload is a\nmesocycle in its own right and does not know which block it closes. Filed as\nitem 5 with the mechanism and two rejected levers. Guard 4 is floor-only and\nsays so in its name; the hole is recorded with its captured non-red — doubling\nevery unload row''s sets produces no failure.\n\nCloses audit findings F4, F5, F16 and guard findings 2, 3, 14, 15; F6 and guard\nfinding 7 half-closed. `GENERATOR_VERSION` 6.0.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqm0PACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAo6EQAHt/dXJC3jgh3TaIXRtk1u0V\nF6osF4Yf+EfjMa0IFnwUEQgDrC8R/6bQQzFj74p9kQd/jlaRyTE/sHpDwYgCenaX\n2DwEZps5rfFTtW6J7wycxLeUDvLp23yH9Qb6tYuGFkZsmCP32xCn74lkpIX2wiUN\nlCOis4RCfblStrmnJNvee+9JHAiPKfEHQOBaaTUzKOSVllr5prctil/Aw8/34WDE\ngBGrFfONf5X9/kDJV8MonA3SGqZ7sslD+UjzmYKTu/e3QrlHOt4ol+rqdKMTTpLL\nVwEUzRLqgzlFU3PyquS5M8ysriYKqfhXuhBy2mFL3KEqho97Tima4ALlDCTzMzBW\nZcvyVLbRfv2p6n4/PX1vpKztaiRt8NVlshlspiFgnkD8P2wS3kRbGpmRz+lR7UlD\nwkTyZUumcmcSNbN4zuBBa4oZElzXbTZaDtxGcyPaA5hsfSglPclxTJIyutFzl45P\nkvABqqFxNsEtXBiDciW8WInhACl7QKAY//sTbRFl1IYgPdDAsbEZxc7uIruoEsvu\nsVpq0mb+kvwkcZOJpAaJZh18sEgDjMeqWi3UtHQWl7VmWqbm2MA0OkttPAOryXlB\noNx9F6O1EExVL54JqvD3Y8HJStJ+9YsDcd9P6RwSiEXu2XskO6fj8vYqvxzwXFHZ\nMyj429J8aeZw7jnFKeaG\n=XG8h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T22:18:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/f48ac6dfae0fde170de13a8d078fc36c3b246704","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKGY0OGFjNmRmYWUwZmRlMTcwZGUxM2E4ZDA3OGZjMzZjM2IyNDY3MDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/e3271d4015edbc8f4dc9cfe3c67a3a89e0c45f21","sha":"e3271d4015edbc8f4dc9cfe3c67a3a89e0c45f21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/e3271d4015edbc8f4dc9cfe3c67a3a89e0c45f21"}],"sha":"f48ac6dfae0fde170de13a8d078fc36c3b246704","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/f48ac6dfae0fde170de13a8d078fc36c3b246704"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/e3271d4015edbc8f4dc9cfe3c67a3a89e0c45f21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:19:01Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:19:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(planner): make every PHASE_GUIDE claim true of a generated plan (#121)\n\nThe guard on the phase copy compared it to ASPECT_EMPHASIS — the app''s\nintention against itself — so it stayed green while all six lead claims\nwere false in a generated plan. It now reads plans the generator\nproduced, in the shapes the sentences actually make.\n\nThree behaviour changes were needed to make the sentences true:\n\n- three on-wall max-effort rows re-filed general_strength -> power, and\n  their text moved into the power section so they land at the end of the\n  pool rather than its head\n- a deload gets its own rules: DELOAD_CLIMBING_FLOOR_PCT = 50 and\n  technique/mobility ordered ahead of the climbing. Mobility goes from\n  5.0% to 9.1% of deload minutes and now opens sessions at all\n- ASPECT_EMPHASIS[POWER_ENDURANCE] moves endurance from index 1 to 7,\n  cutting it from 4 wall turns to 2\n\nGENERATOR_VERSION 4.0.0 -> 5.0.0.\n\nThree exceptions registered with diagnosed reasons and reverse arms, and\nthe advanced band ceiling re-baselined 62 -> 64 off a defect: excluding\ndeload weeks, dev already measured 62.3% before this PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b7fbd9c3648f04c04990c2cc92faa6a91adee49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/7b7fbd9c3648f04c04990c2cc92faa6a91adee49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/e3271d4015edbc8f4dc9cfe3c67a3a89e0c45f21","verification":{"payload":"tree 7b7fbd9c3648f04c04990c2cc92faa6a91adee49\nparent 8edc819b1fa71733256c195eb47b81a58ad4beb6\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788549541 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788549541 +0200\n\nfix(planner): make every PHASE_GUIDE claim true of a generated plan (#121)\n\nThe guard on the phase copy compared it to ASPECT_EMPHASIS — the app''s\nintention against itself — so it stayed green while all six lead claims\nwere false in a generated plan. It now reads plans the generator\nproduced, in the shapes the sentences actually make.\n\nThree behaviour changes were needed to make the sentences true:\n\n- three on-wall max-effort rows re-filed general_strength -> power, and\n  their text moved into the power section so they land at the end of the\n  pool rather than its head\n- a deload gets its own rules: DELOAD_CLIMBING_FLOOR_PCT = 50 and\n  technique/mobility ordered ahead of the climbing. Mobility goes from\n  5.0% to 9.1% of deload minutes and now opens sessions at all\n- ASPECT_EMPHASIS[POWER_ENDURANCE] moves endurance from index 1 to 7,\n  cutting it from 4 wall turns to 2\n\nGENERATOR_VERSION 4.0.0 -> 5.0.0.\n\nThree exceptions registered with diagnosed reasons and reverse arms, and\nthe advanced band ceiling re-baselined 62 -> 64 off a defect: excluding\ndeload weeks, dev already measured 62.3% before this PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmxmlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATLIQAIFDk598R1mEZpJ7sCA6Dizy\nMaL6DaawSf7ybY5VSoVg2btq7QWNocs5VKmvd8lPx53nW2c1SwdqwNjhthyLOu2N\nBCQ9B/IGl+yzudQ0RYydCL7Ie8b2uWhNzbX+mJF08K1ZtS8RRUMrqN+mJHVpiwVj\nRK34/9p23Z7q3CXLKCbZUgX2DF733rBaYJtkdH09gHVp0vk5KBm/oonpufzfCB9B\n9WhFzL/2dCZhl5aL+VcrmGEaOaErdvenO8eYimGQhO3BybAcd4cSUIKmOV/VOnfs\nctz5WryWSM/OXOUbhW/ycMslHw3sJSysD72nzb9vMAU1oKoD/VnNypIKK+MlzeIG\ndQLqmVMnMtuAWXzQVEWfEoRvx2Hm2tx0rCSDqEYRKy2Gdajk2ezhIJovyEJpG4/6\n8oVukKRwt3/NYB/q9lAc1680St/PKWKgq2Py1fuwpHj6BSCSoSvXETTfdWCBAc/l\nNYcYUFS4bg0dJNYzx8Xj81CwvtvGzej12pfEaAQAaTTMPwL2npjXQsR3fSt0gtY3\nvF4LaRBFeuvbcplsEm40kWCeTvVPdoHF/g1Qvg0mpG4wGOTmnvgKTBOttVOI0y/d\nOyhVCqXn6iNwh37Q5zvPDeseAIgt8VPWYdf7QofwYws18Ubgg2ZxdcnY24xAlG34\n0i71SOgM6jMyUV4domvB\n=KNEq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T19:19:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/e3271d4015edbc8f4dc9cfe3c67a3a89e0c45f21","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKGUzMjcxZDQwMTVlZGJjOGY0ZGM5Y2ZlM2M2N2EzYTg5ZTBjNDVmMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/8edc819b1fa71733256c195eb47b81a58ad4beb6","sha":"8edc819b1fa71733256c195eb47b81a58ad4beb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/8edc819b1fa71733256c195eb47b81a58ad4beb6"}],"sha":"e3271d4015edbc8f4dc9cfe3c67a3a89e0c45f21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/e3271d4015edbc8f4dc9cfe3c67a3a89e0c45f21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/8edc819b1fa71733256c195eb47b81a58ad4beb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T17:09:53Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T17:09:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(library): author the thin indoor cells and audit the doses (#89) (#120)\n\nThe plain-gym monoculture is fixed at its cause: `limit_boulders` was the\nonly on-wall `power` row a bouldering-gym user could reach that carried a\n`STRENGTH` prescription, so the generator drew it 18 times running. Six new\nplain-gym power rows now carry one, and no single exercise exceeds 8.5% of a\nplan''s prescribed minutes (was 25.5-27.9%).\n\n13 exercises added, library 87 -> 100: six `power`, two `anaerobic_capacity`\n(the aspect had no on-wall option at all), four `general_strength`, and one\n`endurance` to break the `arc_traversing` monoculture the plan''s own proposal\nlist did not cover. Seven existing rows re-dosed against Barrows'' §7 table.\n\nThree generator defects the content exposed, each fixed on its merits:\nsessions under their type''s floor are now topped up with climbing rather than\naccessories; the wall-share band''s top edge is read per session rather than\nper week, so a day added is climbing added; and the base-ordering guard is\nre-scoped to §3.2''s actual claim (the two MAINTAINED qualities take <=15% of\nbase wall time) instead of a strict pairwise ranking no source states.\n\nAlso fixes a latent persistence bug: generated titles could exceed their\n`String(80)` column and raise `StringDataRightTruncation` on save.\n\n`GENERATOR_VERSION` 3.0.0 -> 4.0.0 for the behaviour changes; the content\nalone would not have needed it, since `library_digest()` already makes a\ncontent edit read as a different input.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"843337221c926945485599ed71df9453f2b054e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/843337221c926945485599ed71df9453f2b054e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/8edc819b1fa71733256c195eb47b81a58ad4beb6","verification":{"payload":"tree 843337221c926945485599ed71df9453f2b054e7\nparent 890c4a265fa5b621dd3f864e938c289e9a16c9d4\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788541793 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788541793 +0000\n\nfeat(library): author the thin indoor cells and audit the doses (#89) (#120)\n\nThe plain-gym monoculture is fixed at its cause: `limit_boulders` was the\nonly on-wall `power` row a bouldering-gym user could reach that carried a\n`STRENGTH` prescription, so the generator drew it 18 times running. Six new\nplain-gym power rows now carry one, and no single exercise exceeds 8.5% of a\nplan''s prescribed minutes (was 25.5-27.9%).\n\n13 exercises added, library 87 -> 100: six `power`, two `anaerobic_capacity`\n(the aspect had no on-wall option at all), four `general_strength`, and one\n`endurance` to break the `arc_traversing` monoculture the plan''s own proposal\nlist did not cover. Seven existing rows re-dosed against Barrows'' §7 table.\n\nThree generator defects the content exposed, each fixed on its merits:\nsessions under their type''s floor are now topped up with climbing rather than\naccessories; the wall-share band''s top edge is read per session rather than\nper week, so a day added is climbing added; and the base-ordering guard is\nre-scoped to §3.2''s actual claim (the two MAINTAINED qualities take <=15% of\nbase wall time) instead of a strict pairwise ranking no source states.\n\nAlso fixes a latent persistence bug: generated titles could exceed their\n`String(80)` column and raise `StringDataRightTruncation` on save.\n\n`GENERATOR_VERSION` 3.0.0 -> 4.0.0 for the behaviour changes; the content\nalone would not have needed it, since `library_digest()` already makes a\ncontent edit read as a different input.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmvthCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAshIQAGXaIwrxiTYSYguTPq2iqSrQ\nBD4ITpj2PbOeoCm59tj1KeHIzQqcd1pGyRn+HdLzK8eLDFS9wA0H