938c289e9a16c9d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/890c4a265fa5b621dd3f864e938c289e9a16c9d4"}],"sha":"8edc819b1fa71733256c195eb47b81a58ad4beb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/8edc819b1fa71733256c195eb47b81a58ad4beb6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/890c4a265fa5b621dd3f864e938c289e9a16c9d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:15:49Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:15:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(model): split the aspect vocabulary into ten (#98) (#119)\n\n`power` had to mean both max force and fast force, and `power_endurance` both\nanaerobic capacity and aerobic power — pairs with opposite doses and opposite\nprogression rules. So a Max strength block labelled its days `P`.\n\nAdd `general_strength` and `anaerobic_capacity`. Purely additive: no key is\nretired or renamed, so no migration and no `ALTER TYPE`. The key is NOT\n`strength` — that would collide with the `Phase.STRENGTH` enum value in every\npayload, query and log line.\n\n- Re-file 9 exercises: 5 max-force rows `power` -> `general_strength`, 4\n  half-minute-burst rows `power_endurance` -> `anaerobic_capacity`.\n  `limit_boulders` and `outdoor_boulder_projecting` deliberately stay.\n- Replace all seven `ASPECT_EMPHASIS` rows with the source-derived priority\n  matrix (Barrows v2 §2-§3, Dylan wk 1-12). Kilian''s three calls, 2026-09-04:\n  endurance keeps the base wall lead; anaerobic capacity is unprescribed in\n  performance and taper; general strength unprescribed in power endurance\n  and taper.\n- Author `split_squats` and `self_resisted_forearm_intervals` — both new\n  aspects had no zero-equipment option after the re-file, which the per-aspect\n  gearless floor requires. No new `CELLS_WITH_NO_GEARLESS_OPTION` row needed.\n- `PHASE_GUIDE`''s order claims become executable rather than prose: three\n  guards in `test_phase_guide.py` restate them independently, plus a measured\n  arm in `test_planner_climbing_floor.py`. A substring check was rejected\n  because \"endurance\" is a substring of \"power endurance\".\n- `GENERATOR_VERSION` 2.1.0 -> 3.0.0: new `aspect_key` values reach every\n  payload, the same class as the 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0 bump.\n\n`general_strength` is IN `WALL_LED_ASPECTS`: `wall_led_aspects()` filters it\nper phase to on-wall candidates, so no gym lift can name a session, while\nthree exercises whose own instructions say \"the strength session\" now can.\nLeaving it out made them unreachable by any profile.\n\nMeasured, full equipment vocabulary, sport 6a->6c: `power` 35.8% -> 23.5%,\n`general_strength` 23.5%. In a plain bouldering gym it changes almost nothing\nand `limit_boulders` stays at 21-28% — no on-wall option exists for either new\naspect there, and no sub-maximal on-wall power option exists at all. That is\n#89, sequenced next.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c3dd18fad7ab98ab6a65efcbab746846797eb29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/2c3dd18fad7ab98ab6a65efcbab746846797eb29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/890c4a265fa5b621dd3f864e938c289e9a16c9d4","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c3dd18fad7ab98ab6a65efcbab746846797eb29\nparent 48aa7b52803568811351651877fc4193ca3aadf6\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788531349 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788531349 +0200\n\nfeat(model): split the aspect vocabulary into ten (#98) (#119)\n\n`power` had to mean both max force and fast force, and `power_endurance` both\nanaerobic capacity and aerobic power — pairs with opposite doses and opposite\nprogression rules. So a Max strength block labelled its days `P`.\n\nAdd `general_strength` and `anaerobic_capacity`. Purely additive: no key is\nretired or renamed, so no migration and no `ALTER TYPE`. The key is NOT\n`strength` — that would collide with the `Phase.STRENGTH` enum value in every\npayload, query and log line.\n\n- Re-file 9 exercises: 5 max-force rows `power` -> `general_strength`, 4\n  half-minute-burst rows `power_endurance` -> `anaerobic_capacity`.\n  `limit_boulders` and `outdoor_boulder_projecting` deliberately stay.\n- Replace all seven `ASPECT_EMPHASIS` rows with the source-derived priority\n  matrix (Barrows v2 §2-§3, Dylan wk 1-12). Kilian''s three calls, 2026-09-04:\n  endurance keeps the base wall lead; anaerobic capacity is unprescribed in\n  performance and taper; general strength unprescribed in power endurance\n  and taper.\n- Author `split_squats` and `self_resisted_forearm_intervals` — both new\n  aspects had no zero-equipment option after the re-file, which the per-aspect\n  gearless floor requires. No new `CELLS_WITH_NO_GEARLESS_OPTION` row needed.\n- `PHASE_GUIDE`''s order claims become executable rather than prose: three\n  guards in `test_phase_guide.py` restate them independently, plus a measured\n  arm in `test_planner_climbing_floor.py`. A substring check was rejected\n  because \"endurance\" is a substring of \"power endurance\".\n- `GENERATOR_VERSION` 2.1.0 -> 3.0.0: new `aspect_key` values reach every\n  payload, the same class as the 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0 bump.\n\n`general_strength` is IN `WALL_LED_ASPECTS`: `wall_led_aspects()` filters it\nper phase to on-wall candidates, so no gym lift can name a session, while\nthree exercises whose own instructions say \"the strength session\" now can.\nLeaving it out made them unreachable by any profile.\n\nMeasured, full equipment vocabulary, sport 6a->6c: `power` 35.8% -> 23.5%,\n`general_strength` 23.5%. In a plain bouldering gym it changes almost nothing\nand `limit_boulders` stays at 21-28% — no on-wall option exists for either new\naspect there, and no sub-maximal on-wall power option exists at all. That is\n#89, sequenced next.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmtKVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgUoQAHcKYQx/OFK3vV5WXhY6hjpW\nmhvOqh5Ker0JrimO6pxm8OQdPKulhKDBEWg2zGR/0ZhgGLffG+aQt6l28Fovh4j7\nn4Guun8Yqnori8750csSjqQYAeAO7LDHhs/0PCHUvLAKAoQ+rFIerO5/VTDPb3ve\nkn+g0XmQWpNrResFPUr53DSmTLKQeu9oB+khHjMpq3DD5T5/jN/Cs99r4R5l9RD1\npZSVaHUXckq8HkBS9rWbN4wPjt0zUnF8bX+cywJI10NvHp+nqXbsI5XyfYrrU08X\nK1NH0pKaHpuUud+zMGTWxH2rJ3kkUnBebzTkJbXTGQlh4OfqjQHcpQsKilP0hUdI\nAo7yeGWrpWKpDvn2PsEZKSt2vpLbWQQ9fys3HUugsgfrIeMghZ+IjsmKKStILvDz\nMofqrRU73HXc5O3uRQVuh9a9/J0sxhLUbPPaIJWBgw8+uzwCct8mQzhm6UIXLo+y\nvwXufvyPdB4dOxg2Rx9dwUSE6OoN3JaJ4rADlrOY57C17zEMc8W5U1lFSBzbLLFT\nK6z0uMdowa/Ex1wgMmvFfLf8biuqn+s3pKD6JtXZCWZIs2g1tg5fwSF7Gdk/1pqa\nLsiaa5F11lYsGr6/f4T00EXm9xiX4/XvTpBu9D9LD4qCm6pMBbgry8nKejLCw13l\n4rKCjRBW/UVlOrT/eszO\n=04Fi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T14:15:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/890c4a265fa5b621dd3f864e938c289e9a16c9d4","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDg5MGM0YTI2NWZhNWI2MjFkZDNmODY0ZTkzOGMyODllOWExNmM5ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/48aa7b52803568811351651877fc4193ca3aadf6","sha":"48aa7b52803568811351651877fc4193ca3aadf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/48aa7b52803568811351651877fc4193ca3aadf6"}],"sha":"890c4a265fa5b621dd3f864e938c289e9a16c9d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/890c4a265fa5b621dd3f864e938c289e9a16c9d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/48aa7b52803568811351651877fc4193ca3aadf6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:08:15Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:08:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rank the climbing pass by the phase''s authored emphasis order (#116)\n\n`ASPECT_EMPHASIS[Phase.BASE]` ranks power last and power-endurance\nsecond-to-last, and `PHASE_GUIDE[base]` says so in prose — but that\nordering only governed the supplementary pass. `_wall_picks` walked a\nflat rotation giving every wall-led aspect one entry each, so power and\npower-endurance took a wall block in nearly every base session anyway,\nand technique (ranked second) took the fewest wall minutes of the four.\n\nThe climbing pass now walks a rank-weighted ring of turns from\n`wall_aspect_turns(phase)`: an aspect''s turns come from its distance\nfrom the bottom of the emphasis row, capped at `BLOCKS_PER_SESSION + 1`\nand interleaved so they never arrive in runs. The ring is indexed by\n`_spread` rather than the old `offset`, because `week_no - 1 +\nsession_index` takes only ~5 values inside a three-week phase and a\nlonger ring would never be sampled.\n\nStrict rank order was measured and rejected: it takes base to 100%\nendurance wall minutes, zeroes technique and breaks the reach guard,\nbecause a leading endurance block expands to the fill target and\n`_fill_climbing` then breaks. The cap is what keeps\n`test_more_available_days_never_reduces_climbing_minutes` green.\n\nBeginner base block, share of prescribed minutes on power +\npower-endurance: sport 6a→6c 30.5% → 13.5%, boulder 6A→7A 22.0% → 11.5%.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aa1374b6ae8163532ac7c44db3026d4be116217b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/aa1374b6ae8163532ac7c44db3026d4be116217b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/48aa7b52803568811351651877fc4193ca3aadf6","verification":{"payload":"tree aa1374b6ae8163532ac7c44db3026d4be116217b\nparent 9812a67dfad82a46783f12ee78697c97d8d5b5d9\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788527295 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788527295 +0200\n\nRank the climbing pass by the phase''s authored emphasis order (#116)\n\n`ASPECT_EMPHASIS[Phase.BASE]` ranks power last and power-endurance\nsecond-to-last, and `PHASE_GUIDE[base]` says so in prose — but that\nordering only governed the supplementary pass. `_wall_picks` walked a\nflat rotation giving every wall-led aspect one entry each, so power and\npower-endurance took a wall block in nearly every base session anyway,\nand technique (ranked second) took the fewest wall minutes of the four.\n\nThe climbing pass now walks a rank-weighted ring of turns from\n`wall_aspect_turns(phase)`: an aspect''s turns come from its distance\nfrom the bottom of the emphasis row, capped at `BLOCKS_PER_SESSION + 1`\nand interleaved so they never arrive in runs. The ring is indexed by\n`_spread` rather than the old `offset`, because `week_no - 1 +\nsession_index` takes only ~5 values inside a three-week phase and a\nlonger ring would never be sampled.\n\nStrict rank order was measured and rejected: it takes base to 100%\nendurance wall minutes, zeroes technique and breaks the reach guard,\nbecause a leading endurance block expands to the fill target and\n`_fill_climbing` then breaks. The cap is what keeps\n`test_more_available_days_never_reduces_climbing_minutes` green.\n\nBeginner base block, share of prescribed minutes on power +\npower-endurance: sport 6a→6c 30.5% → 13.5%, boulder 6A→7A 22.0% → 11.5%.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmsLACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf+cQAGmefAT6vWSK1xG/MXccMZow\nCT41qpDvIoU44FeeSnZpiowKQDO+ChdHrMprUcxidbfqYxQwWbZCI8FkHJgg1hzB\nJpn/5SxXLFl9+hWieWAF1bQ1MPQUm5Erq34Vq8Jfdp0DadNj8/uJsy+I5EMw9qEl\nlGrPvKsJwO8zNicKCofeuFNWSfQud22fk1uT4ha9GYZww+2deKWkCmyQGCMy3L9e\nxy6Iyy1fsC3kEgDay7rFpfBc/uDW+UVrw705s6YYMmGPaMydJib7bR2cwJsth85b\nwjr0vbOMQaNC0d4R8kMiFbxS6Hlj7VQSdbbozqFCXqFS+KMjBIzprmLKcbYpPs4r\nRFXjghfJBcA5q+dYBpvcjwDCGktzPZX3nqlZxw6RBVVhfKMB5DlND8MNM9uMOajP\nWaw41h6lUZ98oa2VueWFEXug/DQSrZ+TGuZ2VKRuIns5NabS6BgFtUfo1CdU5sj+\nbzHcbE8EilgptnG7xVTrlUImL+rpnonBYlJMXklnmTcNmnhygKA8LmfvGD210MD/\nXMCfCsjXSibVcxejXCDTmpeKF1MZt3A9XEWobM8hBehXcobzwAnjQetQFSwHP/0R\n/SuKxt3c9wQjXcN0Xch6tyc49Ld4XmZVX6mfQfK2+T9hEb0TRmjXZs4tW36DR2S1\n3DNyo2InGM7j7KSpEZAB\n=2VMr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T13:08:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https