url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/87739ee29abad2d438c8d55cdf8a5cfa421d8b0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T12:56:51Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T12:56:51Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"guard: assert remoteEntry.js and the MF chunks stay precached (#74)\n\n`inlineWorkboxRuntime: true` bakes the precache list into `dist/sw.js` as a\nminified literal, and nothing read it back. The standalone app boots through\n`/remoteEntry.js` and MF''s virtual chunks, so a `globIgnores` on the federation\nentry looked like a tidy-up, kept the whole gate green, and broke the installed\napp offline.\n\nSix arms plus a positive control in the built-output contract test, all derived\nfrom the built output rather than listing hashed filenames: the unhashed URLs\ncarry a real revision, every `index.html` boot href is precached, every chunk\nreachable from `remoteEntry.js` is precached, and the precached set stays inside\na byte ceiling so a widened `globPatterns` cannot push `dist/landing/` into a\nphone''s Cache Storage.\n\n`remoteStylesheets()` becomes `remoteGraph()` and returns the chunk set the walk\nalready built instead of discarding it. The PWA tripwire in CLAUDE.md loses its\nprecache clause: the claim is executable now, so it must not be prose.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ccda6c43e15908d8c19b482b62d2fc3a7b8c0a06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/ccda6c43e15908d8c19b482b62d2fc3a7b8c0a06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/87739ee29abad2d438c8d55cdf8a5cfa421d8b0a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/87739ee29abad2d438c8d55cdf8a5cfa421d8b0a","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDg3NzM5ZWUyOWFiYWQyZDQzOGM4ZDU1Y2RmOGE1Y2ZhNDIxZDhiMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/db22f1b4362f487eb8e6574d680e2fc7d030f075","sha":"db22f1b4362f487eb8e6574d680e2fc7d030f075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/db22f1b4362f487eb8e6574d680e2fc7d030f075"}],"sha":"87739ee29abad2d438c8d55cdf8a5cfa421d8b0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/87739ee29abad2d438c8d55cdf8a5cfa421d8b0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/db22f1b4362f487eb8e6574d680e2fc7d030f075/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T10:40:35Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T10:40:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: replace CLAUDE.md with a tripwire index, and archive the reasoning (#114)\n\nCLAUDE.md was 4,036 lines / 298KB, auto-loaded into every session in this\nrepo. It is now 163 lines: only what working code cannot tell you, which is\nprohibitions, traps and decisions already reversed once. Each line names the\narchive heading that holds its reasoning.\n\nThe full file is frozen verbatim outside every git repo, at\n../.archive/climb-trainer-CLAUDE-2026-09-03.md, together with the project\nmemory that grew the same way (1,780 lines, now a 30-line router). Verbatim\nmatters: 52 guard docstrings in 22 test files cite CLAUDE.md section\nheadings, and a verbatim archive keeps every one of them resolving.\n\nWhy a tripwire index rather than a pointer file: \"look it up in the archive\nif the code does not answer it\" works for how-does-X-work and fails for\ndo-not-do-X. Opening vercel.json shows valid config and gives no hint that\nframework: \"fastapi\" is catastrophic, so nothing prompts the lookup. A\nprohibition has to stay in the loaded file; only its reasoning can move.\n\nGuards reconciled so none contradicts the trim:\n\n- The four index arms are deleted along with UNINDEXED_SECTIONS and\n  _index_bounds. There is no ## Index any more. That arm was also a regrowth\n  engine: every new section owed a prose index row.\n- test_every_repo_rooted_path_it_names_resolves asserted len(named) > 50 and\n  would have failed on the new file. Floor is now 15 against 23 real.\n- Three arms with nothing left to check are deleted rather than left green\n  over an empty set: the cited-test-name arm, the alembic-revision arm and\n  the heading-level control.\n- ENV_VARS 9 -> 4, plus a new assertion that every key is still named in\n  CLAUDE.md, so the list cannot outlive the doc.\n- test_every_readme_section_this_file_cites_resolves gains `assert cited`.\n- 9 orphaned allowlist rows removed; BASELINE_RATCHET 990 -> 983, the exact\n  real count.\n\nA ## Findings inbox replaces the habit of adding a section per discovery:\none dated line each, triaged at every promotion to main into a guard, a\ntripwire, the archive, or deleted. Its first entry is a defect found while\nproving the reworked guards still bite - the quality-gate chain arm tests\neach step with substring membership, so it catches a renamed step but not a\nreordered chain, though its docstring claims the documented order is the\nonly place that order exists (#26).\n\nBoth probes went red before being reverted: a renamed path failed the path\narm, and a reworded chain line failed the chain arm.\n\nnpm run check green, run once at the end: web 1,219 passed, server 901\npassed, 0 skipped. The local test database holds non-demo accounts, so the\nserver arm ran against a throwaway database that was dropped afterwards.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df6cee36febb36bdb1652b72f3bcedb6e0be83ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/df6cee36febb36bdb1652b72f3bcedb6e0be83ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/db22f1b4362f487eb8e6574d680e2fc7d030f075","verification":{"payload":"tree df6cee36febb36bdb1652b72f3bcedb6e0be83ce\nparent fe285ee55fa0c2c65498388388f308a0b5b7c342\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788432035 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788432035 +0200\n\ndocs: replace CLAUDE.md with a tripwire index, and archive the reasoning (#114)\n\nCLAUDE.md was 4,036 lines / 298KB, auto-loaded into every session in this\nrepo. It is now 163 lines: only what working code cannot tell you, which is\nprohibitions, traps and decisions already reversed once. Each line names the\narchive heading that holds its reasoning.\n\nThe full file is frozen verbatim outside every git repo, at\n../.archive/climb-trainer-CLAUDE-2026-09-03.md, together with the project\nmemory that grew the same way (1,780 lines, now a 30-line router). Verbatim\nmatters: 52 guard docstrings in 22 test files cite CLAUDE.md section\nheadings, and a verbatim archive keeps every one of them resolving.\n\nWhy a tripwire index rather than a pointer file: \"look it up in the archive\nif the code does not answer it\" works for how-does-X-work and fails for\ndo-not-do-X. Opening vercel.json shows valid config and gives no hint that\nframework: \"fastapi\" is catastrophic, so nothing prompts the lookup. A\nprohibition has to stay in the loaded file; only its reasoning can move.\n\nGuards reconciled so none contradicts the trim:\n\n- The four index arms are deleted along with UNINDEXED_SECTIONS and\n  _index_bounds. There is no ## Index any more. That arm was also a regrowth\n  engine: every new section owed a prose index row.\n- test_every_repo_rooted_path_it_names_resolves asserted len(named) > 50 and\n  would have failed on the new file. Floor is now 15 against 23 real.\n- Three arms with nothing left to check are deleted rather than left green\n  over an empty set: the cited-test-name arm, the alembic-revision arm and\n  the heading-level control.\n- ENV_VARS 9 -> 4, plus a new assertion that every key is still named in\n  CLAUDE.md, so the list cannot outlive the doc.\n- test_every_readme_section_this_file_cites_resolves gains `assert cited`.\n- 9 orphaned allowlist rows removed; BASELINE_RATCHET 990 -> 983, the exact\n  real count.\n\nA ## Findings inbox replaces the habit of adding a section per discovery:\none dated line each, triaged at every promotion to main into a guard, a\ntripwire, the archive, or deleted. Its first entry is a defect found while\nproving the reworked guards still bite - the quality-gate chain arm tests\neach step with substring membership, so it catches a renamed step but not a\nreordered chain, though its docstring claims the documented order is the\nonly place that order exists (#26).\n\nBoth probes went red before being reverted: a renamed path failed the path\narm, and a reworded chain line failed the chain arm.\n\nnpm run check green, run once at the end: web 1,219 passed, server 901\npassed, 0 skipped. The local test database holds non-demo accounts, so the\nserver arm ran against a throwaway database that was dropped afterwards.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"va