ers/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/fe285ee55fa0c2c65498388388f308a0b5b7c342","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKGZlMjg1ZWU1NWZhMGMyYzY1NDk4Mzg4Mzg4ZjMwOGEwYjViN2MzNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/5e6f4fdfb56bece04acefe524dd7d25a7cf4455c","sha":"5e6f4fdfb56bece04acefe524dd7d25a7cf4455c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/5e6f4fdfb56bece04acefe524dd7d25a7cf4455c"}],"sha":"fe285ee55fa0c2c65498388388f308a0b5b7c342","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/fe285ee55fa0c2c65498388388f308a0b5b7c342"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/5e6f4fdfb56bece04acefe524dd7d25a7cf4455c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:17:56Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:17:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(docs): cut README to the pitch, and guard the cut (#112)\n\nREADME carried 183 lines that CLAUDE.md already carried with the reasons attached —\n*Design direction*, *Repo layout*, *Getting started*, *Tests and quality gate*,\n*Signing in*, *Dual mount* and *Deployment*. Nobody reads it, so it is now the shop\nwindow only: *What it does* and *Stack*.\n\nNothing was lost. The repo tree was a description `ls` regenerates. The `AUTH_SECRET`\none-liner is in `.env.example` with the 32-character minimum, the Vercel-every-scope\nrule and the rotation behaviour that README omitted. The setup commands moved into\n*Local development*, which until now stated rules about commands it did not show.\n\nThree pointers in CLAUDE.md aimed into the deleted sections and are repaired; the\nmaster map now says README is the pitch only, and says not to restore a section to it.\nThe private-notes bullet also stopped cataloguing files the repo cannot see — a\ncatalogue that goes stale invisibly is the same failure one level up.\n\n**The guard, because markdown is this gate''s blind spot.** `ruff`, `tsc`, `mypy` and\n`test_comment_budget.py` all read source only, so this cleanup could have been undone\nby one well-meaning \"the README is missing a Getting started section\" edit with nothing\ngoing red. `tests/test_docs_layout.py` pins README''s two sections and its line cap, and\nrefuses any ten-word run of prose present in both README and CLAUDE.md. The arm that\nchecks CLAUDE.md''s *citations* of README went into `test_claude_md_claims.py`, which\nalready owns every claim that file makes — a second citation-checker elsewhere would be\nthe duplication this PR deletes.\n\nThe duplication arm ships with an EMPTY allowlist and no ratchet or deadline, which is\nonly possible because README is clean today. That stops being true the next time either\nfile grows.\n\n`test_comment_budget.py` caught the new guards'' own comments (five over cap). Trimmed\nrather than registered: the ratchet only goes down.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e9ca4334d04d60076daa99e7d828e0b8df65068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/3e9ca4334d04d60076daa99e7d828e0b8df65068"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/5e6f4fdfb56bece04acefe524dd7d25a7cf4455c","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e9ca4334d04d60076daa99e7d828e0b8df65068\nparent d1911d101bee7dc12450d171b1a292915f2aadfb\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788365876 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788365876 +0200\n\nchore(docs): cut README to the pitch, and guard the cut (#112)\n\nREADME carried 183 lines that CLAUDE.md already carried with the reasons attached —\n*Design direction*, *Repo layout*, *Getting started*, *Tests and quality gate*,\n*Signing in*, *Dual mount* and *Deployment*. Nobody reads it, so it is now the shop\nwindow only: *What it does* and *Stack*.\n\nNothing was lost. The repo tree was a description `ls` regenerates. The `AUTH_SECRET`\none-liner is in `.env.example` with the 32-character minimum, the Vercel-every-scope\nrule and the rotation behaviour that README omitted. The setup commands moved into\n*Local development*, which until now stated rules about commands it did not show.\n\nThree pointers in CLAUDE.md aimed into the deleted sections and are repaired; the\nmaster map now says README is the pitch only, and says not to restore a section to it.\nThe private-notes bullet also stopped cataloguing files the repo cannot see — a\ncatalogue that goes stale invisibly is the same failure one level up.\n\n**The guard, because markdown is this gate''s blind spot.** `ruff`, `tsc`, `mypy` and\n`test_comment_budget.py` all read source only, so this cleanup could have been undone\nby one well-meaning \"the README is missing a Getting started section\" edit with nothing\ngoing red. `tests/test_docs_layout.py` pins README''s two sections and its line cap, and\nrefuses any ten-word run of prose present in both README and CLAUDE.md. The arm that\nchecks CLAUDE.md''s *citations* of README went into `test_claude_md_claims.py`, which\nalready owns every claim that file makes — a second citation-checker elsewhere would be\nthe duplication this PR deletes.\n\nThe duplication arm ships with an EMPTY allowlist and no ratchet or deadline, which is\nonly possible because README is clean today. That stops being true the next time either\nfile grows.\n\n`test_comment_budget.py` caught the new guards'' own comments (five over cap). Trimmed\nrather than registered: the ratchet only goes down.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmEw0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn08QAFHKd0Wbq4MIc59/aKc7EGzQ\n6jGkBb9bL8+w0TizUYgGklm6F4+8NO802/ma0v6L86huzrMFlzBBvqfg45NnTeDj\nGUABcXYT57jfea2bXfVrIgV4DjGVpbA+aEKtqc1QR9uWsMLme0ZkQ8s4hafl/nVS\nrB1jgnAsB/vYZvMQWXA/N8yvZ/WDPmkajpjegvdOSmAY37Y4ic4Jl5XBgFs4gILh\nzquEx0JJUf9KJO8PGrpQ0wCRlXc8kHuL6QFW20PgzxrIwlKGMjb1RVlO/p5qkC3c\nrp/mKJFyeJ5EYpABEGyosHRuAvhSJRIeV4f0MkYsroNcdkXu6ogdI0k2vVL1sXnn\no2bnrgBcwIrejy4ipCKL7dgoNFkh4H6xMI+C10Q1TeatzDWnLUjRHueyX2k0sByq\nz53RsXTzB8jKmFyMoniigftJ3fb/Dr534RGig+C5uIjAzhW8e3UaZhP8RW0cJK/h\nKaqndOPQUPvO+5oOzBswxtCsdXqc9odA6gXVHS+kUdSlRRy7onzpLzEIh4/KmcmH\nnxQVrTT4Cq1tMnNNNgfnlfvQo+n2fFVXHVT05+uisQaYQ9SmU3T3Qne5gkOoiMuo\njpjZPODvlhqbaL76hwyHpP1APMPsxBVdhJqubYIlmjaIAZ4AXpmM+dtDetStOhBO\nNUgw6Iv8ghQGYujbvggb\n=kfM0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T16:17:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/5e6f4fdfb56bece04acefe524dd7d25a7cf4455c","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDVlNmY0ZmRmYjU2YmVjZTA0YWNlZmU1MjRkZDdkMjVhN2NmNDQ1NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/d1911d101bee7dc12450d171b1a292915f2aadfb","sha":"d1911d101bee7dc12450d171b1a292915f2aadfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/d1911d101bee7dc12450d171b1a292915f2aadfb"}],"sha":"5e6f4fdfb56bece04acefe524dd7d25a7cf4455c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/5e6f4fdfb56bece04acefe524dd7d25a7cf4455c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/d1911d101bee7dc12450d171b1a292915f2aadfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T14:49:46Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T14:49:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(session): show what is still owed, and make \"completed\" mean every item done (#111)\n\nCloses #82. The reporting half of partial completion shipped in v8; what was left was\nthe generator question nobody had answered. Kilian''s answer: nothing happens in the plan.\nA shortfall is neither carried forward nor does it extend a phase — it surfaces on\n`/session` instead.\n\nThe screen is now, top to bottom: this week''s calendar, what is still owed from earlier\nin the week, today, and the next session. Each owed session is a full card carrying its\nown completion band — red when nothing was logged, amber when some was — and each is\nstartable until it is done. Restarting one seeds the items the server already holds every\nset for, so a session three-quarters finished no longer reopens as untouched.\n\n**\"Completed\" is a property of the items, not of the Finish button.** An item is done or\nnot done; skipped and never-started are the same result. A session is completed only when\nevery item is done, and only then does it leave the three offer sections and stop being\nrestartable. `planned_session.status` still means \"Finish was pressed\" and no user-facing\nword is derived from it — that was the defect: a session skipped through and finished read\n\"Completed\" in the week calendar. The server''s done predicate is now \"every prescribed set\nof the block is logged\" rather than \"at least one\", which needs no stored item state\nbecause pressing Done or letting the clock run logs all of a block''s sets.\n\nTwo pre-existing bugs found on the way and fixed here:\n\n- `dropUnflushed` identified a block''s sets by an ordinal window, but ordinals come off a\n  global ceiling — so a set minted for a later block could fall inside an earlier block''s\n  window and be silently discarded while still unsent. It now filters on\n  `prescribed_set_id` membership. Acked sets are still left alone (#81 unchanged).\n- `GET /api/sessions/completion` answered for stood-down plans, whose rows consume the\n  response''s row cap and could push live sessions out of the answer. It takes an optional\n  `plan_id`; absent, its behaviour is unchanged.\n\nNo schema change and no migration. `RUN_VERSION` 4 → 5, so a persisted run from the\nprevious shape is discarded rather than misread.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d89107809319cde6fd14f58445e6310267b36b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/2d89107809319cde6fd14f58445e6310267b36b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/d1911d101bee7dc12450d171b1a292915f2aadfb","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d89107809319cde6fd14f58445e6310267b36b7\nparent 092eb0c96f076e8b24408ab459e9d6f719ba10be\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788360586 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788360586 +0200\n\nfeat(session): show what is still owed, and make \"completed\" mean every item done (#111)\n\nCloses #82. The reporting half of partial completion shipped in v8; what was left was\nthe generator question nobody had answered. Kilian''s answer: nothing happens in the plan.\nA shortfall is neither carried forward nor does it extend a phase — it surfaces on\n`/session` instead.\n\nThe screen is now, top to bottom: this week''s calendar, what is still owed from earlier\nin the week, today, and the next session. Each owed session is a full card carrying its\nown completion band — red when nothing was logged, amber when some was — and each is\nstartable until it is done. Restarting one seeds the items the server already holds every\nset for, so a session three-quarters finished no longer reopens as untouched.\n\n**\"Completed\" is a property of the items, not of the Finish button.** An item is done or\nnot done; skipped and never-started are the same result. A session is completed only when\nevery item is done, and only then does it leave the three offer sections and stop being\nrestartable. `planned_session.status` still means \"Finish was pressed\" and no user-facing\nword is derived from it — that was the defect: a session skipped through and finished read\n\"Completed\" in the week calendar. The server''s done predicate is now \"every prescribed set\nof the block is logged\" rather than \"at least one\", which needs no stored item state\nbecause pressing Done or letting the clock run logs all of a block''s sets.\n\nTwo pre-existing bugs found on the way and fixed here:\n\n- `dropUnflushed` identified a block''s sets by an ordinal window, but ordinals come off a\n  global ceiling — so a set minted for a later block could fall inside an earlier block''s\n  window and be silently discarded while still unsent. It now filters on\n  `prescribed_set_id` membership. Acked sets are still left alone (#81 unchanged).\n- `GET /api/sessions/completion` answered for stood-down plans, whose rows consume the\n  response''s row cap and could push live sessions out of the answer. It takes an optional\n  `plan_id`; absent, its behaviour is unchanged.\n\nNo schema change and no migration. `RUN_VERSION` 4 → 5, so a persisted run from the\nprevious shape is discarded rather than misread.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmDeKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAchsQAJUCXly/oudgmlnFlDfGDLhh\ndm7B1HuXEQ1EFdjLfnYGteVfZN79LRMyh8mxexdAi1LPPcQIB2jDuNKA5dlXRLBR\ndQE1SYu2iRChAyhjso0IQdjzxpAzt5ESFKqbXaHwQyTULmbcRNa7UMXJib775EvG\n1WiNNH0UP83VGobbPfcHaLUuqCZnzEvIazXevwxcEQSIMN2JnVav8tx2tw5YTryh\n2tKGck3m9S51fw/PDSGJIn5+N/SLdQShzDaSLd7oxlFCPhfZChRUvtfQNVl+EgPk\ngqL47FC94PaGeaSeuZfROez/7I3ywqbuLtfr0w2OI5JmevYn0lf5sGg8hTXezAkD\n4EXW1M+mUz9EiXHtcgxBGw3LBxO675ya4UHiTDqcZTr2YZYnqvuJLFsh34lbDYE/\ntmXXC9gOjgYT2vYq9JKjFU6qtN8MbXA7eXIUFvXpbQ0comnEZlYPUldoBg5AKl5R\nTcNXyfHvV+iPby91wRHM4S+QJukITJjNmXqwtTVYZy5hjlCl3k0dJ62DCeOQtTST\nL40WkdMZibfzTJrdH+HEz6FJx9lYgFI/oWtqGhQe277GaVkDdTSBjviOFixERTyo\nJZROwWio3uJ3vEOvmRZTSwISIozfTsIWAso3WbuCpcBX7Se5aULlvyIMB3TF3jP5\nxmE1inXQdeJO858GHNSw\n=Qa3e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T14:49:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/