mc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T13:02:36Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"chore(release): v8.0.0 — session logging, the session player, climbing-first plans, and the plan calendar\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f5d9c9cd4cfd1ffbb062aaba5b87099eeec5bc36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/f5d9c9cd4cfd1ffbb062aaba5b87099eeec5bc36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/918b0445dbc298c2a7c043d575add81df985c212","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/918b0445dbc298c2a7c043d575add81df985c212","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDkxOGIwNDQ1ZGJjMjk4YzJhN2MwNDNkNTc1YWRkODFkZjk4NWMyMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/c8382d61fa065e30465a5c754d82689ada5d1451","sha":"c8382d61fa065e30465a5c754d82689ada5d1451","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/c8382d61fa065e30465a5c754d82689ada5d1451"}],"sha":"918b0445dbc298c2a7c043d575add81df985c212","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/918b0445dbc298c2a7c043d575add81df985c212"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/c8382d61fa065e30465a5c754d82689ada5d1451/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T13:01:29Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T13:01:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: key the vocabulary cache on the build id, and stop shipping a stale bundle (#108)\n\nTwo halves of the same deploy problem: for up to an hour after a release, some\nclients ran new code against old data and others old code against a new server.\n\n`GET /api/vocabulary` is served `private, max-age=3600` and the client fetch passes\nno `cache` option, so the browser answered from its own cache without contacting\nthe server. PR #94 added `plan_goal` and `phase_guide` and `PhaseGuide.tsx` maps\n`phase_guide` unguarded, so a pre-deploy body threw a TypeError on `/plan` and in\nthe session brief. The request now carries `?v=${BUILD_ID}`, the pattern\n`/api/library` has used since the same problem bit the exercise library; the server\nhandler mirrors the library''s bounded `v` param, which moves the OpenAPI document\nand so regenerates `schema.ts`.\n\n`registerType` moves from `prompt` to `autoUpdate`, so an old bundle no longer sits\nin a client until someone accepts a prompt. That makes the whole update-prompt path\ndead — `UpdateBar`, `updatePrompt.ts`, `update-bar.scss`, the `update-bar-metrics`\nmixin and the `body:has()` height reservation are removed, and the registration is\nnow a plain `registerSW()` in `pwa/register.ts`.\n\nBumps to 7.10.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"11baecfbeecee8839a433e859af5514090811ec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/11baecfbeecee8839a433e859af5514090811ec3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/c8382d61fa065e30465a5c754d82689ada5d1451","verification":{"payload":"tree 11baecfbeecee8839a433e859af5514090811ec3\nparent 98cb0e727a786d656adf6dee92a7617588ea5c1c\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788267689 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788267689 +0200\n\nfix: key the vocabulary cache on the build id, and stop shipping a stale bundle (#108)\n\nTwo halves of the same deploy problem: for up to an hour after a release, some\nclients ran new code against old data and others old code against a new server.\n\n`GET /api/vocabulary` is served `private, max-age=3600` and the client fetch passes\nno `cache` option, so the browser answered from its own cache without contacting\nthe server. PR #94 added `plan_goal` and `phase_guide` and `PhaseGuide.tsx` maps\n`phase_guide` unguarded, so a pre-deploy body threw a TypeError on `/plan` and in\nthe session brief. The request now carries `?v=${BUILD_ID}`, the pattern\n`/api/library` has used since the same problem bit the exercise library; the server\nhandler mirrors the library''s bounded `v` param, which moves the OpenAPI document\nand so regenerates `schema.ts`.\n\n`registerType` moves from `prompt` to `autoUpdate`, so an old bundle no longer sits\nin a client until someone accepts a prompt. That makes the whole update-prompt path\ndead — `UpdateBar`, `updatePrompt.ts`, `update-bar.scss`, the `update-bar-metrics`\nmixin and the `body:has()` height reservation are removed, and the registration is\nnow a plain `registerSW()` in `pwa/register.ts`.\n\nBumps to 7.10.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlsypCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfdsQADUj7TitR3fAoFrXpd+73CzI\nzY6PK0sj7IzT3m8WJpP54OMXhnDH8Laa0y8OPSGGESYkFh+FPe8bgt8F3kBJRIao\nLfwyyQJ9zrnyvAg0zXXu0nlbtMifOL4RXHJpHo+JHkUybY1n2nFsWe2UVYghNIzz\nzXf2YZQD+T1Dx1xgEgWpBkbG7bE6l+Zir4E8ZpbIrTV/aBsm+pTcmOs6AzmegCO4\nUuYaB7mgzpuO6Y0AMycV8vzt/rGONT+n7wevYw3XMzqaMraHuivGvgFayn1fktRq\n4kOhT2q5TL9Ta8CC0FxvfbZfhAcoCLkH3SZZm9k3sfJOlUcZyF79E+9bvH4cz44/\nP8x8neVss6HPU2Qw/vEOBWxkElBnfBlOIex92xW2YXeFcaqtuGTPc36vE708d5DP\njLaxIWd5+ESNQO11UlhdgVkHx8lOLfCegWjW+d6zJoWFWpiuytXLg6FyQV5k2kFz\nQhC/IxR6wK3R+QYnMX5IyRoLx0JcOUnhzSmjln26Tzc0mbOOCl2BEKoNY7PDOhXl\n2sGBGyvgYnHvtXGKCFQkmp4Jk5GQGgRrMkgi1iyPhfMXBDsy50sIr4TE+a969gC7\ngbdeRqUV80ca6ApD5KBuTIPLyvIxlNGadutOQd+7jPMsNPkqKgikpKPU4m9tTlSn\nDXwZil6hAPOhp7Nv5/JL\n=Og1j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T13:01:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/c8382d61fa065e30465a5c754d82689ada5d1451","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKGM4MzgyZDYxZmEwNjVlMzA0NjVhNWM3NTRkODI2ODlhZGE1ZDE0NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/98cb0e727a786d656adf6dee92a7617588ea5c1c","sha":"98cb0e727a786d656adf6dee92a7617588ea5c1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/98cb0e727a786d656adf6dee92a7617588ea5c1c"}],"sha":"c8382d61fa065e30465a5c754d82689ada5d1451","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/c8382d61fa065e30465a5c754d82689ada5d1451"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/98cb0e727a786d656adf6dee92a7617588ea5c1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T11:38:14Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T11:38:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: name the four screen sizes as container breakpoints (#99) (#107)\n\nThe four sizes Kilian specified now live in one place, `web/src/styles/_sizes.scss`:\ntablet 48rem, desktop 64rem, big 75rem, with mobile (350px) as the unqueried base.\n\nSass variables interpolated into the prelude, not custom properties: a query prelude\nis parsed before custom-property substitution, so `@container ct-app (min-inline-size:\nvar(--bp))` is an \"Invalid media query\" build failure, not merely unidiomatic. rem\nrather than px so the layout follows a reader who raised their default font size.\n\nContainer, never viewport. The federated mount is a narrow panel inside kilianmc.com''s\nwide window, so a width `@media` there reports the host and would hand a ~600px panel\nthe big-screen layout.\n\nNothing was migrated onto the scale. Every existing `34rem` is a MEASUREMENT — 544px\nfalls inside the Mobile band, so the only candidate is tablet, which would delay the\ntwo-column bento, the two-up profile choices and the week table''s full exercise names\nby 224px of app width. `_landing.scss`''s `46rem` is `--ct-measure` spelled literally.\n`_chrome.scss`''s nav thresholds stay exempt, per \"make the buttons appear as soon as\nthey fit\". Each exemption is named with its reason in `_sizes.scss` so the next reader\ndoes not \"finish the job\".\n\nThe plan timeline and phase week table now use the width via a new `.ct-app__wide`.\nNot the bleed column: the week table is `main > section > details > table` and a\n`<details>`'' light children sit behind a shadow slot, so they are the grid items of\nnothing. `.ct-app__wide` is intrinsic and therefore depth-independent, sized with\n`100cqi` — the nearest query container is `.ct-app` itself, which is the app''s own box\nin both mounts, and unlike the `50% - 50vw` idiom it cannot produce a scrollbar.\n\nGuarded on both sides, since the invariant is a rule about width questions and not\nabout CSS: no width `@media` in any `.scss`, and no width `matchMedia` in a shipped\n`.ts`/`.tsx`. The latter judges the query text, never the call, so the five legitimate\n`prefers-color-scheme` / `prefers-reduced-motion` / `display-mode` uses pass. Both were\nshown failing before being restored.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9688b1d136943bb5c6866d874fc6e586211ab02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/e9688b1d136943bb5c6866d874fc6e586211ab02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/98cb0e727a786d656adf6dee92a7617588ea5c1c","verification":{"payload":"tree e9688b1d136943bb5c6866d874fc6e586211ab02\nparent c601ca0dbcdbaa69b433cd08b3e053d7e0e2f285\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1788262694 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788262694 +0200\n\nfeat: name the four screen sizes as container breakpoints (#99) (#107)\n\nThe four sizes Kilian specified now live in one place, `web/src/styles/_sizes.scss`:\ntablet 48rem, desktop 64rem, big 75rem, with mobile (350px) as the unqueried base.\n\nSass variables interpolated into the prelude, not custom properties: a query prelude\nis parsed before custom-property substitution, so `@container ct-app (min-inline-size:\nvar(--bp))` is an \"Invalid media query\" build failure, not merely unidiomatic. rem\nrather than px so the layout follows a reader who raised their default font size.\n\nContainer, never viewport. The federated mount is a narrow panel inside kilianmc.com''s\nwide window, so a width `@media` there reports the host and would hand a ~600px panel\nthe big-screen layout.\n\nNothing was migrated onto the scale. Every existing `34rem` is a MEASUREMENT — 544px\nfalls inside the Mobile band, so the only candidate is tablet, which would delay the\ntwo-column bento, the two-up profile choices and the week table''s full exercise names\nby 224px of app width. `_landing.scss`''s `46rem` is `--ct-measure` spelled literally.\n`_chrome.scss`''s nav thresholds stay exempt, per \"make the buttons appear as soon as\nthey fit\". Each exemption is named with its reason in `_sizes.scss` so the next reader\ndoes not \"finish the job\".\n\nThe plan timeline and phase week table now use the width via a new `.ct-app__wide`.\nNot the bleed column: the week table is `main > section > details > table` and a\n`<details>`'' light children sit behind a shadow slot, so they are the grid items of\nnothing. `.ct-app__wide` is intrinsic and therefore depth-independent, sized with\n`100cqi` — the nearest query container is `.ct-app` itself, which is the app''s own box\nin both mounts, and unlike the `50% - 50vw` idiom it cannot produce a scrollbar.\n\nGuarded on both sides, since the invariant is a rule about width questions and not\nabout CSS: no width `@media` in any `.scss`, and no width `matchMedia` in a shipped\n`.ts`/`.tsx`. The latter judges the query text, never the call, so the five legitimate\n`prefers-color-scheme` / `prefers-reduced-motion` / `display-mode` uses pass. Both were\nshown failing before being restored.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply