pos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/5e4f6065cc3fd3cc48ddc5862ccb30d40b87da98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:04:20Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:04:20Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"chore: requote the enabled-gating citation after the react-query rename\n\n5.102.8 merges `resolveStaleTime` and `resolveQueryBoolean` into one\n`resolveQueryValue` with an identical body, which removed the construct\n`libraryCitations.test.ts` cites. Verified by a full-file diff of 5.102.2\nagainst the installed 5.102.8, not a grep: every `enabled` decision site in\n`queryObserver.js` still gates `!== false`, and `#shouldScheduleTimer` now\ngates the stale-timeout path that 5.102.2 left ungated. So the claim the\ncitation carries is unchanged and only the literal name moved.\n\n`CLAUDE.md` was citing `queryObserver.js:445/451/461` two lines above the rule\nbanning line numbers, and those numbers resolve to nothing in the ~340-line\nmodern build. Nothing guards CLAUDE.md''s library citations, so it rotted\nsilently.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"41d1953a61df039c581b2ad632a71f883dedfe15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/41d1953a61df039c581b2ad632a71f883dedfe15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/5e4f6065cc3fd3cc48ddc5862ccb30d40b87da98","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},