html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/98bfc4e6bd3b6c50a2304e6cafa3bbb4d3e4c0c2","sha":"98bfc4e6bd3b6c50a2304e6cafa3bbb4d3e4c0c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/98bfc4e6bd3b6c50a2304e6cafa3bbb4d3e4c0c2"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/7c229dadbe635f9aa38d0fc891b7b36e96d0459b","sha":"7c229dadbe635f9aa38d0fc891b7b36e96d0459b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/7c229dadbe635f9aa38d0fc891b7b36e96d0459b"}],"sha":"7d5564f245ef706406721ce362b7bc1c9717cf69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/7d5564f245ef706406721ce362b7bc1c9717cf69"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/7c229dadbe635f9aa38d0fc891b7b36e96d0459b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:38:07Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:38:07Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"cleanup-step3\n\nTurn the two prose facts the migrations strip destroyed into a guard, and hold\nfuture revisions to the comment cap.\n\ntests/test_migration_revision_shape.py (new, AST-based, DB-free) enforces:\n- a CHECK constraint name must not be pre-derived. The naming convention\n  re-applies only to keys whose pattern contains %(constraint_name)s, which\n  today is `ck` alone — `uq`/`pk`/`fk`/`ix` names are taken literally. The\n  affected keys are derived from NAMING_CONVENTION, not hardcoded. Also covers\n  op.create_check_constraint and op.drop_constraint(type_=\"check\").\n- an enum must be the postgresql dialect''s ENUM with create_type=False.\n  sa.Enum accepts create_type with no error and no warning and drops it, so\n  the wrong class is refused outright rather than having its kwarg checked.\n\nBoth library premises are asserted against the installed packages, so a\ndependency bump fails there instead of making the guard vacuous. Permanent\npositive controls cover all three doubling shapes, the literal-name cases that\nmust stay clear, and a no-op arm that fails if either scan inspects nothing.\n\ntest_comment_budget.py: drop the migrations/versions skip so future revisions\nare budgeted. BASELINE_RATCHET and the allowlist are unchanged; 0004''s\ndowngrade docstring was trimmed to fit rather than allowlisted.\n\nCLAUDE.md: name the BASELINE_DEADLINE burn-down and the ratchet''s slack arm,\npoint at the new guard, and note migrations/versions is now in scope. The\nmilestone dates are not transcribed — read the constants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4fcf759c74bf103c973189762b28949e10f298b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/4fcf759c74bf103c973189762b28949e10f298b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/7c229dadbe635f9aa38d0fc891b7b36e96d0459b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signa