,"name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"feat(sessions): the session-logging API — one idempotent PUT\n\n`PUT /api/sessions/{client_uuid}` is the backend half of the session player\n(planned PR #15b). It is called at session start (empty `sets`), at any Tier-1\nmid-run moment, and at Finish — one shape, so there is no second request to\nforget to attach the outbox to, which is what makes CLAUDE.md''s piggyback rule\nstructural rather than a matter of discipline.\n\nNo Alembic revision: `activity`, `logged_session` and `logged_set` have existed\nsince `0004`. So no production migration and no approval gate.\n\nThree decisions the code cannot explain on its own, all recorded in CLAUDE.md''s\nnew \"Logging a session\" section:\n\n- **`sets` is a DELTA, not a replacement.** The route carries whatever the\n  outbox holds, i.e. the unsent tail, so replace semantics would make a mid-run\n  piggyback flush delete every set already persisted. Replace is also not\n  idempotent under an at-least-once outbox, where a late retry can land after a\n  newer request.\n- **`duration_minutes` only ever grows** (`GREATEST`), because `srpe_load` is a\n  generated column and a stale retry shortening a session would silently corrupt\n  training load. The cost: this route cannot shorten, so the diary''s edit path\n  (#12) must not reuse it.\n- **A logged set that names a different exercise than its prescription is a 422\n  and rejects the whole flush** — closing issue #62''s invariant 2. Accepting the\n  rest would write a plausible-looking lie, which is the thing that issue exists\n  to prevent.\n\nPartial completion (\"I did 2 of 3 parts\") is answerable by query rather than by\na column: block membership rides on `logged_set.prescribed_set_id`. `completed`\nmeans the user pressed Finish, not that everything was done.\n\nStatement count is bounded at 5 and independent of the set count. Ownership and\nthe exercise invariant are one UNION ALL statement for the whole batch; another\nuser''s id is indistinguishable from a missing one.\n\nCloses #62. Follow-ups filed: #79 (ascents), #80 (live-or-finished for off-plan\nruns), #81 (deleting a set), #82 (surfacing partial completion).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4bf865a080812c34a8c808412280445d1b2647ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/4bf865a080812c34a8c808412280445d1b2647ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/82b5d8066f6c55780b9ed244032810c7ad5b2e23","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/82b5d8066f6c55780b9ed244032810c7ad5b2e23","node_id":"C_kwDOT2NbNNoAKDgyYjVkODA2NmY2YzU1NzgwYjllZDI0NDAzMjgxMGM3YWQ1YjJlMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/9ec174602848fc789f98d43644d27b700c2704ba","sha":"9ec174602848fc789f98d43644d27b700c2704ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer