6f54a909626044ec93afbb5"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commit/f57692d797caa1ac547c44444893f05bcfe30c96","sha":"f57692d797caa1ac547c44444893f05bcfe30c96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/f57692d797caa1ac547c44444893f05bcfe30c96"}],"sha":"1b1dd6fa0881bfdace7124eea42f86f0c0287b86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/1b1dd6fa0881bfdace7124eea42f86f0c0287b86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/commits/f57692d797caa1ac547c44444893f05bcfe30c96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T13:57:37Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T13:57:37Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"docs: reconcile CLAUDE.md with the dependency bumps\n\nSwept the docs for claims the #67/#73 bumps falsified. Three findings.\n\n1. ESLint 10.8.1 -> 10.9.0 made one claim stale, and the block containing it carries\n   its own instruction: \"re-run the lint against a known-bad component to confirm the\n   rules still fire — a plugin that fails to register is SILENT, and an a11y lint that\n   checks nothing looks exactly like one that passes.\" Nobody had. So I planted a\n   component with four violations and confirmed jsx-a11y still fires on 10.9.0:\n   alt-text, anchor-is-valid, click-events-have-key-events,\n   no-static-element-interactions. The doc now NAMES those four rules instead of an\n   ESLint version — reproducible, and it does not rot on the next bump. Same move as\n   the construct citations.\n\n2. web/src/api/libraryCitations.test.ts was documented under the query-cache rule but\n   missing from the Testing policy''s list of invariant guards — the exact omission\n   that list''s own rule warns about (\"a guard nobody lists is a guard the next reader\n   deletes\").\n\n3. NOT stale, and worth recording so nobody \"fixes\" them: the FastAPI mentions read\n   \"since FastAPI 0.137\" and \"on by default since FastAPI 0.132\". Those are version\n   FLOORS, still true at the installed 0.141.1, and line 412 is a dated historical\n   defect. A floor and a dated fact do not rot; a current-state pin does. That is the\n   distinction the ESLint fix turns on.\n\nDuplication: checked both directions, cross-file and within-file, plus the one topic\nthe bumps touch. Zero. README''s Stack is the version list; CLAUDE.md''s dependency\npolicy is the pinning RULE and its two exceptions — different documents, not copies.\n\nGate: web 688 passed / 32 files, server 581 passed / 0 skipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab04cc2e22a2b0606a789fda90986c36f9f837b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/trees/ab04cc2e22a2b0606a789fda90986c36f9f837b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/climb-trainer/git/commits/f57692d797caa1ac547c44444893f05bcfe30c96","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"u