ix Migration Dry-Run / Backend Tests CI\n\nMerged origin/main into this branch:\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml: main had already independently added the\n  same \"zk-tests\" job content this branch''s diff collided with, which\n  left main with that job duplicated verbatim. Resolved by keeping one\n  copy of zk-tests and appending this branch''s new migration-dry-run\n  job after it, as originally authored.\n- backend/src/db/timescale.ts: kept this branch''s new dryRunMigrations\n  and getMigrationStatus functions; main had no competing changes here.\n\nFixed two bugs the merge/CI run surfaced:\n- dryRunMigrations ran every pending migration in its own\n  BEGIN/ROLLBACK, so a migration''s schema changes never persisted for\n  the next one in the same run — any migration depending on an earlier\n  one (e.g. 007_commitments_cursor_indexes.sql referencing\n  commitment_outcomes from 001_timescale_setup.sql) always failed with\n  \"relation does not exist\", regardless of whether the SQL was\n  actually correct. Switched to one outer transaction with a savepoint\n  per migration, matching what the existing code comment already\n  described.\n- The Migration Dry-Run job used plain postgres:16, which doesn''t have\n  the timescaledb extension 001_timescale_setup.sql requires (unlike\n  the real docker-compose stack, which uses\n  timescale/timescaledb:latest-pg16). Switched the CI service to the\n  same image so the dry-run is actually representative.\n- This branch''s own rename of 004_horizon_sse_cursors.sql ->\n  006_horizon_sse_cursors.sql (deduplicating a numbering collision\n  with 004_reputation_snapshots.sql) left a stale hardcoded path in\n  sse-indexer.test.ts pointing at the old filename, failing Backend\n  Tests. Updated both references.\n\nVerified locally: full backend build, `npm test` (all 3 suites), and\nmigrate-dry-run.js against a real timescale/timescaledb:latest-pg16\ncontainer — all 10 migrations now validate successfully.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonn