ropped when the\ncard''s lines are gone. Migration 0005 adds card_buy_overrides.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d22cb147b1e32900811ba8a239fb115cc79c4bdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gfilliere/family-tools/git/trees/d22cb147b1e32900811ba8a239fb115cc79c4bdd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gfilliere/family-tools/git/commits/fdafae7d23c877cc544b9d220a1e0d14bf0ff363","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1927105?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gfilliere","id":1927105,"login":"gfilliere","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjcxMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gfilliere/family-tools/commit/fdafae7d23c877cc544b9d220a1e0d14bf0ff363","node_id":"C_kwDOT2fim9oAKGZkYWZhZTdkMjNjODc3Y2M1NDRiOWQyMjBhMWUwZDE0YmYwZmYzNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gfilliere/family-tools/commit/dd4cb424a6793a5967556f3b0dfe2f5c7e48ce9e","sha":"dd4cb424a6793a5967556f3b0dfe2f5c7e48ce9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gfilliere/family-tools/commits/dd4cb424a6793a5967556f3b0dfe2f5c7e48ce9e"}],"sha":"fdafae7d23c877cc544b9d220a1e0d14bf0ff363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gfilliere/family-tools/commits/fdafae7d23c877cc544b9d220a1e0d14bf0ff363"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1927105?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gfilliere","id":1927105,"login":"gfilliere","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjcxMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gfilliere","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gfilliere/family-tools/commits/dd4cb424a6793a5967556f3b0dfe2f5c7e48ce9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:00:20Z","email":"guillaume.filliere@webedia-group.com","name":"Guillaume Filliere"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:00:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rebuild shopping list on a shared ingredient catalog (#8)\n\n* Preserve cookbook navigation in browser history\n\n* Rebuild shopping list on a shared ingredient catalog\n\nThe list mis-filed steak under Beverages (substring regex), duplicated\nbutter across g and ml, split chicken three ways, and dumped a third of\nevery recipe into Other. Root causes: aisle by substring match, free-form\nmodel canonical names per recipe, merge rules keyed on identical units,\nand merge-on-insert that destroyed provenance.\n\n- New packages/pantry: curated ingredient catalog (EN + DE aliases, aisle,\n  buying measure, densities), line parser (ranges, bullets, parenthetical\n  metric hints, package sizes, conjunctions and alternatives), word-boundary\n  matcher with longest-alias-wins, unit conversion into buying amounts.\n  Golden test over 279 real imported recipe lines: 0 unmatched.\n- List: one row per source line, aggregated at read time into one card per\n  ingredient with a summed buying total and per-recipe breakdown. Staples\n  collapse into a ''Check the pantry'' group. Aisle, staple and identity can\n  be corrected from the UI and are learned. Recipes can be removed as a\n  whole. Model fallback only for names the catalog does not know.\n- Cookbook: import parser and identity resolution use the shared catalog\n  first; ''Add to list'' now passes the original line and the aisle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Polish catalog display names and document the pantry package\n\nGeneric bucket entries (garlic powder, seasoning mixes, sauces) now show\nthe alias that matched instead of the bucket name. Bulk-bought items get\nplural display names. Pasta and rice are no longer treated as staples.\nText export pluralises counted items.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Learn corrections per spelling and keep legacy list tables\n\nA card reassignment now learns only the recipe''s own spelling (with\namounts and prep removed), never the catalog name, so correcting\n''grilled chicken'' does not redirect every chicken. Rows that resolve to\na skipped entry (water) no longer surface as cards. The migration keeps\ningredient_aisles and ingredient_aliases because CI applies migrations\nbefore the new Worker is live.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address review: split aisles, editable catalog, French support\n\n- Aisles: Meat / Fish & Seafood, Dairy / Eggs, Baking / Spices, as German\n  supermarkets shelve them. Legacy names are still accepted as hints.\n- Every catalog attribute (name, aisle, staple, buying unit, density,\n  piece weight, spellings) can be corrected at runtime from a new Catalog\n  view in the list app; corrections overlay the code seed and apply to\n  lines already on the list. Migration 0004.\n- Type-sensitive buckets (vinegar, cheese, pasta, rice, flour, beef, ...)\n  keep one card per matched alias instead of merging.\n- Dropped the catch-all vegetables entry.\n- French: units (c. à s., gousse, botte, pincée, boîte, cl, dl), number\n  words, qualifiers, elisions (d''ail), prep participles, flags, and French\n  aliases across the catalog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"522c30a4db0d2afaa4f7a0348c5715ac88c8b870","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gfilliere/family-tools/git/trees/522c30a4db0d2afaa4f7a0348c5715ac88c8b870"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gfilliere/family-tools/git/commits/dd4cb424a6793a5967556f3b0dfe2f5c7e48ce9e","verification":{"payload":"tree 522c30a4db0d2afaa4f7a0348c5715ac88c8b870\nparent 1e8f9de4d3b8f1398bcb69e1f76483af5915ba31\nauthor Guillaume Filliere <guillaume.filliere@webedia-group.com> 1789290020 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789290020 +0200\n\nRebuild shopping list on a shared ingredient catalog (#8)\n\n* Preserve cookbook navigation in browser history\n\n* Rebuild shopping list on a shared ingredient catalog\n\nThe list mis-filed steak under Beverages (substring regex), duplicated\nbutter across g and ml, split chicken three ways, and dumped a third of\nevery recipe into Other. Root causes: aisle by substring match, free-form\nmodel canonical names per recipe, merge rules keyed on identical units,\nand merge-on-insert that destroyed provenance.\n\n- New packages/pantry: curated ingredient catalog (EN + DE aliases, aisle,\n  buying measure, densities), line parser (ranges, bullets, parenthetical\n  metric hints, package sizes, conjunctions and alternatives), word-boundary\n  matcher with longest-alias-wins, unit conversion into buying amounts.\n  Golden test over 279 real imported recipe lines: 0 unmatched.\n- List: one row per source line, aggregated at read time into one card per\n  ingredient with a summed buying total and per-recipe breakdown. Staples\n  collapse into a ''Check the pantry'' group. Aisle, staple and identity can\n  be corrected from the UI and are learned. Recipes can be removed as a\n  whole. Model fallback only for names the catalog does not know.\n- Cookbook: import parser and identity resolution use the shared catalog\n  first; ''Add to list'' now passes the original line and the aisle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Polish catalog display names and document the pantry package\n\nGeneric bucket entries (garlic powder, seasoning mixes, sauces) now show\nthe alias that matched instead of the bucket name. Bulk-bought items get\nplural display names. Pasta and rice are no longer treated as staples.\nText export pluralises counted items.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Learn corrections per spelling and keep legacy list tables\n\nA card reassignment now learns only the recipe''s own spelling (with\namounts and prep removed), never the catalog name, so correcting\n''grilled chicken'' does not redirect every chicken. Rows that resolve to\na skipped entry (water) no longer surface as cards. The migration keeps\ningredient_aisles and ingredient_aliases because CI applies migrations\nbefore the new Worker is live.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address review: split aisles, editable catalog, French support\n\n- Aisles: Meat / Fish & Seafood, Dairy / Eggs, Baking / Spices, as German\n  supermarkets shelve them. Legacy names are still accepted as hints.\n- Every catalog attribute (name, aisle, staple, buying unit, density,\n  piece weight, spellings) can be corrected at runtime from a new Catalog\n  view in the list app; corrections overlay the code seed and apply to\n  lines already on the list. Migration 0004.\n- Type-sensitive buckets (vinegar, cheese, pasta, rice, flour, beef, ...)\n  keep one card per matched alias instead of merging.\n- Dropped the catch-all vegetables entry.\n- French: units (c. à s., gousse, botte, pincée, boîte, cl, dl), number\n  words, qualifiers, elisions (d''ail), prep participles, flags, and French\n  aliases across the catalog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpmYkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkpUQAFv3g23gHH++NXkVHwpAsj4Q\nJaUxKx8/N0vTcKc3iFQnCSRdVOkaDUn/CMvsd76Ylqb3CHtlxGS+qexYWe6Gnk32\n1k7VfBwbf3s+4HDSA7GiBEv70YEdRSzNFYLJb/S8+SISZSZNdlyvT2zEwwrsCedl\nYs//XB0Aro3WtB8+FydZUEdFG1c6EPrExrWP79brNtl7xaQSNRqN9gAnglZAbB/v\nOSzVURbGNE6jhc8L9nfu3A1CfNFNbwAw6T4RlSAWG52kNarMriT3BZJDqbX3yRVn\nPDAjAP1qkulDuNMlg/nvK1jFhOxIe8SrqXbPa942OuzFQqpmE4Zbn019H2PXqyXb\nl6aBwUCrtwdBckLXkmMLixNMLOkwJBhGq92LRHzyJ/QnoWil9aLpnKXf5aTBtP+4\npBFj5lI/tLY26yPWmvv+ZR5QZfJDcr9LebO/qSbtu+qmT7ViOS2IYkclIwEWnxDw\nNc5REO2sSyGywYssrnsbRHIFNpxyJBIWkWrmNPSHGNS/qR2DtOeOdyfam7oiwOAN\nzT6jgEGsL9FfPZL50LzAAtU5nHYyiX/Y/xn+zklLRfdzlGTSrEy2ijkYiAJQzXcu\njA9kXulY8FHfg8wuFm/1g2T6Q7q4f5ZStJO0awj15AEMwrINAge5WidClbC2EEDU\nAT45C+q3QG49Hag4dNB0\n=KcNk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T09:00:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNl