"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kannan-santharam/kannan-portfolio/commits/41cf6cbcec1fe4951505c675599dba69211a3a70/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T05:23:34Z","email":"kannan.santharam4@gmail.com","name":"Kannan Appiya Santharam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T05:23:34Z","email":"kannan.santharam4@gmail.com","name":"Kannan Appiya Santharam"},"message":"feat(resume): lead with outcomes, add the Dubai photo, and fix the SEO stamping bug\n\nResume\n- Key Achievements rewritten as seven active-voice lines that map to\n  leadership, revenue, full-stack reach, AI-native work, performance and\n  hiring, so a recruiter gets the whole story in the first ten seconds.\n- Bullets tightened; the accounts, MCP server and load-time lines carry\n  their business numbers; grammar pass (misplaced modifiers, dangling\n  clauses, Oxford comma) applied after two independent reviews.\n- Dubai edition gets a circular photo in the top-right corner, drawn as an\n  image so text extraction is unchanged; the header stays centred on the\n  full width. India edition has no photo. Both fit two pages.\n- Tagline separators are pipes, which parsers tokenise more reliably.\n- Dubai asks for the same title as India.\n\nSite\n- Milestones grid re-prioritised to match: ARR per account, team and\n  hiring merged, 70% load time; hero rotates two photos with a hover-pause\n  carousel; AI showcase and timeline copy aligned to the resume.\n- vite.config: SEO stamping used string replacers, so \"$100K to $1M\" in\n  the description was read as $1 backreferences. This corrupted the meta\n  tag on every page and left Dubai relocation copy in the built India\n  head. Function replacers fix both.\n- Large photo sources gitignored; only the 97KB web JPG is tracked.","tree":{"sha":"63bc39fee