ent.com/u/42336714?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kannan-santharam","id":42336714,"login":"kannan-santharam","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzM2NzE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kannan-santharam/kannan-portfolio/commits/b83735793c4f025bb7ca85f18410b1c56d0eeaf1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T05:17:43Z","email":"kannan.santharam4@gmail.com","name":"Kannan Appiya Santharam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T05:17:43Z","email":"kannan.santharam4@gmail.com","name":"Kannan Appiya Santharam"},"message":"feat(resume): state business impact in numbers, and stop the site contradicting it\n\nDubai hiring advice is consistent that outcomes in numbers beat descriptions\nof work. Nine of seventeen experience bullets carried no number at all, and\nseveral that did carried engineering output rather than a result: a count of\ntest cases, a count of packages. Every figure below came from Kannan; none\nwere invented.\n\n- Regression: 6 hours of manual testing across the product to a 40-minute\n  automated run in Jenkins, with the 300+ Playwright cases as supporting\n  detail rather than the headline\n- Build: \"hundreds of engineering hours per month\" was wrong by roughly an\n  order of magnitude. 115 seconds saved, five starts a day, fifteen\n  engineers, is about 50 engineer-hours a month, which is what it now says\n- Hiring: 9 engineers hired across both employers at 90% retention, the\n  strongest people metric available and previously absent\n- Design system: 30+ reusable components across 40 to 50+ pages and\n  sections. The claim of a UI SDK adopted across product teams is gone\n- Page load keeps 5s to 1.5s and gains the outcome, slowness-related\n  support tickets removed\n- Freshworks: 100+ mid-market and enterprise accounts over four years, the\n  Jira integration adopted by 4,000+ Freshworks customers, and the DocuSign\n  integration credited with the $500K ARR deal it unlocked\n- Platform scale is now millions of customer endpoints. The 4,000+ customer\n  count read small and belonged to the employer, not to him\n- Team size settles at 6 everywhere rather than a 4 to 6 range\n\nThe header leads with Dubai so a resume parser, which takes the first\ngeographic entity it resolves and stops, records the UAE rather than\nChennai. The relocation stays in the same line and the sponsorship\nrequirement is one line below, so nothing is concealed from a human.\n\nThe summary drops a repeat of the title printed directly above it and gives\narchitecture equal weight to AI: a 12-package monorepo, design systems,\nbuild and runtime performance.\n\nAn audit of the site against the resume found one genuine contradiction:\nthe metrics grid still advertised a reusable UI SDK adopted across product\nteams, the exact claim removed from the resume, in the most-read block on\nthe page. It now describes the design system the resume actually claims.\nindex.html carried a stale team size that the build plugin happened to\noverwrite, which made it invisible rather than harmless.\n\nThe hero was the weakest telling of the story on a page that links to the\nstrongest, so it now leads with the same numbers the CV does.","tree":{"sha":"2c7e638dcfcc266f6c2f4724f74fc9061f56cfea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kannan-santharam/kannan-portfolio/git/trees/2c7e638dcfcc266f6c2f4724f74fc9061f56cfea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kannan-santharam/kannan-portfolio/git/commits/b83735793c4f025bb7ca85f18410b1c56d0eeaf1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42336714?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kannan-santharam","id":42336714,"login":"kannan-santharam","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzM2NzE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kannan-santharam","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kannan-santharam/kannan-portfolio/commit/b83735793c4f025bb7ca85f18410b1c56d0eeaf1","node_id":"C_kwDOT2g0BNoAKGI4MzczNTc5M2M0ZjAyNWJiN2NhODVmMTg0MTBiMWM1NmQwZWVhZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kannan-santharam/kannan-portfolio/commit/d4b627c53b7412e03e9a2a71383b736fa58371c7","sha":"d4b627c53b7412e03e9a2a71383b736fa58371c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kannan-santharam/kannan-portfolio/commits/d4b627c53b7412e03e9a2a71383b736fa58371c7"}],"sha":"b83735793c4f025bb7