.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh/Provenance/commit/986bfad446c869c348dbae7c1b45fa4d2cbfc9c7","node_id":"C_kwDOT2lIzdoAKDk4NmJmYWQ0NDZjODY5YzM0OGRiYWU3YzFiNDVmYTRkMmNiZmM5Yzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh/Provenance/commit/44ea5009e4e12ef951bed1491dbe809d3c626c5d","sha":"44ea5009e4e12ef951bed1491dbe809d3c626c5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/44ea5009e4e12ef951bed1491dbe809d3c626c5d"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh/Provenance/commit/531b7513de19b3fe8d0ab5a09a22579f897938b2","sha":"531b7513de19b3fe8d0ab5a09a22579f897938b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/531b7513de19b3fe8d0ab5a09a22579f897938b2"}],"sha":"986bfad446c869c348dbae7c1b45fa4d2cbfc9c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/986bfad446c869c348dbae7c1b45fa4d2cbfc9c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143943640?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh","id":143943640,"login":"mohithhhh","node_id":"U_kgDOCJRn2A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/531b7513de19b3fe8d0ab5a09a22579f897938b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T17:41:56Z","email":"143943640+mohithhhh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mohithhhh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T17:41:56Z","email":"143943640+mohithhhh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mohithhhh"},"message":"Phase 4: Module B zero-shot statistical detector\n\napps/api (first module using a real generative LM, not just embeddings):\n- detectors/models.py: lazy-loaded gpt2 (performer, 124M) + distilgpt2\n  (observer, 82M) — small enough to run on a laptop CPU, same family so\n  they share a tokenizer (required for the cross-perplexity method below).\n- detectors/perplexity.py: three signals from one pass over both models —\n  Binoculars-style cross-perplexity (Hans et al. 2024, independently\n  reimplemented and recalibrated for this much smaller model pair rather\n  than reusing the paper''s 0.9015 threshold, which is calibrated for a\n  different, much larger pair), GLTR-style rank buckets (Gehrmann et al.\n  2019), and burstiness of per-sentence surprisal.\n- routers/detect.py: POST /detect/statistical.\n- scripts/calibrate_binoculars.py: committed, reproducible calibration —\n  8 original human-written sentences (written for this project, not\n  scraped) vs. 8 sentences gpt2 generated from itself (seed 0). Clean\n  separation: AI scores 0.09-0.23, human scores 0.29-0.73. Real numbers\n  now in docs/benchmark.md, not guessed.\n- 42 tests total (20 new): core stats (rank/perplexity/cross-perplexity/\n  burstiness), sentence splitting, and HTTP-level router tests including\n  one that regenerates gpt2''s own output to confirm the \"likely-ai\"\n  verdict path end-to-end, not just structural shape.\n\nTwo honest findings from actually testing this, both now in\ndocs/architecture.md and docs/limitations.md: perplexity-based detection\nmeasures predictability-to-this-specific-model, not humanness — a famous/\nmemorized phrase can score unpredictably (manual testing with a pangram\ndidn''t break it here, but the risk is real and inherent to the method,\nnot a bug); and Module B shares the base-model blind spot already\ndocumented for Module C.\n\napps/web: new /detect page — verdict card (Binoculars score, perplexity,\ncross-perplexity, top-10 fraction, burstiness), a GLTR per-token heatmap,\nand a per-sentence breakdown table. Verified end-to-end in a real browser\nagainst a live API server, both the likely-ai and likely-human verdict\npaths, zero console errors.\n\nInfra: torch + transformers added to apps/api (on macOS ARM, torch''s\nwheel is ~111MB with no bundled CUDA — much lighter than feared given\nPhase 0''s earlier disk crunch; net effect here was full venv 326MB→1.1GB\nand gpt2+distilgpt2 weights ~780MB on top of that under\n~/.cache/huggingface, monitored throughout, still comfortably within\nbudget). CI''s HF cache step now covers both Module F''s and Module B''s\nmodels under one key. pyproject.toml unaffected; models.py deliberately\ntypes transformers'' lazily-imported objects as Any rather than fighting\nits incomplete stubs. apps/api/README documents a real gotcha hit during\ndevelopment — a fully-downloaded model can still hang on a stalled\nHub network round-trip; HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 is the documented escape hatch.\n\nREADME/docs updated: Phase 4 checkbox, Module B architecture section,\nbenchmark numbers, limitations.\n\nAll checks pass: format/lint/typecheck/test/build across every TS\nworkspace (78 tests), ruff/mypy/pytest for apps/api (42 tests).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f66e453345f4a6da9b45815d1dc5a34f024cbc56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/git/trees/f66e453345f4a6da9b45815d1dc5a34f024cbc56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/git/commits/531b7513de19b3fe8d0ab5a09a22579f897938b2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143943640?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh","id":143943640,"login":"mohithhhh","node_id":"U_kgDOCJRn2A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh/Provenance/commit/531b7513de19b3fe8d0ab5a09a22579f897938b2","node_id":"C_kwDOT2lIzdoAKDUzMWI3NTEzZGUxOWIzZmU4ZDBhYjVhMDlhMjI1NzlmODk3OTM4YjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh/Provenance/commit/3c054b6e4625475770eb83c5b6c3e36dfd21de53","sha":"3c054b6e4625475770eb83c5b6c3e36dfd21de53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/3c054b6e4625475770eb83c5b6c3e36dfd21de53"}],"sha":"531b7513de19b3fe8d0ab5a09a22579f897938b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/531b7513de19b3fe8d0ab5a09a22579f897938b2"},{"author":{"avatar_u