ns_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh/Provenance/commit/f55787f2dac1ad54a059da61acf1a1b5ed0b8169","node_id":"C_kwDOT2lIzdoAKGY1NTc4N2YyZGFjMWFkNTRhMDU5ZGE2MWFjZjFhMWI1ZWQwYjgxNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh/Provenance/commit/069276e2cbe9c0bf86f005e0d738c0c3d507b818","sha":"069276e2cbe9c0bf86f005e0d738c0c3d507b818","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/069276e2cbe9c0bf86f005e0d738c0c3d507b818"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh/Provenance/commit/986642da789925c8cb47c869fcefd9ca3f1d9dc9","sha":"986642da789925c8cb47c869fcefd9ca3f1d9dc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/986642da789925c8cb47c869fcefd9ca3f1d9dc9"}],"sha":"f55787f2dac1ad54a059da61acf1a1b5ed0b8169","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/f55787f2dac1ad54a059da61acf1a1b5ed0b8169"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143943640?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mohithhhh","id":143943640,"login":"mohithhhh","node_id":"U_kgDOCJRn2A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mohithhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/commits/986642da789925c8cb47c869fcefd9ca3f1d9dc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:56:17Z","email":"143943640+mohithhhh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mohithhhh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:56:17Z","email":"143943640+mohithhhh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mohithhhh"},"message":"Phase 2: Module A robustness + delta tradeoff analysis\n\npackages/watermark-core:\n- attacks.ts: four structural perturbations (substitute/delete/insert/\n  reorder), each a strength 0..1 fraction of words affected. Explicitly\n  documented as naive analogs, not real paraphrasing — a real paraphrase\n  attack is Module G''s job (Phase 7) and expected to be considerably more\n  damaging. 16 tests covering no-op at strength 0, requested-fraction\n  accuracy, determinism, category-preserving substitution, and multiset\n  preservation for reordering.\n- analysis.ts: sweep helpers (runRobustnessSweep, runMultiAttackSweep,\n  runDeltaTradeoffSweep) — pure orchestration over generate/attack/detect,\n  shared by both the UI and the benchmark script below. 7 tests.\n- scripts/robustness-benchmark.mjs: produces docs/benchmark.md''s numbers\n  from 30 seeded PRNG runs against the built package, so they''re exactly\n  reproducible rather than a one-off screenshot.\n\napps/web: new /watermark/robustness page — runs all four attacks against\none watermarked passage and charts z-score vs. attack strength, plus (for\nthe green-list scheme) two charts for the δ tradeoff: detection strength\nand a green-fraction distortion proxy vs. δ. Charts are a small\ndependency-free SVG line chart component following the dataviz skill''s\nmark specs (thin 2px lines, legend, gridlines, per-point tooltips, a\ntable-view fallback) with the skill''s validated default categorical\npalette wired through CSS custom properties in globals.css, dark-mode\naware. Verified end-to-end in a real browser, zero console errors.\n\ndocs/benchmark.md gets real Module A numbers (mean z-score and\nwatermarked-verdict rate per attack per strength; z-score and green\nfraction per δ) with exact reproduction instructions, replacing the\n\"planned\" stub. docs/architecture.md gets a Phase 2 design-notes section,\nincluding an honest note on what the distortion proxy is standing in for\n(no real perplexity/fluency model exists for this toy grammar). README''s\nPhase 2 checkbox is marked done.\n\nAlso: moved the sweep logic that started in apps/web into\npackages/watermark-core (it''s generic, pure, and now shared by the\nbenchmark script too, instead of being duplicated); unified the `Scheme`\ntype across chips.ts and the new analysis module instead of declaring it\ntwice; fixed the package''s ESLint config to recognize Node globals in\nscripts/**/*.mjs.\n\nHousekeeping: the working tree had been checked out to `mdk2` (an older\nbranch with no Phase 0/1 history) at the start of this session — switched\nback to `mdk`, which has everything and is what this commit continues.\n\nAll checks pass: format/lint/typecheck/test/build across every workspace\n(71 TS tests total), plus apps/api''s unaffected ruff/mypy/pytest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8a50290847f1c3fc399b76b61eb413fe187ab232","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/git/trees/8a50290847f1c3fc399b76b61eb413fe187ab232"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohithhhh/Provenance/git/commits/986642da789925c8cb47c869fcefd9ca3f1d9dc9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143943640?v=4","e