OTJhMDBlZjZhNjQzMTBmYTNiNGJmNzYwMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TiredRebel/LexTime/commit/abb8e1996d3f95070113bc7031fd18f025c2275c","sha":"abb8e1996d3f95070113bc7031fd18f025c2275c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TiredRebel/LexTime/commits/abb8e1996d3f95070113bc7031fd18f025c2275c"}],"sha":"3b04295903751692a00ef6a64310fa3b4bf76007","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TiredRebel/LexTime/commits/3b04295903751692a00ef6a64310fa3b4bf76007"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/601607?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TiredRebel","id":601607,"login":"TiredRebel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTYwNw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TiredRebel/LexTime/commits/d724e13b1a05258531ccd4fe25ea1c17b227d7e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T08:29:33Z","email":"dlsaus@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Saus"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T08:29:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"001 solution and schema (#1)\n\n* docs: specify local environment and schema (001)\n\n* docs: clarify local environment and schema spec (001)\n\n* docs: split feature 001 into solution-and-schema and bootstrap-and-seed\n\nThe /speckit-plan Constitution Check on 001-local-environment-schema failed P3\n(one evening per spec). The original covered four projects, the build and\ndocumentation gate, the schema and migration, the container definition, token\nvalidation, a health endpoint, a Testcontainers harness, a bootstrap script with\nreadiness polling and procedure application, deterministic generation of 400,000\nrows with verification, and token minting. That is not one evening.\n\nGovernance permits Complexity Tracking entries only for SHOULD principles, so a\nMUST failure is reworked rather than waived. Split along the original spec''s own\nuser story boundaries, so no requirement was rewritten to fit:\n\n  001-solution-and-schema  projects, build gate, schema, migration, compose file,\n                           auth boundary, health endpoint, test harness\n  002-bootstrap-and-seed   bootstrap script, seeding, verification, token minting\n\nSequential numbering rather than 001a/001b: create-new-feature.ps1 matches\n^(\\d{3,})- when scanning for the next number, so 001a-* would not match and the\nfollowing feature would collide back at 001. The rollup is now 003.\n\nTwo consequences worth recording. 001 satisfies P18 only partially by design -\nit leaves three manual commands, and the README states that rather than\npromising the two-command quickstart before 002 delivers it. And 001 FR-012\nrequires that WorkDate carry no check constraint, which is a requirement that\nsomething be absent; it has a positive test asserting a three-year-old date is\naccepted, so that adding the constraint later breaks a test instead of silently\nbreaking 002''s seed.\n\nCarries forward the bootstrap contract and the seeding, determinism, readiness,\nprocedure-application and token-minting research from the original planning run\ninto 002, to be validated by its own /speckit-plan rather than re-derived.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: remove career framing from PRD section 1\n\n* docs: remove personal framing from PRD and README\n\n* docs: generate tasks for 001 and remove personal framing\n\n* feat: solution, schema, health endpoint and access boundary (001)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4798c286e7efdc15f774be3dda168fbfebc08dd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TiredRebel/LexTime/git/trees/4798c286e7efdc15f774be3dda168fbfebc08dd7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TiredRebel/LexTime/git/commits/d724e13b1a05258531ccd4fe25ea1c17b227d7e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 4798c286e7efdc15f774be3dda168fbfebc08dd7\nparent 56c19608135baeb6fb476cd7443742f0c8eeb3d4\nauthor Dmytro Saus <dlsaus@gmail.com> 1786609773 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786609773 +0300\n\n001 solution and schema (#1)\n\n* docs: specify local environment and schema (001)\n\n* docs: clarify local environment and schema spec (001)\n\n* docs: split feature 001 into solution-and-schema and bootstrap-and-seed\n\nThe /speckit-plan Constitution Check on 001-local-environment-schema failed P3\n(one evening per spec). The original covered four projects, the build and\ndocumentation gate, the schema and migration, the container definition, token\nvalidation, a health endpoint, a Testcontainers harness, a bootstrap script with\nreadiness polling and procedure application, deterministic generation of 400,000\nrows with verification, and token minting. That is not one evening.\n\nGovernance permits Complexity Tracking entries only for SHOULD principles, so a\nMUST failure is reworked rather than waived. Split along the original spec''s own\nuser story boundaries, so no requirement was rewritten to fit:\n\n  001-solution-and-schema  projects, build gate, schema, migration, compose file,\n                           auth boundary, health endpoint, test harness\n  002-bootstrap-and-seed   bootstrap script, seeding, verification, token minting\n\nSequential numbering rather than 001a/001b: create-new-feature.ps1 matches\n^(\\d{3,})- when scanning for the next number, so 001a-* would not match and the\nfollowing feature would collide back at 001. The rollup is now 003.\n\nTwo consequences worth recording. 001 satisfies P18 only partially by design -\nit leaves three manual commands, and the README states that rather than\npromising the two-command quickstart before 002 delivers it. And 001 FR-012\nrequires that WorkDate carry no check constraint, which is a requirement that\nsomething be absent; it has a positive test asserting a three-year-old date is\naccepted, so that adding the constraint later breaks a test instead of silently\nbreaking 002''s seed.\n\nCarries forward the bootstrap contract and the seeding, determinism, readiness,\nprocedure-application and token-minting research from the original planning run\ninto 002, to be validated by its own /speckit-plan rather than re-derived.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: remove career framing from PRD section 1\n\n* docs: remove personal framing from PRD and README\n\n* docs: generate tasks for 001 and remove personal framing\n\n* feat: solution, schema, health endpoint and access boundary (001)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfYBuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvCsQALAuOixhYU6mLuw/p8XGVJuY\nAULwUZrK5jHWVl6FrqEU1criAMjEBClAqGZR0Egif+eP5mZYYKIdSebvtLs2Mrar\nV/HWxbku0eZAmIScVpp1gCdLYrjdKXii74J+E+iTFuxtHJEtzu99qbXgwhNjzXx0\nHftn5cLurN8QvwMjE6+PII0Qx6uHqFGlkku3UDpIBnYIFUkEtQKjkT2051FFlZhh\ngVdbxsoj380I6awdFqtXq6Q0Buai/3FF7WR7HLqlKOLvqvvvyqsaUokioeF+mrRc\ne0mPBJnz1CZZJTbHhsLh8w6I3vaD4Tyor6PwsZKJBIcz8OJSnJJMDdFrrePiigv0\nmACfNRUfVi1pvBAo/Rov3MClrCy1j/N8f6SOtuW8JhUHJpeSQuUpLoYZWmK/H5Rv\n8vrYbBN5OXR4sbVPzZxaI3tbPZsRdhHcQkMJX4YK59WQK9BNUnc5oBtRW0Pj+56U\nAYE0JxG0zNDMojflKHjtO3Fj+jJn9I5yHVDUQiOoNrEJkApzqAdo4XfwoLlVwrNF\nyFWOVIud7BTB6DUWfhSjX+AlQYb3sXXQ7Tb6sO2igcDbkM7FIVQ8cVlmFbdvgyoY\nKZOpbnOacV2hmV5jYcKKL