pos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/8ea9938aa19822328c008ed29acd67d29173c544/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T00:27:25Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T00:32:08Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"message":"fix(test): the rate-limit bursts fire both servers together, and the D-1150 Go pair moves off plugin_hooks'' ports\n\nbursts_are_refused_as_go_refuses_them sent each request to Go and then to this server, so the\nsecond server saw every request one round trip late; under a loaded full run that put one login\non each side of the login limiter''s 200ms refill (Go 400, ours 429 at #12), or stretched the\nburst past it entirely (no refusal at all). Each pair now goes out with tokio::join!, the exact\nlogin refusal count is asserted only when the burst fits one refill (the per-request comparison\nalways runs), the bare route refusal is taken from the 2/1 desktop-token burst, and the ping\nburst that exhausts the 1/s global budget has room for a few seconds of refill.\n\nforwarded_requests_are_limited_once_on_the_clients_key started its two Go servers at +82 and\n+83, which plugin_hooks'' download and upload tranches also use; they move to +48 and +49, and\nsecond_server_ports reserves those instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e7b84c563fbd0369ffa8280c4f22692eae56e2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/trees/1e7b84c563fbd0369ffa8280c4f22692eae56e2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/commits/8ea9938aa19822328c008ed29acd67d29173c544","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","