starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/27203e88e5795dfb21de395fcc6607bc92866c49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:35:14Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:35:14Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"message":"fix(webhooks): the owner''s access check on an incoming-hook move, and the outgoing team checks — D-1220, D-1221 closed\n\nupdateIncomingHook: when the body moves the hook to another channel, the\nold hook''s owner must be able to read it (ValidateIncomingWebhookUserChannelAccess,\nnow split out of validate_incoming_webhook_user), or 403\napi.webhook.incoming.user_membership.app_error with the \"fail - invalid\nwebhook user\" audit row — after the caller''s own checks and before the\nchannel-lock rewrite, as in Go.\n\nupdateOutgoingHook: an empty team_id is filled from the stored hook and any\nother is 400 api.webhook.team_mismatch.app_error, after \"attempt\" and before\nthe permission checks; the app layer used to reset the team silently.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"52265a0b499946f06d64533f2a20f68bc588c4e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/trees/52265a0b499946f06d64533f2a20f68bc588c4e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/commits/27203e88e5795dfb21de395fcc6607bc92866c49","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.