,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/7064964e552a6b56d8d42af9b7f811dccde81223/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:23:26Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:23:26Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"message":"fix(audit): record Go''s decoded r.URL.Path, and let net/http refuse what it cannot parse\n\nAuditRequest''s action was the raw request target; Go''s c.AppContext.Path()\nis r.URL.Path from url.ParseRequestURI, percent-decoded (%2F included, +\nkept). A path parameter is decoded before the id check, so\n/api/v4/users/m%65/patch is served here and must be recorded as\n/api/v4/users/me/patch. A target ParseRequestURI refuses never reaches a Go\nhandler (net/http writes its own 400), so no row is written for it; nor for\na path that decodes to non-UTF-8, which Go''s insert cannot store.\n\nThe same probe showed a route with a non-id parameter answering such a\ntarget (/users/username/ab%zz: our 401, Go''s 400); mux_guard now hands any\nunparseable target to Go on both routers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"faa53b5189be3e704d8db989ae951807f3540fe1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/trees/faa53b5189be3e704d8db989ae951807f3540fe1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/commits/7064964e552a6b56d8d42af9b7f811dccde81223","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh","id":874046,"login":"niklabh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDA0Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commit/7064964e552a6b56d8d42af9b7f811dccde81223","node_id":"C_kwDOT3fvHtoAKDcwNjQ5NjRlNTUyYTZiNTZkOGQ0MmFmOWI3ZjgxMWRjY2RlODEyMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commit/6a083a6a0b3ec3eb594a507cd51fa625ca76f419","sha":"6a083a6a0b3ec3eb594a507cd51fa625ca76f419","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/6a083a6a0b3ec3eb594a507cd51fa625ca76f419"}],"sha":"7064964e552a6b56d8d42af9b7f811dccde81223","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/7064964e552a6b56d8d42af9b7f811dccde81223"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh","id":874046,"login":"niklabh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDA0Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/7f72246cc46e0f845dad1b888bd8b2b61ca4a73d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:21:25Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:21:25Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"message":"fix(api): Go''s MaximumURLLength 414 on every served route — D-1211 closed\n\nweb.Handler.ServeHTTP runs basicSecurityChecks before anything else: a request URI longer than\nServiceSettings.MaximumURLLength is the 414 basic_security_check.url.too_long_error, written\nbefore the security headers and the per-user rate limit, so it carries only Content-Type and\ngzhttp''s Vary. The web client''s page and /manualtest already checked it; the API router and\nthe local socket did not (GET /api/v4/system/ping?x=<3000 bytes> was Go 414, ours 200).\n\nmm_api::serve_http is the preamble route_layer on both routers: gorilla''s charset match (a\nsegment outside it is the api4 catch-all, which checks nothing), the length check, then the\nper-user step moved from ratelimit. MaximumURLLength joins mm_app::config and the config\nfixture projection (config_active.json gains the one key).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd7ba7e4f5e894e8e790500e6eea705e34326186","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/trees/dd7ba7e4f5e894e8e790500e6eea705e34326186"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/commits/7f72246cc46e0f845dad1b888bd8b2b61ca4a73d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","following_