"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:08:04Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"message":"fix(api): the rate-limit parity bursts tolerate a period boundary under load — follows D-1150\n\nA full parity run measured a login''s route Remaining one apart between the two servers: under\nload a burst can straddle any limiter''s period, not only the shared global one''s. Anonymous\nbursts now compare Remaining and Reset within one at every position; statuses, limits and\nRetry-After stay exact, and the per-user bursts stay exact throughout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5dd74dcb74bc5e7032f85785704305f0d731ff95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/trees/5dd74dcb74bc5e7032f85785704305f0d731ff95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/commits/4c4648dac0f369ea31e943486eb24aa1646d5d60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh","id":874046,"login":"niklabh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDA0Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commit/4c4648dac0f369ea31e943486eb24aa1646d5d60","node_id":"C_kwDOT3fvHtoAKDRjNDY0OGRhYzBmMzY5ZWEzMWU5NDM0ODZlYjI0YWExNjQ2ZDVkNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commit/db9c74bf178011e4cf651fca39b71fb99a95f045","sha":"db9c74bf178011e4cf651fca39b71fb99a95f045","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/db9c74bf178011e4cf651fca39b71fb99a95f045"}],"sha":"4c4648dac0f369ea31e943486eb24aa1646d5d60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/4c4648dac0f369ea31e943486eb24aa1646d5d60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh","id":874046,"login":"niklabh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDA0Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/76a0fc6f7a18c62b0df139f0c8c642bfdd8e0532/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T20:48:45Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T20:48:45Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"message":"feat(audit): write Go''s Audits rows on every served LogAudit branch — D-270, D-870 closed\n\nEvery api4 handler that calls c.LogAudit / c.LogAuditWithUserId and whose\nroute this server answers now writes the same Audits rows at the same point\n(on entry, on the refusals Go audits, on success), through a new\nmm_api::audit_log::AuditRequest extractor that reads the request path and\nthe TrustedProxyIPHeader-aware client address. Covered: channels (HTTP and\nlocal), views, commands, webhooks, OAuth apps, outgoing OAuth connections,\nlicences (HTTP and local), marketplace visit, product notices, onboarding,\nroles, teams, brand and profile images, user updates, auth, MFA, passwords,\nlogout, login and desktop-token login (LogAuditWithUserId and its\nsession_user suffix, under the new session for \"success\"), sessions and\ndevice ids, tokens, terms of service, e-mail verification.\n\nD-870: the Go session-cache purge now calls PUT /users/sessions/device\nwith an empty body, authenticated as the probe session, which Go does not\naudit; the probe row is deleted afterwards.\n\nAlso the add paths'' group-constrained branch: FilterNonGroupChannelMembers\nis ported for addChannelMember, localAddChannelMember and addUserToChannel\n(a NonGroupFilterError keeps Go''s two error kinds apart), so a\ngroup-constrained add is served instead of forwarded.\n\nOpens D-1220 and D-1221 (two webhook-update checks found missing while\nreading the handlers).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b38915c7ed0206f6b4afd2b4fc9a866e0dbbc831","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/trees/b38915c7ed0206f6b4afd2b4fc9a866e0dbbc831"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/commits/76a0fc6f7a18c62b0df139f0c8c642bfdd8e0532","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","following_url":"ht