ps://api.github.com/users/niklabh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh","id":874046,"login":"niklabh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDA0Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/8b6ca4f28436d1caf1019791d233b92f7f055d34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T19:52:19Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T19:52:19Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"message":"Merge branch ''wt/debt-body-decode'': absent keys zero-fill under a source guard, and every body decoder takes [] and null as Go does — D-192, D-043, D-941 closed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tMIGRATION.md\n#\tcrates/mm-api/tests/parity.rs\n#\treference/dump/main.go","tree":{"sha":"6559d43dc4eb4a297974006103370c03d16fe045","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/trees/6559d43dc4eb4a297974006103370c03d16fe045"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/commits/8b6ca4f28436d1caf1019791d233b92f7f055d34","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh","id":874046,"login":"niklabh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDA0Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commit/8b6ca4f28436d1caf1019791d233b92f7f055d34","node_id":"C_kwDOT3fvHtoAKDhiNmNhNGYyODQzNmQxY2FmMTAxOTc5MWQyMzNiOTJmN2YwNTVkMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commit/8ec2758111088d289d3bd554eaf0b65ae85e895e","sha":"8ec2758111088d289d3bd554eaf0b65ae85e895e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/8ec2758111088d289d3bd554eaf0b65ae85e895e"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commit/e46bda3f1339ef8f10763435924942138c087844","sha":"e46bda3f1339ef8f10763435924942138c087844","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/e46bda3f1339ef8f10763435924942138c087844"}],"sha":"8b6ca4f28436d1caf1019791d233b92f7f055d34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/8b6ca4f28436d1caf1019791d233b92f7f055d34"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/niklabh","id":874046,"login":"niklabh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDA0Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/commits/e46bda3f1339ef8f10763435924942138c087844/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T19:51:34Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T19:51:34Z","email":"niklabh811@gmail.com","name":"Nikhil Ranjan"},"message":"fix(api): every body decoder refuses an array for a struct and takes null as Go does — D-941 closed\n\nserde''s derive reads a JSON array into a struct positionally, so `[]` was a\nzero-valued body that walked on to a later check and named a field where Go\nnames the body; `null` was an error where Go''s value target keeps its zero\nvalue; trailing bytes were an error where Decoder.Decode never reads them;\na repeated key was `duplicate field` where Go is last-wins.\n\nmm_model::go_decode::Strict is a Deserializer adapter every body decoder in\nmm_model::utils goes through: deserialize_struct''s visitor refuses a\nsequence, every nested value is reached through wrapped Map/Seq/EnumAccess so\nthe rule holds at any depth, and a struct''s members are buffered so a\nrepeated key is last-wins (D-071 narrowed). decode_one_object_from_json is\ngone — the plain decoder now does what it did. Added unmarshal_from_json\n(json.Unmarshal), map_from_json, map_bool_from_json and\nstring_interface_from_json.\n\nAll ~120 body-decode sites in mm-api were audited against their Go handler''s\ndeclaration and moved to the matching form: value targets to\ndecode_one_value_from_json (posts, drafts, reactions, status, teams, webhooks,\nOAuth, dialogs, commands, schemes, uploads, scheme roles, jobs, ...), pointer\ntargets stay Option<T>, the two json.Unmarshal handlers (group syncables,\nscheduled-post update) use unmarshal_from_json. The eleven local MapFromJSON /\nStringInterfaceFromJSON copies now delegate to the shared helpers, which keep\nGo''s partial decode (a mistyped member is \"\", not an empty map); their tests\nasserted the old collapse and now assert Go''s answer.\n\nOracle: reference/dump/behaviour_body_decode.go (48 bodies through Decode into\na value, Decode into a pointer and Unmarshal; MapBoolFromJSON; an int64\ntarget). Full generator run touched only the new fixture.\nparity::malformed_bodies posts [], null and trailing bytes to 24\nroute/body pairs across posts, reactions, status, teams, channels, webhooks,\nbots, preferences, drafts, scheme roles and commands and compares whole error\nbodies with Go.\n\nTests: mm-model 1543, mm-api lib 524 passed; parity 4736 passed, 8 failed —\n4 pass alone (boards, channel_search_all, configlic, licensed_sweep priority),\nmanualtest / marketplace / site_url_test ping fail at base, and\nlicensed_sweep::the_config_and_environment_reads_are_served_licensed fails at\nbase too (the licensed oracle''s stale EmailSettings.FeedbackName).\nMutations (scripts/mutations/body-decode-*.plan): 16 run, 14 caught,\n2 controls survived.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e8d217055d45a7a4eba51f4fc297428006f09094","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/trees/e8d217055d45a7a4eba51f4fc297428006f09094"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niklabh/mattermost-rs/git/commits/e46bda3f1339ef8f10763435924942138c087844","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/874046?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niklabh/events{/privacy}","foll