orkflows (no edge,\nrelease-please, or release run exists for 68ab578), so\nghcr.io/7k-inari/inari-ui-bundle:edge still serves the pre-#85 bundle.\nA manual dispatch trigger provides the repair path without requiring an\nempty commit.\n\nCo-authored-by: kandev-agent <kandev-agent@7kgroup.org>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvtVbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWg8QABppUTAPt8FKPx2B38BRdGhM\nNSRDE2O5gDteuRgNtWmqc6IU+9e85XITtcbj7wwziKv+ERloKUxLx8PT9HRBogrn\nIbnNlxkkkaCvXUph3yMlzaZ/nINWxVqxmBkCO+lMhln58iDOwC+MuFcaBNExYJNO\nyqNpVzCbB29mJLuDHjfj6YTYgJZFGr87tF6z7LhsQJEvpWFxyQs2LuLdGskRKCo+\nZKzge0OVhS9AiBDx3IDOema6C6KOFc0SAWIP7+l1Mh+jV1Xf2Ipfoi8v6Mv0msdL\nGe70MQPKwPoAVS0GTj2UGQujOqiJ59ucTYzUJPTQv+H820JRyOOz8LixCSVIfMNq\noebM/XQ/teYeGBDYqKt0yw2VTR7ci7atommyBN9747z15FtStpcAJAj98fcpN+ES\noxTEym+3WgK3iCyXMlY0UuePZioOUvEI7hwFckQfc/fIIKb6h5M98f3xaUaU6HDa\nEe1AZqMo3howlyMDyxEUnECW5Z/6gMVdZqj7/4UwnnXl8JG7IGyx0MraSXQAaHfs\nsVE83M7xJzoD10STFOJXNCORuTzlriKzGvCjwDk09K7j9MVXoJYXuZM4V+RioiIT\nn9djcto47iznmO7Wjrym3JBbEWQ40EaLlp4ebxBjMs8ojinTYFAaC5T/z372q8sg\nVHxZNWbOIPdF760m0s6A\n=RuBF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T21:49:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commit/41deff8b5415ab8f8c54a696db4775169225e2dc","node_id":"C_kwDOT3j7o9oAKDQxZGVmZjhiNTQxNWFiOGY4YzU0YTY5NmRiNDc3NTE2OTIyNWUyZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commit/68ab57863408ae039b535bc88ccb5d5730555a4e","sha":"68ab57863408ae039b535bc88ccb5d5730555a4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/68ab57863408ae039b535bc88ccb5d5730555a4e"}],"sha":"41deff8b5415ab8f8c54a696db4775169225e2dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/41deff8b5415ab8f8c54a696db4775169225e2dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32569584?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joaodss2","id":32569584,"login":"joaodss2","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTY5NTg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/68ab57863408ae039b535bc88ccb5d5730555a4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T23:55:27Z","email":"32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com","name":"João Santos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T23:55:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(access): role engine UI — role editor, role-entity matrix, permission projection (#85)\n\n* feat(access): role engine UI — role editor, roleId contract, permission projection\n\nADR-0013 (M1W2): org roles are DB entities over the static permission\ncatalog. Syncs the server OpenAPI snapshot (edge) and regenerates types.\n\n- New Roles tab on the access console: RoleEditor with the permission\n  checklist grouped by domain from GET .../permissions/catalog; create\n  custom roles, edit built-in permission bundles (names immutable),\n  delete custom roles; server 409s (built-in guardrail, team-bound\n  delete) surfaced inline. Gated on manageRbac.\n- Contract migration: me/permissions orgRoles -> roles (name sets,\n  isAdmin = set contains admin); PUT rbac/mappings writes\n  {team, roleId}; PUT members/{subject} and team create take roleId;\n  org members consume OrgMemberView (roles set + teams).\n- Members tab: role selects populated from GET /roles; member rows show\n  the roles set with a single-role setter; team create picks a role.\n- msw: seeded built-in roles + static permission catalog, roles CRUD\n  handlers with built-in/team-bound 409s, OrgMemberView fixtures,\n  roleId write handlers, roles projection on /me/permissions.\n\n* feat(access): switch Teams & Roles matrix to role entities\n\nPlan W1 Phase B: the matrix rows are teams and each row''s select lists the\norg''s role entities (built-in + custom from GET /roles); saving writes the\ngeneralized {team, roleId} bulk PUT directly instead of round-tripping\nClusterRole names through the read projection. Current assignments are\nrecovered by stripping the tenant-<slug>- prefix and matching role names.\n\n- New putTeamRoleMappings adapter (direct team→roleId PUT).\n- Per-row select replaces the radio grid; options carry role display\n  names + description tooltips; Manage roles link to the Roles tab.\n- Drops the dead client-side role catalog (roleDisplay).\n\n* fix(access): preserve unknown matrix mappings, confirm role delete, strict DNS-1123 name pattern\n\n* fix(access): resolve roleId on mock ClusterRole synthesis, enforce tenant.admin guardrail in mocks, tighten matrix roles-ready race","tree":{"sha":"7b0238c4edf533b181835f1eb8d5b70ffd9eba80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/trees/7b0238c4edf533b181835f1eb8d5b70ffd9eba80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/commits/68ab57863408ae039b535bc88ccb5d5730555a4e","verification":{"payload":"tree 7b0238c4edf533b181835f1eb8d5b70ffd9eba80\nparent b87554a2d344ecd790315ae4d60c938c8c11c727\nauthor João Santos <32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com> 1790812527 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790812527 +0100\n\nfeat(access): role engine UI — role editor, role-entity matrix, permission projection (#85)\n\n* feat(access): role engine UI — role editor, roleId contract, permission projection\n\nADR-0013 (M1W2): org roles are DB entities over the static permission\ncatalog. Syncs the server OpenAPI snapshot (edge) and regenerates types.\n\n- New Roles tab on the access console: RoleEditor with the permission\n  checklist grouped by domain from GET .../permissions/catalog; create\n  custom roles, edit built-in permission bundles (names immutable),\n  delete custom roles; server 409s (built-in guardrail, team-bound\n  delete) surfaced inline. Gated on manageRbac.\n- Contract migration: me/permissions orgRoles -> roles (name sets,\n  isAdmin = set contains admin); PUT rbac/mappings writes\n  {team, roleId}; PUT members/{subject} and team create take roleId;\n  org members consume OrgMemberView (roles set + teams).\n- Members tab: role selects populated from GET /roles; member rows show\n  the roles set with a single-role setter; team create picks a role.\n- msw: seeded built-in roles + static permission catalog, roles CRUD\n  handlers with built-in/team-bound 409s, OrgMemberView fixtures,\n  roleId write handlers, roles projection on /me/permissions.\n\n* feat(access): switch Teams & Roles matrix to role entities\n\nPlan W1 Phase B: the matrix rows are teams and each row''s select lists the\norg''s role entities (built-in + custom from GET /roles); saving writes the\ngeneralized {team, roleId} bulk PUT directly instead of round-tripping\nClusterRole names through the read projection. Current assignments are\nrecovered by stripping the tenant-<slug>- prefix and matching role names.\n\n- New putTeamRoleMappings adapter (direct team→roleId PUT).\n- Per-row select replaces the radio grid; options carry role display\n  names + description tooltips; Manage roles link to the Roles tab.\n- Drops the dead client-side role catalog (roleDisplay).\n\n* fix(access): preserve unknown matrix mappings, confirm role delete, strict DNS-1123 name pattern\n\n* fix(access): resolve roleId on mock ClusterRole synthesis, enforce tenant.admin guardrail in mocks, tighten matrix roles-ready race","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvaFvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAp0QAAtd/pYQ1mfwZiCdvuivxAPL\nXpujR0PSm5EYjq3t2sIk7GS8wJY/YTonk47Ot20m1sDZfMyeg8fgSf9oMUbQ52Kz\nxIqfyIIQddfO12NHOgcmjL7vUwhKRGkDK+Hrfh2+NfiPRPXhE8sgSJJ3lLyGrF5/\nJTiKU8eXsEPeq1Axzcifzr16QuMp/U/nMUImyjFuYkStuQgPcgNvXW+BsJjy75za\nWgg3MioIn+XVyTY50fAwVSe697jM6h0RlWaipnYqpDCMMVER5WCu89YKg+0IV9PA\npZenDFja8HjRnxElmvpXpVJl8tXo6WOmYKRURP/BBzbS26UH+IqpAMhaMf86YPR0\n4ebcbjvQpCxnepheDQF8HvcUQi58wz3ODWktDcG+GlaKCRGFSEkU7TLEpn+6SjSK\n5K8/lwc0MrDYusb5F43E/puMU/VKx5rr0FekIH+54Gec0YaPHQm9indZQq+rjQ/6\nJ6OSVR9AKrcufUqna+27eFWNFy3Lu/YzKum5lHG7BmomM/YzGC4DUgmjTmmgcIMB\nXem7ZPUCeKCzPVmOirpxOCWOzsFXhQAMpCEIuIjBm8pXNw92EE+ouVmNZnOTF9Ui\nCecfUnOCbS9d+PYoUOqGWNW9s0QxBNFRm3P3wjQnEa7rqaqrCbyj/jL3Wk9rUteP\nQhvfKV+W6crxbK8rbSHX\n=2WyB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T23:55:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commit/68ab57863408ae039b535bc88ccb5d5730555a4e","node_id":"C_kwDOT3j7o9oAKDY4YWI1Nzg2MzQwOGFlMDM5YjUzNWJjODhjY2I1ZDU3MzA1NTVhNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commit/b87554a2d344ecd790315ae4d60c938c8c11c727","sha":"b87554a2d344ecd790315ae4d60c938c8c11c727","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/b87554a2d344ecd790315ae4d60c938c8c11c727"}],"sha":"68ab57863408ae039b535bc88ccb5d5730555a4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/68ab57863408ae039b535bc88ccb5d5730555a4e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32569584?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joaodss2","id":32569584,"login":"joaodss2","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTY5NTg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/b87554a2d344ecd790315ae4d60c938c8c11c727/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:58:46Z","email":"32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com","name":"João Santos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:58:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(access): RBAC Phase A access console — unified members/teams/roles UI (#84)\n\n* feat(access): RBAC Phase A access console — unified members/teams/roles UI\n\nConsolidate the two RBAC matrix screens and org member/team settings into\na single Access console at /:tenant/access (Members / Teams & Roles /\nIdentity tabs) plus a platform-level console at /platform/access.\n\n- RoleMatrix: teams as rows with friendly display names, one role per\n  team as radios (server rejects duplicates with 400), draft state +\n  single bulk PUT .../rbac/mappings; friendly role catalog with\n  description tooltips replaces raw group paths/ClusterRole names.\n- MembersTab: email-invite flow elevated from settings/org/members;\n  team membership absorbed from settings/org/teams with a debounced\n  user picker over the new GET .../members?q= search instead of raw\n  Keycloak UUID input.\n- PlatformAccessPage: list/grant/revoke platform admins via the new\n  GET/PUT/DELETE /api/v1/platform/admins[/{subject}] endpoints.\n- CapabilityGate/useOrgCapabilities: per-capability flags\n  (canManageMembers/canManageTeams/canManageRbac) from the tenants\n  projection on GET /me/permissions, with admin-derived fallback and\n  disabled-with-tooltip mode instead of unmounting.\n- Routes: /:tenant/rbac, settings/identity/rbac, settings/org/members\n  and settings/org/teams redirect into the Access console; nav and\n  settings nav updated; old pages deleted.\n- msw: platform admins handlers, ?q= member search, tenants capability\n  projection, duplicate-team 400 on PUT rbac/mappings.\n\nNew endpoints are mocked per the M1 plan contract; codegen tail\n(npm run sync:api) follows once the Phase A server task merges.\n\n* fix(access): scope RoleMatrix draft to its tenant\n\nA tenant switch re-renders the access console without unmounting it, so a\ndirty draft from the previous tenant leaked into the new one: every team\nshowed \"No role\", Save stayed enabled, and saving sent an empty mapping\nset that wiped the new tenant''s role assignments. Tag the draft with its\ntenant and treat a foreign draft as pristine; add a regression test.\n\n* chore(api): sync OpenAPI snapshot to inari-server edge (M1.W1 Phase A contract)\n\nThe Phase A server task merged: pull the published spec artifact and\nreplace the hand-written TODO(contract-sync) shapes with generated types.\nNotable drift resolved: PlatformAdminView is {userId, email, displayName}\n(all required), not the mocked {subject, email?, displayName?}; TenantCapabilities\nnow types the tenants projection on GET /me/permissions; PutMemberInputBody /\nCreateTeamInputBody / UpdateTenantInputBody replace local interfaces. Mock\nfixtures and the platform access page updated to the real wire shape.","tree":{"sha":"85663d9382e5a3d6c2f12efe63b3dce81eb72e98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/trees/85663d9382e5a3d6c2f12efe63b3dce81eb72e98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/commits/b87554a2d344ecd790315ae4d60c938c8c11c727","verification":{"payload":"tree 85663d9382e5a3d6c2f12efe63b3dce81eb72e98\nparent b6324687282c1fcda745c0609ebf1a3f12e916ce\nauthor João Santos <32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com> 1790769526 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790769526 +0100\n\nfeat(access): RBAC Phase A access console — unified members/teams/roles UI (#84)\n\n* feat(access): RBAC Phase A access console — unified members/teams/roles UI\n\nConsolidate the two RBAC matrix screens and org member/team settings into\na single Access console at /:tenant/access (Members / Teams & Roles /\nIdentity tabs) plus a platform-level console at /platform/access.\n\n- RoleMatrix: teams as rows with friendly display names, one role per\n  team as radios (server rejects duplicates with 400), draft state +\n  single bulk PUT .../rbac/mappings; friendly role catalog with\n  description tooltips replaces raw group paths/ClusterRole names.\n- MembersTab: email-invite flow elevated from settings/org/members;\n  team membership absorbed from settings/org/teams with a debounced\n  user picker over the new GET .../members?q= search instead of raw\n  Keycloak UUID input.\n- PlatformAccessPage: list/grant/revoke platform admins via the new\n  GET/PUT/DELETE /api/v1/platform/admins[/{subject}] endpoints.\n- CapabilityGate/useOrgCapabilities: per-capability flags\n  (canManageMembers/canManageTeams/canManageRbac) from the tenants\n  projection on GET /me/permissions, with admin-derived fallback and\n  disabled-with-tooltip mode instead of unmounting.\n- Routes: /:tenant/rbac, settings/identity/rbac, settings/org/members\n  and settings/org/teams redirect into the Access console; nav and\n  settings nav updated; old pages deleted.\n- msw: platform admins handlers, ?q= member search, tenants capability\n  projection, duplicate-team 400 on PUT rbac/mappings.\n\nNew endpoints are mocked per the M1 plan contract; codegen tail\n(npm run sync:api) follows once the Phase A server task merges.\n\n* fix(access): scope RoleMatrix draft to its tenant\n\nA tenant switch re-renders the access console without unmounting it, so a\ndirty draft from the previous tenant leaked into the new one: every team\nshowed \"No role\", Save stayed enabled, and saving sent an empty mapping\nset that wiped the new tenant''s role assignments. Tag the draft with its\ntenant and treat a foreign draft as pristine; add a regression test.\n\n* chore(api): sync OpenAPI snapshot to inari-server edge (M1.W1 Phase A contract)\n\nThe Phase A server task merged: pull the published spec artifact and\nreplace the hand-written TODO(contract-sync) shapes with generated types.\nNotable drift resolved: PlatformAdminView is {userId, email, displayName}\n(all required), not the mocked {subject, email?, displayName?}; TenantCapabilities\nnow types the tenants projection on GET /me/permissions; PutMemberInputBody /\nCreateTeamInputBody / UpdateTenantInputBody replace local interfaces. Mock\nfixtures and the platform access page updated to the real wire shape.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPl2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoaUQAJr90/bSbf0zL7C8txPZP8lB\neeb2bpjUyuDoBnwIw8MWZyOvDZWYo54iCsv/TJF6LlYXdA0EHbrFvnBVMKoItNOx\nEuuHNio+rkpC7++s15jJ518PtH7EzfFV/CVbNzXJeELVpGYzmztswZah0ME4ZFp+\nHt7Pl0/+ntngvagkdM+SFxu2s+WfR3SyigOGGAp5a0goOsPqNh+4wEAgjV1a1Zac\n164HnrH0QhnnF90w2wfem9QHr7nXJz11YWxbaCjmME6fTCduIjvU+BxC7a2Mtv+t\nZPaMfZ1r71q3Nl/6mWSDYsphgBSREe3xn+ZoxFKCfMokI2yMb4Z0lY9CuRaq6GHf\nXFZzBGYrtsLJniNcFmf/ZpmX2HIWIhJ2vFhMpmFV2qdQSoXkIh1VPvtaO1rjEIWX\nnqKgSAwKdXt8vmXRY9XSUCI45YMClpVcuTobcOnkRvxE+2NaBBA+4DYbNZNGXH78\n+aobWeqHI15AAyc63W4gC+S3vTlWezokE0g4mC3Ws9TXcPbQsw4kWxUw0wGGEj5e\nxOKmYrQKpSauY/mF8rBb/s2E818myWFSnM2rCWJWOplF4UA9xZs9cKgc2S0qxmsL\nZcY8TqSMQUIbujBNfhDIQc2EvghiiVPnRBuQKVDfwQOUie1Ju3P5VSSjdL+CQYaD\nAXPIyiB7y9hESToBJ8iS\n=e8vf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:58:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://