m/users/joaodss2/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/4cd47a844cce2613d4e69538da47fb21922579b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T10:10:39Z","email":"32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com","name":"João Santos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T10:10:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(api): migrate templates client to canonical scaffold-runs endpoints (#63)\n\n* feat(api): migrate templates client to canonical scaffold-runs endpoints\n\nReplace the hand-written /scaffolds UI-compat client with the canonical\ngenerated API: POST /templates/{name}/runs for run creation and\nGET/POST /scaffold-runs/{runId}[/cancel][/retry] for polling and run\ncontrol. All wire types come from @/api/__generated__/schema; a\nScaffoldRunViewModel adapter maps RunView (per-step states, untyped\noutputs map) to the wizard''s shape.\n\nThe wizard now renders per-step progress and surfaces the newly\navailable cancel and retry actions. MSW fixtures speak the RunView wire\nshape with poll-based step advancement, a simulated-failure control for\nthe retry path, and cancel/retry handlers.\n\nNo UI code path calls /tenants/{org}/scaffolds* anymore, so the\nserver-side compat adapter (internal/scaffold/http.go runView) is\ndeprecatable in a later server release.\n\n* review: link wizard by template name to match canonical /templates/{name} endpoints\n\n* test(templates): cover run-creation 422, cancel failure, and null template list","tree":{"sha":"451ccba080a57f2ae7606a80d9b9b44ca8f1f642","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/trees/451ccba080a57f2ae7606a80d9b9b44ca8f1f642"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/commits/4cd47a844cce2613d4e69538da47fb21922579b3","verification":{"payload":"tree 451ccba080a57f2ae7606a80d9b9b44ca8f1f642\nparent c5f2cae538a032ea4a2211dc9e746095b24e5ff6\nauthor João Santos <32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com> 1790331039 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790331039 +0100\n\nfeat(api): migrate templates client to canonical scaffold-runs endpoints (#63)\n\n* feat(api): migrate templates client to canonical scaffold-runs endpoints\n\nReplace the hand-written /scaffolds UI-compat client with the canonical\ngenerated API: POST /templates/{name}/runs for run creation and\nGET/POST /scaffold-runs/{runId}[/cancel][/retry] for polling and run\ncontrol. All wire types come from @/api/__generated__/schema; a\nScaffoldRunViewModel adapter maps RunView (per-step states, untyped\noutputs map) to the wizard''s shape.\n\nThe wizard now renders per-step progress and surfaces the newly\navailable cancel and retry actions. MSW fixtures speak the RunView wire\nshape with poll-based step advancement, a simulated-failure control for\nthe retry path, and cancel/retry handlers.\n\nNo UI code path calls /tenants/{org}/scaffolds* anymore, so the\nserver-side compat adapter (internal/scaffold/http.go runView) is\ndeprecatable in a later server release.\n\n* review: link wizard by template name to match canonical /templates/{name} endpoints\n\n* test(templates): cover run-creation 422, cancel failure, and null template list","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtkifCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4tUQAKpm0/6gxqvsyL0G2XnPmcjN\n2IrW4+5KSNZc+aAlupRyM7cL9UHAQNW4CeX4aDeJabEzKPTAXaC0JPR/anuJL4Zd\nYYkf6PgBPS8rgMF03W4SRa5b1nEao9gWsOZ1bZpaIEVX2TLoKXn2GQqrUdSGOP4z\nwUwfszJw4yYfPvTR8vALTb8LQGb4rdBUhYbT6Og5qGwQS5Hlc38JtHdc2hyFYJPD\nuwta4Q53pP/ETFLrTHqlEhOZV8Pd9pJrabhR6zkPdHjNV2BoEZv9xXsYwTd9QEii\