"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTY5NTg0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/dfb8a5dcea2af3779777208cdf374fa00b48a709/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T13:18:52Z","email":"32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com","name":"João Santos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T13:18:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(extensions): load server-served UI remotes; tenant notifications settings page (#54)\n\n* feat(settings): tenant notifications settings page\n\nAdd a Notifications section under tenant settings for managing the\ninari-server notification-endpoints API (slack | webhook): endpoints\ntable with kind badge, client-side masked URL, event filter chips and\nenabled toggle; inline create/edit form with per-kind help text\n(Slack incoming webhook, JSON envelope + HMAC-SHA256 signature),\ngrouped event multi-select aligned with the server fan-out set, and\nhttp(s) URL validation; per-endpoint send-test with inline delivery\nresult, edit (PUT, kind immutable, blank secret preserved), and delete\nwith confirm. Viewer-role users get a read-only view.\n\nDelivery history is not exposed by the API yet; the page notes this\nand shows the test-send result instead (follow-up server task).\n\nClient: hand-written src/api/notifications.ts on apiFetch importing\ngenerated contract types. MSW mocks + vitest coverage mirror the\nexisting settings pages (list, create, validation, edit, toggle,\ntest-send feedback, delete confirm, viewer read-only).\n\n* review: mask endpoint URL in hover title, stabilize vitest env and timeout\n\n* test(settings): cover notification row-action errors and secret-on-create\n\n* fix(extensions): map registry state to the healthy badge\n\nThe extensions page read a nonexistent ''healthy'' field, so every backend\nextension showed ''unhealthy''. The API exposes ''state'' (pending|ready|\ndegraded|stopped); project it: ready -> healthy.\n\n* fix(extensions): absolutize server-served remoteEntryUrl; align backend mocks with registry contract\n\nThe shell now resolves the registry''s server-relative remoteEntryUrl\nagainst the API origin before registerRemotes so Module Federation chunk\npublicPath resolution works from any route. Backend-extension MSW\nfixtures return the raw registry record (state, not healthy) matching\nthe real server surface, fixing the extensions-page healthy badge test.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: kandev-agent <kandev@7kgroup.local>","tree":{"sha":"20cdacd28c5b6f684d1049eaad3bba9adba9a0d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/trees/20cdacd28c5b6f684d1049eaad3bba9adba9a0d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/commits/dfb8a5dcea2af3779777208cdf374fa00b48a709","verification":{"payload":"tree 20cdacd28c5b6f684d1049eaad3bba9adba9a0d5\nparent 029c902060fdbc2449d28a59d1ffbf752e4a2d94\nauthor João Santos <32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com> 1790083132 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790083132 +0100\n\nfix(extensions): load server-served UI remotes; tenant notifications settings page (#54)\n\n* feat(settings): tenant notifications settings page\n\nAdd a Notifications section under tenant settings for managing the\ninari-server notification-endpoints API (slack | webhook): endpoints\ntable with kind badge, client-side masked URL, event filter chips and\nenabled toggle; inline create/edit form with per-kind help text\n(Slack incoming webhook, JSON envelope + HMAC-SHA256 signature),\ngrouped event multi-select aligned with the server fan-out set, and\nhttp(s) URL validation; per-endpoint send-test with inline delivery\nresult, edit (PUT, kind immutable, blank secret preserved), and delete\nwith confirm. Viewer-role users get a read-only view.\n\nDelivery history is not exposed by the API yet; the page notes this\nand shows the test-send result instead (follow-up server task).\n\nClient: hand-written src/api/notifications.ts on apiFetch importing\ngenerated contract types. MSW mocks + vitest coverage mirror the\nexisting settings pages (list, create, validation, edit, toggle,\ntest-send feedback, delete confirm, viewer read-only).\n\n* review: mask endpoint URL in hover title, stabilize vitest env and timeout\n\n* test(settings): cover notification row-action errors and secret-on-create\n\n* fix(extensions): map registry state to the healthy badge\n\nThe extensions page read a nonexistent ''healthy'' field, so every backend\nextension showed ''unhealthy''. The API exposes ''state'' (pending|ready|\ndegraded|stopped); project it: ready -> healthy.\n\n* fix(extensions): absolutize server-served remoteEntryUrl; align backend mocks with registry contract\n\nThe shell now resolves the registry''s server-relative remoteEntryUrl\nagainst the API origin before registerRemotes so Module Federation chunk\npublicPath resolution works from any route. Backend-extension MSW\nfixtures return the raw registry record (state, not healthy) matching\nthe real server surface, fixing the extensions-page healthy badge test.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: kandev-agent <kandev@7kgroup.local>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsoA8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2i0QAFaSDNtcjPqelnhrGSIkeWkV\n5Ex00kEBX9olB2bV8AqR3ri7nTBWkKQwzDjPUxKe8fei3ABb48PXXH7JgpEwl/4X\nqP+yKrSLU3jkY5XP1mzfBLkS9BtISxRWacBkwqXfTUj+lJK7uvnctPeqBpei5Gxz\nMVB0357QeKuQ8EwBpxn1AgIIMFJ0rEKpJuQjxKJUh5m1HsycywdbhuN3lnohiRJz\n+i7FNP7MzC9DDDzUFbfvBXdJHTE52sCJpxfBgOSwxSg7jwb2KBTBuyc+lu2trT7O\np1BIkGrCTckahfIM/W