ss2/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/80621ebbf0a36def2d670ab722d8a2f086f95bb1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T10:43:27Z","email":"32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com","name":"João Santos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T10:43:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: server-driven org capabilities, catalog latest-version selection (#51)\n\n* feat(settings): tenant notifications settings page\n\nAdd a Notifications section under tenant settings for managing the\ninari-server notification-endpoints API (slack | webhook): endpoints\ntable with kind badge, client-side masked URL, event filter chips and\nenabled toggle; inline create/edit form with per-kind help text\n(Slack incoming webhook, JSON envelope + HMAC-SHA256 signature),\ngrouped event multi-select aligned with the server fan-out set, and\nhttp(s) URL validation; per-endpoint send-test with inline delivery\nresult, edit (PUT, kind immutable, blank secret preserved), and delete\nwith confirm. Viewer-role users get a read-only view.\n\nDelivery history is not exposed by the API yet; the page notes this\nand shows the test-send result instead (follow-up server task).\n\nClient: hand-written src/api/notifications.ts on apiFetch importing\ngenerated contract types. MSW mocks + vitest coverage mirror the\nexisting settings pages (list, create, validation, edit, toggle,\ntest-send feedback, delete confirm, viewer read-only).\n\n* review: mask endpoint URL in hover title, stabilize vitest env and timeout\n\n* test(settings): cover notification row-action errors and secret-on-create\n\n* fix: server-driven org capabilities, catalog latest-version selection\n\n- capability-gate: derive org admin from /me/permissions orgRoles (FGA,\n  authoritative) with the token claim as legacy fallback only; the\n  token-only derivation degraded every user to read-only viewer\n- api/me: parse orgRoles into MyPermissions\n- api/catalog: server returns versions ascending, so versions[0] was the\n  OLDEST; select pinned → stable-channel → last for schema/uiHints preview\n\nLive-validated in the 5b9304e9 e2e run (test-5b9304e9-e7f44e8-v2).","tree":{"sha":"007a7b839c6df968f6ffa014596f91373863d851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/trees/007a7b839c6df968f6ffa014596f91373863d851"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/commits/80621ebbf0a36def2d670ab722d8a2f086f95bb1","verification":{"payload":"tree 007a7b839c6df968f6ffa014596f91373863d851\nparent 409f19d7f369bbf576ac3c9f4d7b0114621c439d\nauthor João Santos <32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com> 1789728207 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789728207 +0100\n\nfix: server-driven org capabilities, catalog latest-version selection (#51)\n\n* feat(settings): tenant notifications settings page\n\nAdd a Notifications section under tenant settings for managing the\ninari-server notification-endpoints API (slack | webhook): endpoints\ntable with kind badge, client-side masked URL, event filter chips and\nenabled toggle; inline create/edit form with per-kind help text\n(Slack incoming webhook, JSON envelope + HMAC-SHA256 signature),\ngrouped event multi-select aligned with the server fan-out set, and\nhttp(s) URL validation; per-endpoint send-test with inline delivery\nresult, edit (PUT, kind immutable, blank secret preserved), and delete\nwith confirm. Viewer-role users get a read-only view.\n\nDelivery history is not exposed by the API yet; the page notes this\nand shows the test-send result instead (follow-up server task).\n\nClient: hand-written src/api/notifications.ts on apiFetch importing\ngenerated contract types. MSW mocks + vitest coverage mirror the\nexisting settings pages (list, create, validation, edit, toggle,\ntest-send feedback, delete confirm, viewer read-only).\n\n* review: mask endpoint URL in hover title, stabilize vitest env and timeout\n\n* test(settings): cover notification row-action errors and secret-on-create\n\n* fix: server-driven org capabilities, catalog latest-version selection\n\n- capability-gate: derive org admin from /me/permissions orgRoles (FGA,\n  authoritative) with the token claim as legacy fallback only; the\n  token-only derivation degraded every user to read-only viewer\n- api/me: parse orgRoles into MyPermissions\n- api/catalog: server returns versions ascending, so versions[0] was the\n  OLDEST; select pinned → stable-channel → last for schema/uiHints preview\n\nLive-validated in the 5b9304e9 e2e run (test-5b9304e9-e7f44e8-v2).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrRXPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbDYQAEop1lKL9EYxQVvcLk0Eu8uT\n3xoNpeaXepQjOROJIT/2fhg/HKTXwUbShvA2s9j5pyJFi2JjtAnsj5K7+3CuzKEd\ngUxMFfAhCnx79g23SacSVPO1hb+Uo9Irv59GSeuDMlQ+zIS5QZp3w5MpndCB4Nc/\n7gk5VOadiiiqdQCGUYUTI10wuGj1s65nrWzZ9IEA24vIZDxEREZ3i1mqClRTOLYY\n7P0jtWfFmC9zZIhCAVtZu45jSNjN8L6AuameeY99eXNRVkiHkStE1GBx3RLj9bD/\nVIwixHkL5cGwPgCNXY/HsHo9hv4gmbv6WRqK30vW3LmgOiiHStEtSFX7+9jHPzFJ\nT3qyyNR9/zoRkog//IufTif+Eo7sWnP2IdnA8f69JQs2u2i5GFJOJuRFjoQ7aCMh\ntsJrV9gw/QhPbEnPgcbCU935ejH79wyLozw2591hj9qGiJtXMnkLb+Bbtl9GIG6K\nWFPfGUvC0NNtVa5J2T+Pw207Iq9yTK93/Dq8HVj3M0+1+eol8oAjnLnr494YX+jf\nKribtU4DdVb2dM4DHu7DEQy3RtZgvM9wWxGqspl6vT+dFfuTi35e4yJ6KbImf3tU\nOAenMECxwgmG+v58uYsyLxWHJU05Sw4+zI/xhKiAXUIGzZaJODoUs7xEaS1Hcdwx\n491xM+ULMjFFtoQpKVoM\n=dCb6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T10:43:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://ap