dss2/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/commits/5c315fc436e4a252a2fe7aeac7d44f4da42a6214/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:26:49Z","email":"32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com","name":"João Santos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:26:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): request organization:* scope on login (#49)\n\n* fix(auth): request organization:* scope on login\n\nThe plain ''organization'' scope stopped yielding the organization claim on\nthe live Keycloak 26.6.0 realm (verified: org memberships and the scope\nmapper are intact; ''organization:<alias>'' and ''organization:*'' resolve\ncorrectly, plain ''organization'' emits nothing). Without the claim every\norg-scoped API call 403s after login. The wildcard scope explicitly\nrequests all memberships and is robust to the plain-scope behavior.\nOrg switching via organization:<alias> is unchanged.\n\n* test(overview): deflake all-403 activity-section assertion\n\nThe ''hides the section entirely when every org returns 403'' test asserted\nabsence with a bare queryByTestId after a sibling settled; on CI runners\nthe activity fan-out can still be showing its skeleton at that point, so\nthe card was found and the test failed (twice in CI, never locally).\nWait for the card to disappear with waitFor instead.","tree":{"sha":"60c1f0506ffb92c3729a24298e6ddb85299d678f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/trees/60c1f0506ffb92c3729a24298e6ddb85299d678f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ui/git/commits/5c315fc436e4a252a2fe7aeac7d44f4da42a6214","verification":{"payload":"tree 60c1f0506ffb92c3729a24298e6ddb85299d678f\nparent 4a8ec8c3573c74d92e4dc08d462537a8faa78821\nauthor João Santos <32569584+joaodss2@users.noreply.github.com> 1789252009 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789252009 +0100\n\nfix(auth): request organization:* scope on login (#49)\n\n* fix(auth): request organization:* scope on login\n\nThe plain ''organization'' scope stopped yielding the organization claim on\nthe live Keycloak 26.6.0 realm (verified: org memberships and the scope\nmapper are intact; ''organization:<alias>'' and ''organization:*'' resolve\ncorrectly, plain ''organization'' emits nothing). Without the claim every\norg-scoped API call 403s after login. The wildcard scope explicitly\nrequests all memberships and is robust to the plain-scope behavior.\nOrg switching via organization:<alias> is unchanged.\n\n* test(overview): deflake all-403 activity-section assertion\n\nThe ''hides the section entirely when every org returns 403'' test asserted\nabsence with a bare queryByTestId after a sibling settled; on CI runners\nthe activity fan-out can still be showing its skeleton at that point, so\nthe card was found and the test failed (twice in CI, never locally).\nWait for the card to disappear with waitFor instead.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpdGpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcJ4QAHCcih1VSoqroPOasXbWbEqk\nlD1dhWWAV8+P0zRxUTkipr+kG5MjqaRrmeyEFnhJ/F0aVZ6RMa2geG0GkZP0xoKH\naAR+TRpHU4Gcoei0cwV3Jb0uy13Dy/qZwEK6CyF7vEI5DF4EdRSZWMwwG31bIoDf\nCON3l22DQihm0zleYOZaT1NZN0BaEbTcvpgFt35/C4w1Utg5CgsExoPSe4CAW64x\n+8w3zGKgIKU7zdYScMQow68eJ/FxFrcG8a0JWtpj9VKa5JgbQRgklVyrEdktY6hX\nxW6xhEZLX9J+HOH7LEvDcIu9mg7EvTqLSHBOq6Yfvokak0rmKNI2xyzIMbMNEa+g\nMlJTggpL/6AMA9dqRqA7hII6uDujB3gRNED5uFW/UciqIM+hZ3VcxWL+Up+RYaz2\nIM5RQj1HYhQrFsvBAM5oB+5yuDVrapM/fhVW3SREhpOP5joUaMr/xCFDo3fVlD7/\n7DasCKKxZSZkqCvudYM3gA5mmpmXYr0LLDsMS7NiLIFYzHnDIObIYuR8EowwnUb2\