owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ext-argocd/commits/b08635560dcb4239ec3790a7837929f9dd44c319/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:20:08Z","email":"joaodss@live.com.pt","name":"joaodss2"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:20:08Z","email":"joaodss@live.com.pt","name":"joaodss2"},"message":"fix(ci): drop root component so standalone root releases are detected\n\nrelease-please treats a merged Release PR whose body lists a single\ncomponent-less entry (a backend-only release, e.g. PR #15 for v0.3.1)\nas a ''standalone'' release PR and requires the branch-name component to\nmatch the configured component. The root package configured\ncomponent=inari-ext-argocd while the combined release branch\n(release-please--branches--main) carries no component, so rp skipped\nthe release entirely: no tag, no GitHub Release, publish jobs never\nfired (run 36152868466).\n\nWithout an explicit component the root strategy normalizes both sides\nto '''', so standalone root releases match again. Multi-component\nreleases (PR #11) already worked via the body-parsed path and are\nunaffected; tags stay ''v*'' (include-component-in-tag: false).","tree":{"sha":"2dbfaf5d706fdc53a34468e48aa0106e993a75ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ext-argocd/git/trees/2dbfaf5d706fdc53a34468e48aa0106e993a75ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/7K-Inari/inari-ext-argocd/git/commits/b08635560dcb4239ec3790a7837929f9dd44c319","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32569584?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaodss2/followers","following_url":